{
  "title": "2 : Al-Baqarah البقرة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "This Surah has 286 verses and is a ‘Madani’ Surah i.e. it was revealed in Madinah. It is also the longest Surah in the Holy Qur’an.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that whoever recites the first four verses of Surah al-Baqarah, accompanied by the ‘ayatul kursi’ together with the last three verses of this Surah - and makes a habit of reciting these verses daily – his life, property and family will be protected and no evil shall come upon them. Shaitan will not come close to him and he will not be from those who forget Allah (s.w.t.).\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓمّٓۚ‏(1)\nALIF-LAAAM-MEEEM.\nAlif, Lam, Mim\nذٰ لِكَ الْڪِتٰبُ لَا رَيْبَۛۚۖ فِيْهِۛۚ هُدًى لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(2)\nZAALEKAL KETAABO LAA RAYBA, FEEHE, HODAL LIL-MUTTAQEENAL.\nThis is the Book, there is no doubt in it, (being the Word of God) (it is) a guidance for the pious (ones)\nالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْغَيْبِ وَ يُقِيْمُوْنَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَۙ‏(3)\nLAZEENA YOAMENOONA BIL-GHAYBE WA YOQEEMOONAS SALAATA WA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOONA.\nWho believe in the unseen, and establish the prayers and of what We have provided them with, they give (in the way of their Lord)\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِمَۤا اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ وَمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَۚ وَبِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ يُوْقِنُوْنَؕ‏(4)\nWAL LAZEENA YOAMENOONA BEMAA UNZELA ELAYKA WA MAA UNZELA MIN QABLEK, WA BIL-AAKHERATE HUM YOOQENOON.\nAnd who believe in that which hath been sent down unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) and that which hath been sent down (unto the other apostles) before thee, and of the hereafter, they are sure\nاُولٰٓئِكَ عَلٰى هُدًى مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(5)\nOOLAAA-EKA A’LAA HODAM MIR RABBEHIM, WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nThese are the ones on the guidance from their Lord, and these are the ones who shall be the successful ones\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْهِمْ ءَاَنْذَرْتَهُمْ اَمْ لَمْ تُنْذِرْهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(6)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO SAWAAA-UN A’LAYHIM A-ANZARTAHUM AM LAM TUNZIRHUM LAA YOAMENOON.\nVerily (as for) those who disbelieve, alike is it for them, thou warneth them or warneth them not; (for) they will not believe\nخَتَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوْبِهِمْ وَعَلٰى سَمْعِهِمْؕ وَعَلٰىٓ اَبْصَارِهِمْ غِشَاوَةٌ  وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(7)\nKHATAMAL LAAHO A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM WA A’LAA SAM-E’HIM, WA A’LAA ABSAAREHIM GHESHAAWATUNW, WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nGod hath sealed up their hearts and their hearing; and upon their sight is a covering; and for them is a great chastisement\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَّقُوْلُ اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ وَبِالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَمَا هُمْ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَۘ‏(8)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN-Y YAQOOLO AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WA BIL-YAWMIL AAKHERE WA MAA HUM BE-MOAMENEEN.\nAnd of the people (are some) who say, “we believe in God and in the Last Day (of Judgment)”, (while in fact) they are not believers (at all)\nيُخٰدِعُوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ۚ وَمَا يَخْدَعُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَؕ‏(9)\nYOKHAADE-O’ONAL LAAHA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO, WA MAA YAKHDAO’ONA ILLAA ANFOSAHUM WA MAA YASH-O’OROON.\nThey (intend to) ‘deceive God and those who believe, while they deceive not but themselves, but they perceive (it) not\nفِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌۙ فَزَادَهُمُ اللّٰهُ مَرَضًا ۚ وَّلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌۙۢبِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْذِبُوْنَ‏(10)\nFEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN, FA-ZAADAHOMUL LAAHO MARAZAA, WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEMUM, BEMAA KAANAOO YAKZEBOON.\nIn their heart is a disease, and God increaseth their disease, for them is a painful chastisement, because of the lie they were saying\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ لَا تُفْسِدُوْا فِىْ الْاَرْضِۙ قَالُوْاۤ اِنَّمَا نَحْنُ مُصْلِحُوْنَ‏(11)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM LAA TUFSEDOO FIL ARZE, QAALOO INNAMAA NAHNO MUSLEHOON.\nAnd when it is said unto them, “make ye not mischief in the earth” say they, ‘Verily, we are only the well – doers\nاَلَا ۤ اِنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْمُفْسِدُوْنَ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(12)\nALAA INNAHUM HOMUL MUFSEDOONA WA LAAKIL LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nBeware! Verily, they are the mischief - mongers but they perceive (it) not\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ اٰمِنُوْا كَمَاۤ اٰمَنَ النَّاسُ قَالُوْاۤ اَنُؤْمِنُ كَمَاۤ اٰمَنَ السُّفَهَآءُ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ هُمُ السُّفَهَآءُ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM AAMENOO KAMAA AAMANAN NAASO QAALOO A-NOAMENO KAMAA AAMANAS SOFA-HAAA, ALAA INNAHUM HOMUS SOFAHAAA-O WA LAAKIL LAA YA’LAMOON.\nWhen it is said unto them, “Believe ye as the (other) people did believe, they say, “shall we believe as the fools did believe?” Beware! Verily, they are the fools, but they know not\nوَاِذَا لَقُوْا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا قَالُوْاۤ اٰمَنَّا ۖۚ وَاِذَا خَلَوْا اِلٰى شَيٰطِيْنِهِمْۙ قَالُوْاۤ اِنَّا مَعَكُمْۙ اِنَّمَا نَحْنُ مُسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA EZAA LAQUL LAZEENA AAMANOO QAALOO AAMANNAA, WA EZAA KHALAW ELAA SHAYAADEENEHIM, QAALOO INNAA MA-A’KUM, INNAMAA NAHNO MUSTAHZEOON.\nAnd when they meet with those who believe, they say, “we believe” but when they go apart to their devils, they say, “surely we are with you, verily, we did but mock\nاَللّٰهُ يَسْتَهْزِئُ بِهِمْ وَيَمُدُّهُمْ فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(15)\nALLAAHO YASTAHZE-O BEHIM WA YAMUDDOHUM FEE TUGHYAANEHIM YA’MAHOON.\nGod mocketh at them and He only alloweth them to continue bewildered in their rebellion\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اشْتَرَوُا الضَّلٰلَةَ بِالْهُدٰى فَمَا رَبِحَتْ تِّجَارَتُهُمْ وَمَا كَانُوْا مُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(16)\nOOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENASH TARAWUZ ZALAALATA BIL-HODAA, FAMAA RABEHAT TEJAARATOHUM WA MAA KAANOO MOHTADEEN.\nThese are they who purchase error for guidance, hence their transaction profitteth them not, neither are they guided aright\nمَثَلُهُمْ كَمَثَلِ الَّذِى اسْتَوْقَدَ نَارًا ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَضَآءَتْ مَا حَوْلَهٗ ذَهَبَ اللّٰهُ بِنُوْرِهِمْ وَتَرَكَهُمْ فِىْ ظُلُمٰتٍ لَّا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(17)\nMASALOHUM KAMASALIL LAZIS TAWQADA NAARAA, FALAMMAA AZAA-AT MAA HAWLAHU ZAHABAL LAAHO BE-NOOREHIM WA TARAKAHUM FEE ZOLOMAATIL LAA YUBSEROON.\nThe likeness of them is like unto one who kindleth a fire, and when it lighteth all around him, God taketh away the light and leaveth them in darkness, they see not\nصُمٌّۢ بُكْمٌ عُمْىٌ فَهُمْ لَا يَرْجِعُوْنَ ۙ‏(18)\nSUMMUM BUKMUN U’MYUN FAHUM LAA YARJE-O’ONA.\n(They are) deaf, dumb and blind; hence they will return not (from their darkness)\nاَوْ كَصَيِّبٍ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ فِيْهِ ظُلُمٰتٌ وَّرَعْدٌ وَّبَرْقٌ ۚ يَجْعَلُوْنَ اَصَابِعَهُمْ فِىْۤ اٰذَانِهِمْ مِّنَ الصَّوَاعِقِ حَذَرَ الْمَوْتِؕ وَاللّٰهُ مُحِيْطٌۢ بِالْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(19)\nAW KASAYYEBIM MENAS SAMAAA-E FEEHE ZOLOMAATUNW WA RA’DUNW WA BARQ, YAJ-A’LOONA ASAABE-A’HUM FEE AAZAANEHIM MENAS SAWAA-E’QE HAZARAL MAWT, WAL LAAHO MOHEETUM BIL-KAAFEREEN.\nOr like a rainstorm from heaven fraught with darkness, thunder and lightning, they put their fingers in their ears against the thunderclaps for fear of death; and verily, God encompasseth the disbelievers\nيَكَادُ الْبَرْقُ يَخْطَفُ اَبْصَارَهُمْؕ كُلَّمَاۤ اَضَآءَ لَهُمْ مَّشَوْا فِيْهِۙ وَاِذَاۤ اَظْلَمَ عَلَيْهِمْ قَامُوْاؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَذَهَبَ بِسَمْعِهِمْ وَاَبْصَارِهِمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(20)\nYAKAADUL BARQO YAKHTAFO ABSAARAHUM, KULLAMAA A-ZAAA-A LAHUM MASHAW FEEHE, WA EZAA AZLAMA A’LAYHIM QAAMOO, WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAZAHABA BE-SAM-E’HIM WA ABSAAREHIM, INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nThe lightning well - nigh snatcheth away (a)their sight (from them)’, as often as it gleameth for them, they walk therein and when it getteth dark for them, they halt; if God willed, He could take away their hearing and their sight. Verily, God hath power over all things\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اعْبُدُوْا رَبَّكُمُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُوْنَ ۙ‏(21)\nYAA AYYOHAN NAASO’ BODOO RABBAKOMUL LAZEE KHALAQAKUM WAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TATTAQOONAL.\nO mankind! Worship ye (only) your Lord, Who created you and those before you, happily ye may guard (yourselves against evil)\nالَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ فِرَاشًا وَّالسَّمَآءَ بِنَآءً وَّاَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَخْرَجَ بِهٖ مِنَ الثَّمَرٰتِ رِزْقًا لَّكُمْۚ فَلَا تَجْعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ اَنْدَادًا وَّاَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ ‏(22)\nLAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA FERAASHANW WAS SAMAAA-A BENAAA-ANW, WA ANZALA MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA-AKHRAJA BEHI MENAS SAMARAATE RIZQAL LAKUM, FALAA TAJ-A’LOO LILLAAHE ANDAADANW WA ANTUL TA’LAMOON.\nWho made the earth a bed (resting place) for you and the sky a structure and causeth water to descend from heaven and thereby produceth fruits for your sustenance; set ye not Therefore, equals to God while ye already know\nوَاِنْ كُنْتُمْ فِىْ رَيْبٍ مِّمَّا نَزَّلْنَا عَلٰى عَبْدِنَا فَاْتُوْا بِسُوْرَةٍ مِّنْ مِّثْلِهٖ وَادْعُوْا شُهَدَآءَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(23)\nWA IN KUNTUM FEE RAIBIM MIMMAA NAZZALNAA A’LAA A’BDENAA FAATOO BE-SOORATIM MIM MISLEH, WAD-O’O SHOHADAAA-AKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nIf ye be in doubt about what We have sent down unto Our Servant (Muhammad) produce ye then a surah (chapter) like unto it, and call ye your witnesses other than God, if ye be truthful\nفَاِنْ لَّمْ تَفْعَلُوْا وَلَنْ تَفْعَلُوْا فَاتَّقُوْا النَّارَ الَّتِىْ وَقُوْدُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجَارَةُ  ۖۚ اُعِدَّتْ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(24)\nFA-IL LAM TAF-A’LOO WA LAN TAF-A’LOO FAT-TAQUN NAARAL LATEE WA QOODOHAN NAASO WAL HEJAARAH, O-I’DDAT LIL-KAAFEREEN.\nBut if ye do (it) not, and never shall ye do (it) then guard ye (yourselves) against the (Hell) fire whose fuel shall be the people and stones, prepared for the disbelievers\nوَبَشِّرِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ اَنَّ لَهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُؕ ڪُلَّمَا رُزِقُوْا مِنْهَا مِنْ ثَمَرَةٍ رِّزْقًا ۙ قَالُوْا هٰذَا الَّذِىْ رُزِقْنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَاُتُوْا بِهٖ مُتَشَابِهًا ؕ وَلَهُمْ فِيْهَآ اَزْوَاجٌ مُّطَهَّرَةٌ ۙ وَّهُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(25)\nWA BASH-SHERIL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE ANNA LAHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAAR, KULLAMAA ROZEQOO MINHAA MIN SAMARATIR RIZQAN, QAALOO HAAZAL LAZEE ROZIQNAA MIN QABLO, WA OTOO BEHI MOTASHAA-BEHAA, WA LAHUM FEEHAA AZWAAJUM MOTAHHARATUNW, WA HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nGive thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) the glad tiding unto those who believe and do good deeds, that for them are gardens beneath which flow rivers, and whenever they are provided with fruits therefrom they shall say, “This is what we were provided with before!” and they shall be provided with the like (of it) and for them shall be mates purified. They shall dwell therein\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَسْتَحْىٖۤ اَنْ يَّضْرِبَ مَثَلًا مَّا بَعُوْضَةً فَمَا فَوْقَهَا ؕ فَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فَيَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّهِمْۚ وَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ ڪَفَرُوْا فَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَاذَآ اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ بِهٰذَا مَثَلًا ۘ يُضِلُّ بِهٖ ڪَثِيْرًا وَّيَهْدِىْ بِهٖ كَثِيْرًا ؕ وَمَا يُضِلُّ بِهٖۤ اِلَّا الْفٰسِقِيْنَۙ ‏(26)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YASTAHYEE AN-Y YAZREMBA MASALAM MAA BA-O’OZATAN FAMAA FAWQAHAA, FA-AMMAL LAZEENA AAMANOO FA-YA’LAMOONA ANNAHUL HAQQO MIR RABBEHIM, WA AMMAL LAZEENA KAFAROO FA-YAQOOLOONA MAA ZAA ARAADAL LAAHO BEHAAZAA MASALAA, YOZILLO BEHI KASEERANW, WA YAHDEE BEHI KASEERAA, WA MAA YOZILLO BEHI ILLAL FAASEQEENAL.\nVerily God is not ashamed to set forth a parable of a gnat and anything beyond it; those who believe, know that it is the Truth from their Lord; but those who disbelieve say, “What meaneth God by this parable? He leadeth astray thereby many and guideth aright thereby many”; but He leadeth not astray by it except the transgressors\nالَّذِيْنَ يَنْقُضُوْنَ عَهْدَ اللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مِيْثَاقِهٖ وَيَقْطَعُوْنَ مَآ اَمَرَ اللّٰهُ بِهٖۤ اَنْ يُّوْصَلَ وَيُفْسِدُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(27)\nLAZEENA YANQOZOONA A’HDAL LAAHE MIM BA’DE MEESAAQEH, WA YAQTA-O’ONA MAA AMARAL LAAHO BEHI AN-Y YOOSALA WA YUFSEDOONA FIL ARZ, OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nThose who violate the covenant of God after its being covenanted thereof, and sever that which God commandeth to be joined,’ and make mischief in the earth; these are they who are the losers\nكَيْفَ تَكْفُرُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَڪُنْتُمْ اَمْوَاتًا فَاَحْيَاكُمْۚ ثُمَّ يُمِيْتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيْكُمْ ثُمَّ اِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(28)\nKAYFA TAKFOROONA BIL-LAAHE WA KUNTUM AMWAATAN FA-AHYAAKUM, SUMMA YOMEETOKUM SUMMA YOHYEEKUM SUMMA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nHow can ye disbelieve in God; for ye were lifeless (in your mother’s womb). He brought you to life. He causeth you to die and again (He will) restore you to life then unto Him (only) will ye be returned\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ لَكُمْ مَّا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰۤى اِلَى السَّمَآءِ فَسَوّٰٮهُنَّ سَبْعَ سَمٰوٰتٍؕ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(29)\nHOWAL LAZEE KHALAQA LAKUM MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A, SUMMAS TAWAA ELAS SAMAAA-E FASAWWAAHUNNA SAB-A’ SAMAAWAAT, WA HOWA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nHe, it is who created for you all that is in the earth and then directed to the heavens (and) then fashioned them into seven heavens; and (while) He, of all things, is the Knower\nوَاِذْ قَالَ رَبُّكَ لِلْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ اِنِّىْ جَاعِلٌ فِى الْاَرْضِ خَلِيْفَةً ؕ قَالُوْٓا اَتَجْعَلُ فِيْهَا مَنْ يُّفْسِدُ فِيْهَا وَيَسْفِكُ الدِّمَآءَۚ وَنَحْنُ نُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِكَ وَنُقَدِّسُ لَكَؕ قَالَ اِنِّىْٓ اَعْلَمُ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(30)\nWA IZ QAALA RABBOKA LIL-MALAAA-EKATE INNEE JAA-E’LUN FIL ARZE KHALEEFAH, QAALOO A-TAJ-A’LO FEEHAA MAN-Y YUFSEDO FEEHAA WA YASFEKUD DEMAAA, WA NAHNO NOSABBEHO BE-HAMDEKA WA NOQADDESO LAK, QAALA INNEE A-A’LAMO MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\n(Recollect O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) When said thy Lord unto the ‘angels: ‘Verily I (intend to) appoint a vicegerent in the earth’ they said, “Wilt Thou (O’ our Lord!) appoint therein one who will cause mischief and shed blood, while we celebrate by Thy praise and hallow Thee alone?” Said (the Lord to the angels) “Verily, I know what ye know not\nوَعَلَّمَ اٰدَمَ الْاَسْمَآءَ كُلَّهَا ثُمَّ عَرَضَهُمْ عَلَى الْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ فَقَالَ اَنْۢبِئُوْنِىْ بِاَسْمَآءِ هٰٓؤُلَآءِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA A’LLAMA AADAMAL ASMAAA-A KULLAHAA SUMMA A’RAZAHUM A’LAL MALAA-EKATE, FAQAALA AMBE-OONEE BE-ASMAAA-E HAA-OOLAAA-E IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd He taught Adam the Names, all of them, and then set them unto the angels and said, “Declare ye unto Me the names of these if ye be truthful\nقَالُوْا سُبْحٰنَكَ لَا عِلْمَ لَنَآ اِلَّا مَا عَلَّمْتَنَا ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْعَلِيْمُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(32)\nQAALOO SUBHAANAKA LAA I’LMA LANAA ILLAA MAA A’LLAMTANAA, INNKA ANTAL A’LEEMUL HAKEEM.\nThey said: “Glory be to Thee (O’ Lord!) we have no knowledge save what Thou hast taught us; Verily, Thou, Thou (alone) art the All Knowing, the All-Wise\nقَالَ يٰٓاٰدَمُ اَنْۢبِئْهُمْ بِاَسْمَآئِهِمْۚ فَلَمَّآ اَنْۢبَاَهُمْ بِاَسْمَآئِهِمْۙ قَالَ اَلَمْ اَقُل لَّكُمْ اِنِّىْٓ اَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِۙ وَاَعْلَمُ مَا تُبْدُوْنَ وَمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْتُمُوْنَ‏(33)\nQAALA YAA AADAMO AMBEAHUM BE-ASMAAA-EHIM, FALAMMAA AMBA-AHUM BE-ASMAAA-EHIM, QAALA ALAM AQUL LAKUM INNEE A-A’LAMO GHAYBAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE, WA A-A’LAMO MAA TUBDOONA WA MAA KUNTUM TAKTOMOON.\nSaid He “O’ Adam! inform thou unto them their names,” and when he had informed unto them their name; Said (the Lord): “Said I not unto you that verily, I know the secrets of the heavens and the earth and know that which ye declare and that which ye conceal?\nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ فَسَجَدُوْٓا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ اَبٰى وَاسْتَكْبَرَ  وَكَانَ مِنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(34)\nWA IZ QULNAL MALAA-EKATIS JODOO LE-AADAMA FA-SAJADOO ILLAA IBLEES, ABAA WAS TAKBAR, WA KAANA MENAL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd when said We unto the angels “Prostrate ye before Adam!” they all prostrated save Iblis, he refrained and was puffed with pride and was turned into one of the disbelievers\nوَقُلْنَا يٰٓاٰدَمُ اسْكُنْ اَنْتَ وَزَوْجُكَ الْجَنَّةَ وَكُلَا مِنْهَا رَغَدًا حَيْثُ شِئْتُمَا وَلَا تَقْرَبَا هٰذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُوْنَا مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(35)\nWA QULNAA YAA AADAMUS KUN ANTA WA ZAWJOKAL JANNATA WA KOLAA MINHAA RAGHADAN HAYSO SHEATOMAA, WA LAA TAQRABAA HAAZEHISH SHAJARATA FA-TAKOONAA MENAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd said We “O’ Adam! dwell thou and thy mate in Garden and eat ye two therefrom freely as ye two wish but approach not ye two this tree lest ye two will be of the transgressors!\nفَاَزَلَّهُمَا الشَّيْطٰنُ عَنْهَا فَاَخْرَجَهُمَا مِمَّا كَانَا فِيْهِ وَقُلْنَا اهْبِطُوْا بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ ۚ وَلَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مُسْتَقَرٌّ وَّمَتَاعٌ اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(36)\nFA-AZALLAHOMASH SHAYTAANO A’NHAA FA-AKHRAJAHOMAA MIMMAA KAANAA FEEH, WA QULNAH BETOO BA’ZOKUM LE-BA’ZIN A’DUWW, WA LAKUM FIL ARZE MUSTAQARRUNW WA MATAA-U’N ELAA HEEN.\nBut Satan made them slip and drove them out of what they were in; and (whereupon) said We, “Get ye down! the one of you as an enemy unto the other and there shall be an abode for you in the earth and provision for a (fixed) time\nفَتَلَقّٰٓى اٰدَمُ مِنْ رَّبِّهٖ كَلِمٰتٍ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(37)\nFA-TALAQQAA AADAMO MIR RABBEHI KALEMAATIN FA-TAABA A’LAYH, INNAHU HOWAT TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\nAnd received Adam from his Lord (certain) words (of prayer) and God turned unto him (mercifully) (for) verily, He is the Oft - turning (unto mercy) the Most Merciful\nقُلْنَا اهْبِطُوْا مِنْهَا جَمِيْعًا ۚ فَاِمَّا يَاْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِّنِّىْ هُدًى فَمَنْ تَبِعَ هُدَاىَ فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(38)\nQULNAH BETOO MINHAA JAMEE-A’A, FA-IMMAA YAATEYANNAKUM MINNEE HODAN FAMAN TA-BE-A’ HODAAYA FALAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM YAHZANOON.\nSaid We (then), “Get down ye therefrom all together and when there cometh from Me unto you a guidance, and whoso followeth My guidance, no fear shall come on them, nor shall they grieve!\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَكَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَآ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(39)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR, HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nBut they who disbelieve and belie Our signs, they are those who shall be the fellows of the (Hell) Fire: they shall abide therein\nيٰبَنِىْٓ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتِىَ الَّتِىْٓ اَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَاَوْفُوْا بِعَهْدِىْٓ اُوْفِ بِعَهْدِكُمْۚ وَاِيَّاىَ فَارْهَبُوْنِ‏(40)\nYAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ KOROO NE’MATEYAL LATEE AN-A’MTO A’LAYKUM WA AWFOO BE-A’HDEE OOFE BE-A’HDEKUM, WA IYYAAYA FARHABOON.\nO’ children of Isra’il! Remember ye My bounties I bestowed upon you, and fulfil ye your covenant with Me, I shall fulfil My covenant with you and of Me alone (should) ye be afraid\nوَاٰمِنُوْا بِمَآ اَنْزَلْتُ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا مَعَكُمْ وَلَا تَكُوْنُوْآ اَوَّلَ كَافِرٍۢ بِهٖ وَلَا تَشْتَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِىْ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا وَّاِيَّاىَ فَاتَّقُوْنِ‏(41)\nWA AAMENOO BEMAA ANZALTO MOSADDEQAL LEMAA MA-A’KUM WA LAA TAKOONOO AWWALA KAAFERIM BEH, WA LAA TASHTAROO BE-AAYAATEE SAMANAN QALEELAA, WA IYYAAYA FAT-TAQOON.\nAnd believe ye in (that) (a) which) I have sent down testifying that which ye have with you (of the scriptures) and be not first to disbelieve therein and barter not My signs with a mean price; and in Me alone shall ye take shelter\nوَلَا تَلْبِسُوا الْحَقَّ بِالْبَاطِلِ وَتَكْتُمُوا الْحَقَّ وَاَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(42)\nWA LAA TALBESUL HAQQA BIL-BAATELE WA TAKTOMUL HAQQA WA ANTUM TA’LAMOON.\nMix ye not the truth with falsehood and hide ye not the truth when ye know (it)\nوَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَارْكَعُوْا مَعَ الرّٰكِعِيْنَ‏(43)\nWA AQEEMUS SALAATA WA AATUZ ZAKAATA WAR KA-O’O MA-A’R RAAKE-E’EN.\nEstablish ye the prayer and give ye away the poor - rate and bow ye down (while ye bow down (praying)\nاَتَاْمُرُوْنَ النَّاسَ بِالْبِرِّ وَتَنْسَوْنَ اَنْفُسَكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ تَتْلُوْنَ الْكِتٰبَؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(44)\nA TAAMOROONAN NAASA BIL-BIRRE WA TANSAWNA ANFOSAKUM WA ANTUM TATLOONAL KETAAB, AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nWhat! Enjoin ye upon the people righteousness and ye forget your own selves? Yet ye read the scripture? What! do ye not understand?\nوَاسْتَعِيْنُوْا بِالصَّبْرِ وَالصَّلٰوةِ ؕ وَاِنَّهَا لَكَبِيْرَةٌ اِلَّا عَلَى الْخٰشِعِيْنَۙ‏(45)\nWAS TA-E’ENOO BIS SABRE WAS SALAAH, WA INNAHAA LA-KABEERATUN ILLAA A’LAL KHASHE-E’ENAL.\nAnd seek ye help (from God) through patience and prayer; verily, it is a hard (task) indeed, save upon the humble\nالَّذِيْنَ يَظُنُّوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ مُّلٰقُوْا رَبِّهِمْ وَاَنَّهُمْ اِلَيْهِ رٰجِعُوْنَ‏(46)\nLAZEENA YAZUNNOONA ANNAHUM MOLAAQOO RABBEHIM WA ANNAHUM ELAYHE RAAJE-O’ON.\nThose who think that they will surely meet their Lord and that verily unto Him shall they return\nيٰبَنِىْٓ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتِىَ الَّتِىْٓ اَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَاَنِّىْ فَضَّلْتُكُمْ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(47)\nYAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ KOROO NE’MATEYAL LATEE AN-A’MTO A’LAYKUM WA ANNEE FAZZALTOKUM A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nO’ ye Children of Isra’il! remember My bounties which I favoured you with, and that I gave you a preference to the people of the world\nوَاتَّقُوْا يَوْمًا لَّا تَجْزِىْ نَفْسٌ عَنْ نَّفْسٍ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يُقْبَلُ مِنْهَا شَفَاعَةٌ وَّلَا يُؤْخَذُ مِنْهَا عَدْلٌ وَّلَا هُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(48)\nWAT TAQOO YAWMAL LAA TAJ-ZEE NAFSUN A’N NAFSIN SHAY-AN WA LAA YUQBALO MINHAA SHAFAA-A’TUNW WA LAA YOAKHAZO MINHAA A’DLUNW WA LAA HUM YUNSAROON.\nGuard ye yourselves against the day wherein no soul shall compensate for another nor from it shall intercession be accepted nor from it shall any ransom be taken, nor shall they be helped\nوَاِذْ نَجَّيْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَسُوْمُوْنَكُمْ سُوْٓءَ الْعَذَابِ يُذَبِّحُوْنَ اَبْنَآءَكُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيُوْنَ نِسَآءَكُمْؕ وَفِىْ ذٰلِكُمْ بَلَاۤءٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ عَظِيْمٌ‏(49)\nWA IZ NAJJAYNAAKUM MIN AALE FIR-A’WNA YASOOMOONAKUM SOOO-AL A’ZAABE YOZABBEHOONA ABNAAA-AKUM WA YAS-TAHYOONA NESAAA-AKUM, WA FEE ZAALEKUM BALAAA-UM MIR RABBEKUM A’ZEEM.\nAnd (remember ye) when We delivered you from Pharaoh’s people who afflicted you with grievous torment, slaying your sons and by letting your women alive, and in that was a great trial from your Lord\nوَاِذْ فَرَقْنَا بِكُمُ الْبَحْرَ فَاَنْجَيْنٰكُمْ وَاَغْرَقْنَآ اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَاَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(50)\nWA IZ FARAQNAA BEKOMUL BAHRA FA-ANJAYNAAKUM WA AGHRAQNAA AALA FIR-A’WNA WA ANTUM TANZOROON.\nAnd (remember ye) when We did split for you the sea and rescued you and drowned Pharaoh’s people; while ye looked on\nوَاِذْ وٰعَدْنَا مُوْسٰٓى اَرْبَعِيْنَ لَيْلَةً ثُمَّ اتَّخَذْتُمُ الْعِجْلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ وَاَنْتُمْ ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(51)\nWA IZ WAA-A’DNAA MOOSAA ARBA-E’ENA LAYLATAN SUMMAT TAKHAZTOMUL I’JLA MIM BA’DEHI WA ANTUM ZAALEMUN.\nWhen We made appointment with Moses for forty nights then ye took the calf (for your god) after he left you and (thus) ye transgressed\nثُمَّ عَفَوْنَا عَنْكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰلِكَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(52)\nSUMMA A’FAWNAA A’NKUM MIM BA’DE ZAALEKA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nYet after that We forgave you that ye might be grateful\nوَاِذْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ وَالْفُرْقَانَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(53)\nWA IZ AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA WAL FURQAANA LA-A’LLAKUM TAHTADOON.\nAnd We gave Moses the Scripture and the Distinction (of good and evil) that ye may be guided\nوَاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهٖ يٰقَوْمِ اِنَّكُمْ ظَلَمْتُمْ اَنْفُسَكُمْ بِاتِّخَاذِكُمُ الْعِجْلَ فَتُوْبُوْآ اِلٰى بَارِئِكُمْ فَاقْتُلُوْٓا اَنْفُسَكُمْؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ عِنْدَ بَارِئِكُمْؕ فَتَابَ عَلَيْكُمْؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(54)\nWA IZ QAALA MOOSAA LE-QAWMEHI YAA QAWME INNAKUM ZALAMTUM ANFOSAKUM BIT-TEKHAAZEKOMUL I’JLA FA-TOOOO ELAA BAARE-EKUM FAQTOLOO ANFOSAKUM, ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM I’NDA BAA-RE-EKUM FA-TAABA A’LAYKUM, INNAHU HOWAT TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\nAnd (remember ye) when said Moses unto his people “O’ my people! Verily ye have wronged (unto) yourselves by taking the calf for God, so turn ye (penitent) unto your Creator’ Lord and slay ye yourselves that will be better for you with your Creator Lord” and (thus) did He turn unto you (Merciful and pardoned you) Verily, He is the Oft - turning (to mercy) and the Most Merciful\nوَاِذْ قُلْتُمْ يٰمُوْسٰى لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتّٰى نَرَى اللّٰهَ جَهْرَةً فَاَخَذَتْكُمُ الصّٰعِقَةُ وَاَنْتُمْ تَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(55)\nWA IZ QULTUM YAA MOOSAA LAN NOAMENA LAKA HATTAA NARAL LAAHA JAHRATN FA-AKHA-ZATKOMUS SAA-E’QATO WA ANTUM TANZOROON.\nAnd (remember ye!) when ye said, “O’ Moses! never will we believe in thee until we see manifestly,” the Thunder seized you while ye looked on\nثُمَّ بَعَثْنٰكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَوْتِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(56)\nSUMMA BA-A’SNAAKUM MIM BA’DE MAWTEKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nThen We raised you after your death that haply ye might be thankful\nوَظَلَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْغَمَامَ وَاَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوٰىؕ كُلُوْا مِنْ طَيِّبٰتِ مَا رَزَقْنٰكُمْؕ وَمَا ظَلَمُوْنَا وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْآ اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(57)\nWA ZALLALNAA A’LAYKOMUL GHAMAAMA WA ANZALNAA A’LAYKOMUL MANNA WAS SALWAA, KOLOO MIN TAYYEBAATE MAA RAZAQNAAKUM, WA MAA ZALAMOONAA WA LAAKIN KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nAnd We caused clouds to ‘shadow over you and We sent down unto you ‘Manna’ and quails; (saying) ‘eat ye of good things wherewith We have provided you;’ and they wronged not to Us but they were unto their own selves unjust\nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا ادْخُلُوْا هٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةَ فَكُلُوْا مِنْهَا حَيْثُ شِئْتُمْ رَغَدًا وَّادْخُلُوا الْبَابَ سُجَّدًا وَّقُوْلُوْا حِطَّةٌ نَّغْفِرْ لَكُمْ خَطٰيٰكُمْؕ وَسَنَزِيْدُ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(58)\nWA IZ QULNAD KHOLOO HAAZEHIL QARYATA FA-KOLOO MINHAA HAYSO SHEATUM RAGHADANW WAD-KHOLUL BAABA SUJJADANW WA QOOLOO HITTATUN NAGHFIR LAKUM KHATAAYAAKUM, WA SANAZEEDUL MOHSENEEN.\nAnd (remember ye) when We said, “Enter ye this city, and eat ye as ye like of the plenty therein, and enter ye the gates prostrating (in obeisance) and be ye (prayerfully) uttering ‘Pardon’ (us) We shall forgive your sins; and anon increase (Our favours) unto the doers of good (unto others)\nفَبَدَّلَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا قَوْلاً غَيْرَ الَّذِىْ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ فَاَنْزَلْنَا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا رِجْزًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(59)\nFA-BADDALAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO QAWLAN GHAYRAL LAZEE QEELA LAHUM FA-ANZALNAA A’LAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO RIJZAM MENAS SAMAAA-E BEMAA KAANOO YAFSOQOON.\nBut changed those who were unjust the word into another than that which had been spoken unto them, So, We sent down upon those who were unjust a torment from heaven for what they used to pervert\nوَاِذِ اسْتَسْقَىٰ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهٖ فَقُلْنَا اضْرِب بِّعَصَاكَ الْحَجَرَؕ فَانْفَجَرَتْ مِنْهُ اثْنَتَا عَشْرَةَ عَيْنًاؕ قَدْ عَلِمَ كُلُّ اُنَاسٍ مَّشْرَبَهُمْؕ كُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا مِنْ رِّزْقِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِىْ الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(60)\nWA EZIS TASQAA MOOSAA LE-QAWMEHI FA-QULNAZ RIB BE-A’SAAKAL HAJAR, FANFAJARAT MINHUS NATAA A’SHRATA A’YNAA, QAD A’LEMA KULLO ONAASIM MASHRABAHUM, KOLOO WASH RABOO MIR RIZQIL LAAHE WA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\nAnd remember when Moses sought water for his people; said We, “Strike thou the rock with thy staff!”. Then gushed out therefrom twelve springs; each people knew their, (respective) drinking place; “Eat ye and drink ye of God’s provision, and commit ye not evil in the earth acting mischievously!\nوَاِذْ قُلْتُمْ يٰمُوْسٰى لَنْ نَّصْبِرَ عَلٰى طَعَامٍ وَّاحِدٍ فَادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُخْرِجْ لَنَا مِمَّا تُنْۢبِتُ الْاَرْضُ مِنْۢ بَقْلِهَا وَقِثَّآئِهَا وَفُوْمِهَا وَعَدَسِهَا وَ بَصَلِهَاؕ قَالَ اَتَسْتَبْدِلُوْنَ الَّذِىْ هُوَ اَدْنٰى بِالَّذِىْ هُوَ خَيْرٌؕ اِهْبِطُوْا مِصْرًا فَاِنَّ لَكُمْ مَّا سَاَلْتُمْؕ وَضُرِبَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الذِّلَّةُ وَالْمَسْكَنَةُ وَبَآءُوْ بِغَضَبٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِؕ ذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا يَكْفُرُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَيَقْتُلُوْنَ النَّبِيّٖنَ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّؕ ذٰلِكَ بِمَا عَصَوا وَّڪَانُوْا يَعْتَدُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA IZ QULTUM YAA MOOSAA LAN NASBERA A’LAA TA-A’AMINW WAAHEDIN FAD-O’ LANAA RABBAKA YUKHRIJ LANAA MIMMAA TUMBETUL ARZO MIM BAQLEHAA WA QISSAAA-EHAA WA FOOMEHAA WA A’DASEHAA WA BASALEHAA, QAALA ATASTABDELOONAL LAZEE HOWA ADNAA BIL-LAZEE HOWA KHAYR, EHBETOO MISRAN FA-INNA LAKUM MAA SA-ALTUM, WA ZOREBAT A’LAYHEMUZ ZILLATO WAL MASKANAH, WA BAAA-OO BE-GHAZABIM MENAL LAAH, ZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAANOO YAKFOROONA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WA YAQTOLOONAN NABIYYEENA BEGHAYRIL HAQQ, ZAALEKA BEMAA A’SAW WA KAANOO YA’TADOON.\nAnd (remember ye) when ye said, “O’ Moses! never can we (always) endure one kind of food, so pray thou unto thy Lord for us, to produce for us of what the earth groweth, its herbs, and cucumbers, its garlic, lentils, and onions!” Said he, “Seek ye to exchange that which is inferior for that which is superior? Go ye down to (settle into) some town and there ye shall have what ye ask for!”; And humiliation and wretchedness were stamped upon them, and they drew unto themselves the Wrath from God; This because they used to reject the signs of God and slay his apostles unjustly; this because they disobeyed and were wont to transgress\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَالَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا وَالنَّصٰرٰى وَالصّٰبِئِيْنَ مَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَلَهُمْ اَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْۚ وَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(62)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAL LAZEENA HAADOO WAN NASAARAA WAS SAABE-EENA MAN AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FALAHUM AJROHUM I’NDA RABBEHIM, WA LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM YAHZANOON.\nVerily those who believe (in that) which is revealed unto thee, (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) and those who Are Jews and the Christians and the Sabians and whosoever believeth in God and the Last Day (of Judgment) for them is their reward with their Lord, and there shall be no fear for them nor shall they grieve\nوَاِذْ اَخَذْنَا مِيْثَاقَكُمْ وَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَكُمُ الطُّوْرَؕ خُذُوْا مَآ اٰتَيْنٰكُمْ بِقُوَّةٍ وَّ اذْكُرُوْا مَا فِيْهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(63)\nWA IZ AKHAZNAA MEESAAQAKUM WA RAFA’NAA FAWQAKOMUT TOOR, KHOZOO MAA AATAYNAAKUM BE-QUWWATINW WAZ KOROO MAA FEEHE LA-A’LLAKUM TATTAQOON.\nAnd remember when We made a covenant with you and ^raised the ‘Tur’(a) (the Mountain) above you; (saying), “Hold ye fast that which We have bestowed upon you with the strength (of determination) and remember that which is therein so that ye may guard (yourself) against evil\nثُمَّ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰلِكَۚ فَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ لَكُنْتُمْ مِّنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(64)\nSUMMA TAWALLAYTUM MIM BA’DE ZAALEKA FA-LAWLAA FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA RAHMATOHU LAKUNTUM MENAL KHAASEREEN.\n(Yet) thereafter ye turned back, and had it not been for the grace and mercy of God on you, ye had been among the losers\nوَلَقَدْ عَلِمْتُمُ الَّذِيْنَ اعْتَدَوْا مِنْكُمْ فِىْ السَّبْتِ فَقُلْنَا لَهُمْ كُوْنُوْا قِرَدَةً خَاسِئِيْنَ ۚ‏(65)\nWA LAQAD A’LIMTOMUL LAZEENA’ TADAW MINKUM FIS SABTE FAQULNAA LAHUM KOONOO QERADATAN KHAASE-EEN.\nAnd indeed ye know of those amongst you who transgressed on the Sabbath, so We said unto them, “Be ye apes, despised and spurned!\nفَجَعَلْنٰهَا نَكٰلاً لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهَا وَمَا خَلْفَهَا وَمَوْعِظَةً لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(66)\nFA-JA-A’LNAAHAA NAKAALAL LEMAA BAYNAA YADAYHAA WA MAA KHALFAHAA WA MAW-E’ZATAL LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nSo, We made it a lesson for (those of) their own times and for those (of their posterity) who came after them and an exhortation unto those who guard (themselves) against evil\nوَاِذْ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَاْمُرُكُمْ اَنْ تَذْبَحُوْا بَقَرَةً  ؕ قَالُوْآ اَتَتَّخِذُنَا هُزُوًْا ؕ قَالَ اَعُوْذُ بِاللّٰهِ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(67)\nWA IZ QAALA MOOSAA LE-QAWMEHI INNAL LAAHA YAAMOROKUM AN TAZBAHOO BAQARAH, QAALOO A-TATTAKHEZONAA HOZOWAA, QAALA A-O’OZO BIL-LAAHE AN AKOONA MENAL JAAHELEEN.\nAnd remember when Moses said unto his people, “Verily, God commandeth you to sacrifice a heifer,” Said they, “Dost thou ridicule us?” He said, “I seek protection of God from being one of the ignorant ones\nقَالُوا ادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَّنَا مَا هِىَؕ قَالَ اِنَّهٗ يَقُوْلُ اِنَّهَا بَقَرَةٌ لَّا فَارِضٌ وَّلَا بِكْرٌؕ عَوَانٌۢ بَيْنَ ذٰلِكَؕ فَافْعَلُوْا مَا تُؤْمَرُوْنَ‏(68)\nQAALUD O’ LANAA RABBAKA YOBAYYIL LANAA MAA HEE, QAALA INNAHU YAQOOLO INNAHAA BAQARATUL LAA FAAREZUNW WA LAA BIKR, A’WAANUM BAYNA ZAALEK, FAF-A’LOO MAA TOAMAROON.\nThey said, “Pray for us unto thy Lord to make it plain unto us what heifer it is!” He said, “sayeth He, she is a heifer neither too old nor too young, but of middling age; between that (and this) now act ye Therefore, as ye are commanded\nقَالُوا ادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَّنَا مَا لَوْنُهَا ؕ قَالَ اِنَّهٗ يَقُوْلُ اِنَّهَا بَقَرَةٌ صَفْرَآءُۙ فَاقِعٌ لَّوْنُهَا تَسُرُّ النّٰظِرِيْنَ‏(69)\nQAALUD O’ LANAA RABBAKA YOBAYYIL LANAA MAA LAWNOHAA, QAALA INNAHU YAQOOLO INNAHAA BAQARATUN SAFRAAA-O, FAAQE-U’L LAWNOHAA TASURRUN NAAZEREEN.\nThey said, “Pray for us unto thy Lord that He maketh clear to us of what colour she is. He (Moses) said: “sayeth He, Verily, she is a yellow cow; her colour is intensely yellow, delighting the beholders\nقَالُوا ادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَّنَا مَا هِىَۙ اِنَّ الْبَقَرَ تَشٰبَهَ عَلَيْنَا ؕ وَاِنَّآ اِنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَمُهْتَدُوْنَ‏(70)\nQAALUD O’ LANAA RABBAKA YOBAYYIL LANAA MAA HEYA, INNAL BAQARA TASHAABAHA A’LAYNAA, WA INNAA IN SHAAA-AL LAAHO LA-MOHTADOON.\nThey said, “Pray for us unto thy Lord to make (further) clear to us what (cow) she is. Lo! cows are all alike to us and if God willeth we shall surely be guided aright\nقَالَ اِنَّهٗ يَقُوْلُ اِنَّهَا بَقَرَةٌ لَّا ذَلُوْلٌ تُثِيْرُ الْاَرْضَ وَلَا تَسْقِى الْحَرْثَ ۚ مُسَلَّمَةٌ لَّا شِيَةَ فِيْهَا ؕ قَالُوا الْٴٰنَ جِئْتَ بِالْحَقِّؕ فَذَبَحُوْهَا وَمَا كَادُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏‏(71)\nQAALA INNAHU YAQOOLO INNAHAA BAQARATUL LAA ZALOOLUN TOSEERUL ARZA WA LAA TASQIL HARS, MOSALLAMATUL LAA SHEYATA FEEHAA, QAALUL AANA JEATA BIL-HAQ, FAZABAHOOHAA WA MAA KAADOO YAF-A’LOON.\n(Moses) Said, “Verily, sayeth He, Verily, she is a cow not (yet) used to till the soil or irrigate the tilth; sound and without blemish” They said, “Now hast thou brought the truth;” So they sacrificed her, though they had not the mind to do it\nوَ اِذْ قَتَلْتُمْ نَفْسًا فَادّٰرَءْتُمْ فِيْهَا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ مُخْرِجٌ مَّا كُنْتُمْ تَكْتُمُوْنَۚ‏(72)\nWA IZ QATALTUM NAFSAN FADDAARATUM FEEHAA, WAL LAAHO MUKHREJUM MAA KUNTUM TAKTOMOON.\nAnd remember when ye slew a man and yourselves disputed about it; God was to bring forth (to light) what ye did hide\nفَقُلْنَا اضْرِبُوْهُ بِبَعْضِهَا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُحْىِ اللّٰهُ الْمَوْتٰى ۙ وَيُرِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(73)\nFAQULNAZ REBOOHO BE-BA’ZEHAA, KAZAALEKA YOHYIL LAAHUL MAWTAA, WA YOREEKUM AAYAATEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TA’QELOON.\n(Wherefore) We said, “ye strike him with a part of it; (of the cow); “Thus, God bringeth the dead to life and showeth to you His signs, so that ye may understand\nثُمَّ قَسَتْ قُلُوْبُكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰلِكَ فَهِىَ كَالْحِجَارَةِ اَوْ اَشَدُّ قَسْوَةً  ؕ وَاِنَّ مِنَ الْحِجَارَةِ لَمَا يَتَفَجَّرُ مِنْهُ الْاَنْهٰرُؕ وَاِنَّ مِنْهَا لَمَا يَشَّقَّقُ فَيَخْرُجُ مِنْهُ الْمَآءُؕ وَاِنَّ مِنْهَا لَمَا يَهْبِطُ مِنْ خَشْيَةِ اللّٰهِؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(74)\nSUMMA QASAT QOLOOBOKUM MIM BA’DE ZAALEKA FAHEYA KAL-HEJAARATE AW ASHADDO QASWAH, WA INNA MENAL HEJAARATE LAMAA YATAFAJJARO MINHUL ANHAAR, WA INNA MINHAA LAMAA YASHSHAQQAQO FAYAKHROJO MINHUL MAAA, WA INNA MINHAA LAMAA YAHBETO MIN KHASYATIL LAAH, WA MAL LAAHO BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\n(Yet) Thenceforth were your hearts hardened as stones or harder still; for verily of stones are some from which gush forth streams; others there are which split asunder and from them cometh out water; and of them there are some that fall down for fear of God; And God is not heedless of what ye do\nاَفَتَطْمَعُوْنَ اَنْ يُّؤْمِنُوْا لَكُمْ وَقَدْ كَانَ فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْهُمْ يَسْمَعُوْنَ كَلَامَ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ يُحَرِّفُوْنَهٗ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا عَقَلُوْهُ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(75)\nA FATATMA-O’ONA AN-Y YOAMENOO LAKUM WA QAD KAANA FAREEQUM MINHUM YAS-MA-O’ONA KALAAMAL LAAHE SUMMA YOHARREFOONAHU MIM BA’DE MAA A’QALOOHO WA HUM YA’LAMOON.\nDo ye (O’ believers in God) then hope, that they will believe in you? While a party of them used to hear the word of God and then (knowingly) altered it after they had understood it and they know (This)\nوَاِذَا لَقُوْا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا قَالُوْآ اٰمَنَّا  ۖۚ وَاِذَا خَلَا بَعْضُهُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضٍ قَالُوْآ اَ تُحَدِّثُوْنَهُمْ بِمَا فَتَحَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمْ لِيُحَآجُّوْكُمْ بِهٖ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(76)\nWA EZAA LAQUL LAZEENA AAMANOO QAALOO AAMANNAA, WA EZAA KHALAA BA’ZOHUM ELAA BA’ZIN QAALOO ATOHADDESOONAHUM BEMAA FATAHAL LAAHO A’LAYKUM LE-YOHAAAJJOOKUM BEHI I’NDA RABBEKUM, A-FALAA TA’QELOON.\nAnd when they meet those who believe they say, “We believe” and when they are alone one with another they say, “Do ye talk to them what God hath revealed against you (in Torah) that they may argue with you about it before your Lord;” Do ye not then understand?\nاَوَلَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّوْنَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(77)\nAWA LAA YA’LAMOONA ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA YOSIRROONA WA MAA YO’LENOON.\nWhat! know they not that God knoweth what they conceal and what they proclaim?\nوَ مِنْهُمْ اُمِّيُّوْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ الْكِتٰبَ اِلَّاۤ اَمَانِىَّ وَاِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا يَظُنُّوْنَ‏(78)\nWA MINHUM UMMIYYOONA LAA YA’LAMOONAL KETAABA ILLAA AMAANIYYA WA IN HUM ILLAA YAZUNNOON.\nAmong them are the unlettered folk who know not from the scripture except from hearsay; and they do nothing but conjecture\nفَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَكْتُبُوْنَ الْكِتٰبَ بِاَيْدِيْهِمْ ثُمَّ يَقُوْلُوْنَ هٰذَا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ لِيَشْتَرُوْا بِهٖ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا ؕ فَوَيْلٌ لَّهُمْ مِّمَّا كَتَبَتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَوَيْلٌ لَّهُمْ مِّمَّا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(79)\nFAWAILUL LIL-LAZEENA YAKTOBOONAL KETAABA BE-AYDEEHIM, SUMMA YAQOOLOONA HAAZAA MIN I’NDIL LAAHE LE-YASHTAROO BEHI SAMANAN QALEELAA, FA-WAYLUL LAHUM MIMMAA KATABAT AYDEEHIM WA WAYLUL LAHUM MIMMAA YAKSEBOON.\nThen woe unto them who write the book with their own hands and then say, “This is from God” for they may sell it for a small price; thus, woe unto for what their hands have written (edited) and Unto them for what they earn thereby\nوَقَالُوْا لَنْ تَمَسَّنَا النَّارُ اِلَّاۤ اَيَّامًا مَّعْدُوْدَةً  ؕ قُلْ اَتَّخَذْتُمْ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ عَهْدًا فَلَنْ يُّخْلِفَ اللّٰهُ عَهْدَهٗۤ اَمْ تَقُوْلُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(80)\nWA QAALOO LAN TAMASSANAN NAARO ILLAA AYYAAMAM MA’DOODAH, QUL ATTAKHAZTUM I’NDAL LAAHE A’HDAN FALAN-Y YUKHLEFAL LAAHO A’HDAHU AM TAQOOLOONA A’LAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nAnd they say, “The (Hell) Fire shall never touch but for a numbered day”; Say (O’ Muhammad!), “Have ye taken a promise from God, for He never breaketh His Promise? Or speak ye of God what ye know not?\nبَلٰى مَنْ كَسَبَ سَيِّئَةً وَّاَحَاطَتْ بِهٖ خَطِيْۤئَتُهٗ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(81)\nBALAA MAN KASABA SAYYE-ATANW WA AHAATAT BEHI KHATEEE-ATOHU FA-OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR, HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nYea! whosoever earneth evil and his sin encompasseth him; they are the fellows of the (Hell) Fire, therein shall they abide\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِ ۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(82)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUL JANNAH, HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nAnd (as for) those who believe (in God) and work righteousness, they are the inmates of the garden (and) therein shall they abide\nوَاِذْ اَخَذْنَا مِيْثَاقَ بَنِىْٓ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ لَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ اِلَّا اللّٰهَ وَبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ اِحْسَانًا وَّذِى الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَقُوْلُوْا لِلنَّاسِ حُسْنًا وَّاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ ؕ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّنْكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(83)\nWA IZ AKHAZNAA MEESAAQA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA LAA TA’BODOONA ILLAL LAAH, WA BIL-WAALEDAYNE EHSAANANW WA ZIL QURBAA WAL YATAAMAA WAL MASAAKEENE WA QOOLOO LIN-NAASE HUSNANW WA AQEEMUS SALAATA WA AATUZ ZAKAAH, SUMMA TAWALLAYTUM ILLAA QALEELAM MINKUM WA ANTUM MO’REZOON.\nAnd remember, when we made a covenant with the children of Isra’il (saying), “Ye shall not worship but God; and (shall do) good to parents and kindred and to the orphans and the needy and speak kindly to men and establish the prayer and pay the poor rate;” Then ye turn back save a few of you and (still) ye backslide\nوَاِذْ اَخَذْنَا مِيْثَاقَكُمْ لَا تَسْفِكُوْنَ دِمَآءَكُمْ وَلَا تُخْرِجُوْنَ اَنْفُسَكُمْ مِّنْ دِيَارِكُمْ ثُمَّ اَقْرَرْتُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ تَشْهَدُوْنَ‏(84)\nWA IZ AKHAZNAA MEESAAQAKUM LAA TASFEKOONA DEMAAA-AKUM WA LAA TUKHREJOONA ANFOSAKUM MIN DEYAAREKUM SUMMA AQRARTUM WA ANTUM TASH-HADOON.\nAnd remember, We made a Covenant with you, “Shed not your blood, nor turn your selves out of your dwellings;” And then (this) ye (solemnly) ratified while ye (yourselves) were witness (thereto)\nثُمَّ اَنْتُمْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ تَقْتُلُوْنَ اَنْفُسَكُمْ وَتُخْرِجُوْنَ فَرِيْقًا مِّنْكُمْ مِّنْ دِيَارِهِمْ تَظٰهَرُوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِالْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِؕ وَاِنْ يَّاْتُوْكُمْ اُسٰرٰى تُفٰدُوْهُمْ وَهُوَ مُحَرَّمٌ عَلَيْڪُمْ اِخْرَاجُهُمْؕ اَفَتُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِبَعْضِ الْكِتٰبِ وَتَكْفُرُوْنَ بِبَعْضٍۚ فَمَا جَزَآءُ مَنْ يَّفْعَلُ ذٰلِكَ مِنْكُمْ اِلَّا خِزْىٌ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۚ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ يُرَدُّوْنَ اِلٰٓى اَشَدِّ الْعَذَابِؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(85)\nSUMMA ANTUM HAAOOLAAA-E TAQTOLOONA ANFOSAFUM WA TUKHREJOONA FAREEQAM MINKUM MIN DEYAAREHIM, TAZAAHAROONA A’LAYHIM BIL-ISME WAL U’DWAAN, WA IN-Y YAATOOKUM OSAARAA TOFAADOOHUM WA HOWA MOHARRAMUM A’LAYKUM IKHRAAJOHUM, AFA-TOAMENOONA BE-BA’ZIL KETAABE WA TAKFOROONA BE-BA’Z, FAMAA JAZAAA-O MAN-Y YAF-A’LO ZAALEKA MINKUM ILLAA KHIZYUN FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA, WA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE YORADDOONA ELAA ASHADDDIL A’ZAAB, WA MAL LAAHO BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nYet after this ye are those who slay your selves and banish a party of you from their homes backing each other up against them by sin and transgression; and if they came to you as captives ye would ransom them, while their very banishment (by you) itself was Unlawful Do ye then believe in a part of the Book and reject ye the other? Then what shall be the return for those who do so save disgrace in the life of this world and on the Day of Judgment they shall be returned to the most grievous punishment; And God is not heedless of what ye do\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اشْتَرَوُا الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا بِالْاٰخِرَةِ فَلَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذَابُ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(86)\nOOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENASH TARAWUL HAYAATAD DUNYAA BIL-AAKHERAH, FALAA YOKHAFFAFO A’NHOMUL A’ZAABO WA LAA HUM YUNSAROON.\nThese are they who have bought the present life (of this world in exchange) for the life hereafter; so their punishment shall not be lightened nor shall they be helped\nوَ لَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ وَقَفَّيْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ بِالرُّسُلِ وَاٰتَيْنَا عِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ الْبَيِّنٰتِ وَاَيَّدْنٰهُ بِرُوْحِ الْقُدُسِؕ اَفَكُلَّمَا جَآءَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌۢ بِمَا لَا تَهْوٰٓى اَنْفُسُكُمُ اسْتَكْبَرْتُمْۚ فَفَرِيْقًا كَذَّبْتُمْ وَفَرِيْقًا تَقْتُلُوْنَ‏(87)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA WA QAFFAYNAA MIM BA’DEHI BIR-ROSOL, WA AATAYNAA E’ESAB NA MARYAMAL BAYYENAATE WA AYYADNAAHO BE-ROOHIL QODOS, AFAKULLAMAA JAAA-AKUM RASOOLUM BEMAA LAA TAHWAA ANFOSOKOMUS TAKBARTUM, FA-FAREEQAN KAZZABTUM, WA FAREEQAN TAQTOLOON.\nAnd most certainly We gave Moses the scripture and We caused him to be succeeded with apostles; We gave Jesus, the son of Mary, clear evidence and aided him with the Holy Spirit. What! (and yet) whenever (thereafter) an apostle came unto you with that which your selves desired not, swelled ye with pride, some (of the apostles) ye belied (as imposters) and some ye slew\nوَقَالُوْا قُلُوْبُنَا غُلْفٌؕ بَل لَّعَنَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِكُفْرِهِمْ فَقَلِيْلًا مَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(88)\nWA QAALOO QOLOOBONAA GHULF, BAL LA-A’NAHOMUL LAAHO BEKUFREHIM FA-QALEELAM MAA YOAMENOON.\nAnd they say, “Our hearts are covered” Nay! God hath cursed them for their disbelief; so little is that they believe\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ كِتٰبٌ مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ مُصَدِّقٌ لِّمَا مَعَهُمْۙ وَكَانُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ يَسْتَفْتِحُوْنَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا  ۖۚ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ مَّا عَرَفُوْا كَفَرُوْا بِهٖ فَلَعْنَةُ اللّٰهِ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(89)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-AHUM KETAABUM MIN I’NDIL LAAHE MOSADDEQUL LEMAA MA-A’HUM, WA KAANOO MIN QABLO YASTAFTEHOONA A’LAL LAZEENA KAFAROO, FALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM MAA A’RAFOO KAFAROO BEH, FA-LA’NATUL LAAHE A’LAL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd when there came unto them a Book from God confirming what is with them, although from before they had been praying for victory over those who disbelieved and when there came unto them that which they recognize (and yet) they disbelieved in it; Therefore, God’s curse is on the disbelievers\nبِئْسَمَا اشْتَرَوْا بِهٖۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ اَنْ يَّڪْفُرُوْا بِمَآ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ بَغْيًا اَنْ يُّنَزِّلَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖۚ فَبَآءُوْ بِغَضَبٍ عَلٰى غَضَبٍؕ وَلِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(90)\nBEASAMASH TARAW BEHI ANFOSAHUM AN-Y YAKFOROO BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO BAGHYAN AN-Y YONAZZELAL LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI A’LAA MAN-Y YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEH, FABAAA-OO BE-GHAZABIN A’LAA GHAZAB, WA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABUM MOHEEN.\nVile is it (the price) for which they have sold their souls that they deny the revelation from God, feeling offended and envy that God out of His Grace sendeth it to whomsoever of His servants He pleaseth. They have brought on themselves wrath upon wrath; And for the disbelievers there is the most disgracing punishment\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ اٰمِنُوْا بِمَآ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ قَالُوْا نُؤْمِنُ بِمَآ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنَا وَيَكْفُرُوْنَ بِمَا وَرَآءَهٗ وَهُوَ الْحَقُّ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا مَعَهُمْؕ قُلْ فَلِمَ تَقْتُلُوْنَ اَنْۢبِيَآءَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ قَبْلُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(91)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM AAMENOO BEMAA ANZALAL LAAHO QAALOO NOAMENO BEMAA UNZELA A’LAYNAA WA YAKFOROONA BEMAA WARAAA-AH, WA HOWAL HAQQO MOSADDEQAL LEMAA MA-A’HUM, QUL FALEMA TAQTOLOONA AMBEYAAA-AL LAAHE MIN QABLO IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nWhen it is said to them, “Believe in what God hath sent down,” they say, “We believe in that which was sent down unto us,” And they disbelieve in that which is besides (that) while it is the Truth confirming that which is with them; Say (unto them. O’ Our Apostle Muhammad), “Why then slew ye the apostles of God aforetime if ye did indeed believe?\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ مُّوْسٰى بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ثُمَّ اتَّخَذْتُمُ الْعِجْلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ وَاَنْتُمْ ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(92)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AKUM MOOSAA BIL-BAYYENAATE SUMMAT TAKHAZTOMUL I’JLA MIM BA’DEHI WA ANTUM ZAALEMOON.\nAnd verily Moses came unto you with clear evidences And yet after him (in his absence) ye took the calf (for your god) and ye did behave unjustly\nوَاِذْ اَخَذْنَا مِيْثَاقَكُمْ وَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَكُمُ الطُّوْرَ ؕ خُذُوْا مَآ اٰتَيْنٰكُمْ بِقُوَّةٍ وَّاسْمَعُوْا  ؕ قَالُوْا سَمِعْنَا وَعَصَيْنَا  وَاُشْرِبُوْا فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمُ الْعِجْلَ بِكُفْرِهِمْ ؕ قُلْ بِئْسَمَا يَاْمُرُكُمْ بِهٖۤ اِيْمَانُكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(93)\nWA IZ AKHAZNAA MEESAAQAKUM WA RA-FA’NAA FAWQAKOMUT TOOR, KHOZOO MAA AATAYNAAKUM BE-QUWWATINW WAS MA-O’O, QAALOO SAMEA’NAA WA A’SAYNAA, WA USHREBOO FEE QOLOOBEHEMUL I’JLA BE-KUFREHIM, QUL BEASAMAA YAAMOROKUM BEHI EEMAANOKUM IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nAnd remember when we made a covenant with you and raised the ‘Tur’ above you (saying), “Hold fast by that which We have given you and hearken ye (Our Word) said they, “We have hearkened and disobeyed”; They were made to imbibe (deep) (the love of) the calf into their hearts for their wrong belief; Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad), “Vile is that which your belief bideth you if ye be (true) believers\nقُلْ اِنْ كَانَتْ لَكُمُ الدَّارُ الْاٰخِرَةُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ خَالِصَةً مِّنْ دُوْنِ النَّاسِ فَتَمَنَّوُا الْمَوْتَ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(94)\nQUL IN KAANAT LAKOMUD DAARUL AAKHERATO I’NDAL LAAHE KHAALESATAM MIN DOONIN NAASE FATAMANNAWUL MAWTA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad), “if the (ultimate) abode with God in the hereafter be exclusively for you and not for others of mankind then invoke ye death (for you) if ye be truthful\nوَ لَنْ يَّتَمَنَّوْهُ اَبَدًاۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ اَيْدِيْهِمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(95)\nWA LAN-Y YATAMANNAWHO ABADAM BEMAA QADDAMAT AYDEEHIM, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUM BIZ-ZAALEMEEN.\nBut never will they invoke it because of that which their hands have sent forth before them! (But) Verily, God (well) knoweth the unjust\nوَلَتَجِدَنَّهُمْ اَحْرَصَ النَّاسِ عَلٰى حَيٰوةٍ  ۛۚ وَ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا  ۛۚ يَوَدُّ اَحَدُهُمْ لَوْ يُعَمَّرُ اَ لْفَ سَنَةٍ ۚ وَمَا هُوَ بِمُزَحْزِحِهٖ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ اَنْ يُّعَمَّرَؕ وَاللّٰهُ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ ‏(96)\nWA LA-TAJEDANNAHUM AHRASAN NAASE A’LAA HAYAAH, WA MENAL LAZEENA ASHRAKOO, YAWADDO AHADOHUM LAW YO-A’MMARO ALFA SANAH, WA MAA HOWA BE-MOZAHZEHEHI MENAL A’ZAABE AN-Y YO-A’MMAR, WAL LAAHO BASEERUM BEMAA YA’MALOON.\nAnd thou wilt surely find them greediest of mankind for life, and of the idolaters, each one of them is covetous to live (even) a thousand years, and yet his living a long life will in no way remove him further off from the wrath verily God seeth what they do\nقُلْ مَنْ كَانَ عَدُوًّا لِّجِبْرِيْلَ فَاِنَّهٗ نَزَّلَهٗ عَلٰى قَلْبِكَ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَهُدًى وَّبُشْرٰى لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(97)\nQUL MAN KAANA A’DUWWAL LE-JIBREELA FA-INNAHU NAZZALAHU A’LAA QALBEKA BE-IZNIL LAAHE MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE WA HODANW WA BUSHRAA LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) whoso is an enemy to Gabriel; for, verily it is he who hath brought it unto thy heart by God’s (command) confirming what had (already) been (revealed) before and guidance and glad tidings to the believers\nمَنْ كَانَ عَدُوًّا لِّلّٰهِ وَمَلٰٓئِكَتِهٖ وَ رُسُلِهٖ وَجِبْرِيْلَ وَمِيْكٰٮلَ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَدُوٌّ لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(98)\nMAN KAANA A’DUWWAL LILLAAHE WA MALAA-EKATEHI WA ROSOLEHI WA JIBREELA WA MEEKAALA FA-INNAL LAAHA A’DUWWUL LIL-KAAFEREEN.\nWhoso is an enemy to God and His angels and His apostles, and Gabriel and Michael, so verily God is an enemy to the disbelievers\nوَلَقَدْ اَنْزَلْنَآ اِلَيْكَ اٰيٰتٍۢ بَيِّنٰتٍۚ وَمَا يَكْفُرُ بِهَآ اِلَّا الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(99)\nWA LAQAD ANZALNAA ELAYKA AAYAATIM BAYYENAAT, WA MAA YAKFORO BEHAA ILLAL FAASEQOON.\nAnd verily We sent down, unto thee clear signs, but none disbelieveth in them but the perverse\nاَوَكُلَّمَا عٰهَدُوْا عَهْدًا نَّبَذَهٗ فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْهُمْؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(100)\nAWA KULLAMAA A’AHADOO A’HDAN NABAZAHU FAREEQUM MINHUM, BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YOAMENOON.\nAnd is it not (true) that every time they make a covenant, a party of them cast. it aside? Nay, most of them believe not\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ مُصَدِّقٌ لِّمَا مَعَهُمْ نَبَذَ فَرِيْقٌ مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَۙ كِتٰبَ اللّٰهِ وَرَآءَ ظُهُوْرِهِمْ كَاَنَّهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(101)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-AHUM RASOOLUM MIN I’NDIL LAAHE MOSADDEQUL LEMAA MA-A’HUM NABAZA FAREEQUM MENAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA, KETAABAL LAAHE WARAAA-A ZOHOOREHIM KA-ANNAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd when there came unto them an apostle from God confirming what was (already) with them, some of those to whom the scripture was given cast the Book of God behind their backs as if they knew (it) not\nوَاتَّبَعُوْا مَا تَتْلُوا الشَّيٰطِيْنُ عَلٰى مُلْكِ سُلَيْمٰنَۚ وَمَا كَفَرَ سُلَيْمٰنُ وَلٰكِنَّ الشَّيٰطِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُعَلِّمُوْنَ النَّاسَ السِّحْرَ وَمَآ اُنْزِلَ عَلَى الْمَلَكَيْنِ بِبَابِلَ هَارُوْتَ وَمَارُوْتَؕ وَمَا يُعَلِّمٰنِ مِنْ اَحَدٍ حَتّٰى يَقُوْلَاۤ اِنَّمَا نَحْنُ فِتْنَةٌ فَلَا تَكْفُرْؕ فَيَتَعَلَّمُوْنَ مِنْهُمَا مَا يُفَرِّقُوْنَ بِهٖ بَيْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَ زَوْجِهٖؕ وَمَا هُمْ بِضَآرِّيْنَ بِهٖ مِنْ اَحَدٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَيَتَعَلَّمُوْنَ مَا يَضُرُّهُمْ وَلَا يَنْفَعُهُمْؕ وَلَقَدْ عَلِمُوْا لَمَنِ اشْتَرٰٮهُ مَا لَهٗ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ مِنْ خَلَاقٍؕ وَلَبِئْسَ مَا شَرَوْا بِهٖۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْؕ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(102)\nWAT TABA-O’O MAA TATLUSH SHAYAATEENO A’LAA MULKE SOLAYMAAN, WA MAA KAFARA SOLAYMAANO WA LAAKINNASH SHAYAATEENA KAFAROO YO-A’LLEMOONAN NAASAS SEHR, WA MAA UNZELA A’LAL MALAKAYNE BE BAABELA HAAROOTA WA MAAROOT, WA MAA YO-A’LLEMAANE MIN AHADIN HATTAA YAQOOLAA INNAMAA NAHNO FITNATUN FALAA TAKFOR, FA-YATA-A’LLAMOONA MINHOMAA MAA YOFARREQOONA BEHI BAYNAL MAR-E WA ZAWJEH, WA MAA HUM BE-ZAAAR-REENA BEHI MIN AHADIN ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH, WA YATA-A’LLAMOONA MAA YAZURROHUM WA LAA YANFA-O’HUM, WA LAQAD A’LEMOO LAMANISH TARAAHO MAA LAHU FIL AAKHERATE MIN KHALAAQ, WA LABESA MAA SHARAW BEHI ANFOSAHUM, LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nThey followed what the devils reciteth (falsely) against Solomon’s kingdom; not that Solomon disbelieved but (it was) the devils that disbelieved; sorcery did they teach to men and what was revealed to the two angels at Babylon, Harut and Marut. Neither of these taught anyone without saying, “We are only a trial so disbelieve not (in the guidance of God); They learned from them that which sows discord between man and wife; but they could harm no one (thereby) but by God’s permission. And they learned what harmed them and profiteth them not; and indeed they knew that he who bought that (art) had not shared in the happiness of the hereafter. And vile was the price for which they did sell their selves, had they only known (it)\nوَلَوْ اَنَّهُمْ اٰمَنُوْا وَاتَّقَوْا لَمَثُوْبَةٌ مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ ؕ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(103)\nWA LAW ANNAHUM AAMANOO WAT TAQAW LA-MASOOBATUM MIN I’NDIL LAAHE KHAYR, LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nAnd had they believed (in God) and guarded themselves (against evil) verily their reward from God had been better; had they only known (it)\nيٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَقُوْلُوْا رَاعِنَا وَ قُوْلُوا انْظُرْنَا وَاسْمَعُوْا ؕ وَلِلْڪٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(104)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TAQOOLOO RAA-E’NAA WA QOOLUN ZURNAA WAS MA-O’O, WA LIL-KAAFEREENA A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nO’ye who believe, say not ‘Raina’ but say: ‘Unzurna’ and hearken; And there is for the disbelievers a grievous punishment\nمَا يَوَدُّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ وَلَا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ اَنْ يُّنَزَّلَ عَلَيْڪُمْ مِّنْ خَيْرٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَخْتَصُّ بِرَحْمَتِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(105)\nMAA YAWADDUL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN AHLIL KETAABE WA LAL MUSHREKEENA AN-Y YONAZZALA A’LAYKUM MIN KHAYRIM MIR RABBEKUM, WAL LAAHO YAKHTASSO BE-RAHMATEHI MAN-Y YASHAAA, WAL LAAHO ZUL FAZLIL A’ZEEM.\n(O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) Like not those who disbelieve among the people of the scripture nor the idolaters that anything good should be sent unto you from your Lord. But, God chooseth for His (exclusive) Mercy whomsoever He liketh, for God is (the Lord) of Mighty Grace\nمَا نَنْسَخْ مِنْ اٰيَةٍ اَوْ نُنْسِهَا نَاْتِ بِخَيْرٍ مِّنْهَآ اَوْ مِثْلِهَا ؕ اَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(106)\nMAA NANSAKH MIN AAYATIN AW NUNSEHAA NAATE BE-KHAYRIM MINHAA AW MISLEHAA, ALAM TA’LAM ANNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nWhatever We abrogate of a sign or We bypass it We bring (in its place) one better than it or its like; Knowest thou not that God over all things is Powerful!\nاَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(107)\nALAM TA’LAM ANNAL LAAHA LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MINW WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nKnowest thou not that unto God belongeth the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; and there is not for you, besides God, any guardian or a helper?\nاَمْ تُرِيْدُوْنَ اَنْ تَسْئَلُوْا رَسُوْلَكُمْ كَمَا سُئِلَ مُوْسٰى مِنْ قَبْلُؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَبَدَّلِ الْكُفْرَ بِالْاِيْمَانِ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ سَوَآءَ السَّبِيْلِ‏(108)\nAM TOREEDOONA AN TAS-ALOO RASOOLAKUM KAMAA SO-ELA MOOSAA MIN QABL, WA MAN-Y YATABADDALIL KUFRA BIL-EEMAANE FAQAD ZALLA SAWAAA-AS SABEEL.\nDo ye like to question your Apostle (Muhammad) as Moses was questioned aforetime? And he who exchangeth faith for infidelity verily he hath lost the right path\nوَدَّ كَثِيْرٌ مِّنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتٰبِ لَوْ يَرُدُّوْنَكُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ اِيْمَانِكُمْ كُفَّارًاۖۚ حَسَدًا مِّنْ عِنْدِ اَنْفُسِهِمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الْحَقُّ ۚ فَاعْفُوْا وَاصْفَحُوْا حَتّٰى يَاْتِىَ اللّٰهُ بِاَمْرِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(109)\nWADDA KASEERUM MIN AHLIL KETAABE LAW YARUDDOONAKUM MIM BA’DE EEMAANEKUM KUFFAARAA, HASADAM MIN I’NDE ANFOSEHIM MIM BA’DE MAA TABAYYANA LAHOMUL HAQ, FA’FOO WAS FAHOO HATTAA YAATEYAL LAAHO BE-AMREH, INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nMany of the people of the scripture wish to turn you back to infidelity after ye had believed, out of selfish envy on their part after the Truth had been manifested unto them; But forgive ye and overlook ye till God bringeth about His command; Verily God is over all things Powerful\nوَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ  ؕ وَمَا تُقَدِّمُوْا لِاَنْفُسِكُمْ مِّنْ خَيْرٍ تَجِدُوْهُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(110)\nWA AQEEMUS SALAATA WA AATUZ ZAKAAH, WA MAA TOQADDEMOO LE-ANFOSEKUM MIN KHAYRIN TAJEDOOHO I’NDAL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA BEMAA TA’MALOONA BASEER.\nEstablish ye prayer and give ye the poor rate and whatever of good ye send forth before (you) for yourselves, that shall ye find with God; verily God Seeth what all ye do\nوَقَالُوْا لَنْ يَّدْخُلَ الْجَنَّةَ اِلَّا مَنْ كَانَ هُوْدًا اَوْ نَصٰرٰىؕ تِلْكَ اَمَانِيُّهُمْؕ قُلْ هَاتُوْا بُرْهَانَكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(111)\nWA QAALOO LAN-Y YADKHOLAL JANNATA ILLAA MAN KAANA HOODAN AW NASAARAA, TILKA AMAANIYYOHUM, QUL HAATOO BURHAANAKUM IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd they say, none shall enter Paradise except he be a Jew or a Christian; these are their vain wishes Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad), “bring ye your proof if ye be truthful\nبَلٰى مَنْ اَسْلَمَ وَجْهَهٗ لِلّٰهِ وَهُوَ مُحْسِنٌ فَلَهٗۤ اَجْرُهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ وَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(112)\nBALAA, MAN ASLAMA WAJHAHU LIL-LAAH WA HOWA MOHSENUN FALAHU AJROHU I’NDA RABBEH, WA LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM YAHZANOON.\nYea! whosoever Submitteth his self (entirely) to God and is a doer of good for him there shall be his reward with his Lord, on such shall be no fear, nor shall they grieve\nوَقَالَتِ الْيَهُوْدُ لَيْسَتِ النَّصٰرٰى عَلٰى شَىْءٍ وَّقَالَتِ النَّصٰرٰى لَيْسَتِ الْيَهُوْدُ عَلٰى شَىْءٍۙ وَّهُمْ يَتْلُوْنَ الْكِتٰبَؕ كَذٰلِكَ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ مِثْلَ قَوْلِهِمْۚ فَاللّٰهُ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(113)\nWA QAALATIL YAHOODO LAYSATIN NASAARAA A’LAA SHAYINW, WA QAALATIN NASAARAA LAYSATIL YAHOODO A’LAA SHAYINW, WA HUM YATLOONAL KETAAB, KAZAALEKA QAALAL LAZEENA LAA YA’LAMOONA MISLA QAWLEHIM, FAL-LAAHO YAHKOMO BAYNAHUM YAWMAL QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nThe Jews say the Christians rest on naught; the Christians say the Jews rest on naught; yet they (both) read the (same) Book; Even so like their sayings speak those who know not. God will judge between them on the Day of Judgment in what they differ\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ مَّنَعَ مَسٰجِدَ اللّٰهِ اَنْ يُّذْكَرَ فِيْهَا اسْمُهٗ وَسَعٰى فِىْ خَرَابِهَا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ مَا كَانَ لَهُمْ اَنْ يَّدْخُلُوْهَآ اِلَّا خَآئِفِيْنَ ؕ لَهُمْ فِى الدُّنْيَا خِزْىٌ وَّلَهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(114)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMAM MANA-A’ MASAAJEDAL LAAHE AN-Y YUZKARA FEEHAS MOH WA SA-A’A FEE KHARAABEHAA, OOLAAAA-EKA MAA KAANA LAHUM AN-Y YADKHOLOOHAA ILLAA KHAAA-EFEEN, LAHUM FID DUNYAA KHIZYUNW WA LAHUM FIL AAKHERATE A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nAnd who is more unjust than he who preventeth the Mosques of God of His name being remembered therein and striveth to ruin them? It is not (fit) for such (men) to enter them but in fear; for them is disgrace in this world and a great punishment in the hereafter\nوَلِلّٰهِ الْمَشْرِقُ وَالْمَغْرِبُ فَاَيْنَمَا تُوَلُّوْا فَثَمَّ وَجْهُ اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(115)\nWA LIL-LAAHIL MASHREQO WAL MAGHREB, FA-AYNAMAA TOWALLOO FA-SAMMA WAJHUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA WAASE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAinama tuwallu fathamma waju Allah’ “…Whichever direction ye turn, ye shall find only His face [His Manifestation]\nوَقَالُوا اتَّخَذَ اللّٰهُ وَلَدًا ۙ سُبْحٰنَهٗ ؕ بَل لَّهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ كُلٌّ لَّهٗ قَانِتُوْنَ‏(116)\nWA QAALUT TAKHAZAL LAAHO WALADAN, SUBHAANAH, BAL LAHU MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, KULLUL LAHU QAANETOON.\nAnd they say God hath taken unto Him a son, glory be to Him, Nay! His is all that is in the heavens and the earth; Him (alone) everything Obeyeth (Supplicantly)\nبَدِيْعُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ وَ اِذَا قَضٰٓى اَمْرًا فَاِنَّمَا يَقُوْلُ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ‏(117)\nBADEE-U’S SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, WA EZAA QAZAA AMRAN FA-INNAMAA YAQOOLO LAHU KUN FAYAKUN.\nThe (Wonderful’) Originator of the heavens and the earth (from nought) (is He) and when He decreeth an affair He only sayeth to it “BE” and it “IS\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ لَوْلَا يُكَلِّمُنَا اللّٰهُ اَوْ تَاْتِيْنَآ اٰيَةٌ  ؕ كَذٰلِكَ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّثْلَ قَوْلِهِمْؕ تَشَابَهَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْؕ قَدْ بَيَّنَّا الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يُّوْقِنُوْنَ‏(118)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA LAA YA’LAMOONA LAW LAA YOKALLEMONAL LAAHO AW TAA-TEENAA AAYAH, KAZAALEKA QAALAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM MISLA QAWLEHIM, TASHAABAHAT QOLOOBOHUM, QAD BAYYANNAL AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YOOQENOON.\nAnd say those (pagans) who know not: “Why speaketh not God unto us or why cometh not unto us a sign;” Even so spake those before them; Their hearts are alike; We have indeed made clear the signs to people who are certainly sure\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ بِالْحَقِّ بَشِيْرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا ۙ وَّلَا تُسْئَلُ عَنْ اَصْحٰبِ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(119)\nINNAA ARSALNAAKA BIL-HAQQE BASHEERANW WA NAZEERANW, WA LAA TUS-ALO A’N ASHAABIL JAHEEM.\nVerily We have sent thee with the Truth, a Bearer of glad tidings and a Warner and thou shalt not be questioned as to the companions of the blazing Hell (Fire)\nوَلَنْ تَرْضٰى عَنْكَ الْيَهُوْدُ وَلَا النَّصٰرٰى حَتّٰى تَتَّبِعَ مِلَّتَهُمْؕ قُلْ اِنَّ هُدَى اللّٰهِ هُوَ الْهُدٰىؕ وَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ بَعْدَ الَّذِىْ جَآءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِۙ مَا لَكَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍؔ‏(120)\nWA LAN TARZAA A’NKAL YAHOODO WA LAN NASAARAA HATTAA TATTABE-A’ MILLATAHUM, QUL INNA HODAL LAAHE HOWAL HODAA, WA LA-ENIT TABA’TA AHWAAA-AHUM BA’DAL LAZEE JAAA-AKA MENAL I’LME, MAA LAKA MENAL LAAHE MINW WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nAnd never will the Jews be pleased with thee nor the Christians until thou followeth their creed; Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad), “verily the guidance from God is the (true) guidance”; And verily if thou followeth their whims after the knowledge which hath come unto thee, then wouldst thou have from God neither a protector nor a helper\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يَتْلُوْنَهٗ حَقَّ تِلَاوَتِهٖؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِهٖ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(121)\nAL-LAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YATLOONAHU HAQQA TELAAWATEH, OOLAAA-EKA YOAMENOONA BEH, WA MAN-Y YAKFUR BEHI FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nThose unto whom We have given the Book, who read it as it should be read; it is they who believe therein; and those who disbelieve in it, those are they who are the losers\nيٰبَنِىْٓ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتِىَ الَّتِىْٓ اَنْعَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَاَنِّىْ فَضَّلْتُكُمْ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(122)\nYAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ KOROO NE’MATEYAL LATEE AN-A’MTO A’LAYKUM WA ANNEE FAZZALTOKUM A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nO’ children of Isra’il! Remember the bounties which I bestowed upon you and that I have given you preference over the people of the world\nوَاتَّقُوْا يَوْمًا لَّا تَجْزِىْ نَفْسٌ عَنْ نَّفْسٍ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يُقْبَلُ مِنْهَا عَدْلٌ وَّلَا تَنْفَعُهَا شَفَاعَةٌ وَّلَا هُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(123)\nWAT TAQOO YAWMAL LAA TAJZEE NAFSUN A’N NAFSIN SHAY-ANW WA LAA YUQBALO MINHAA A’DLUNW WA LAA TANFA-O’HAA SHAFAA-A’TUNW WA LAA HUM YUNSAROON.\nAnd guard (yourselves) against the day when no soul will in aught avail another, neither from it any compensation be accepted nor intercession profit it, nor shall they be helped\nوَاِذِ ابْتَلٰٓى اِبْرٰهٖمَ رَبُّهٗ بِكَلِمٰتٍ فَاَتَمَّهُنَّ ؕ قَالَ اِنِّىْ جَاعِلُكَ لِلنَّاسِ اِمَامًا ؕ قَالَ وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِىْ ؕ قَالَ لَا يَنَالُ عَهْدِى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(124)\nWA EZIB TALAA IBRAAHEEMA RABBOHU BEKALEMAATIN FA-ATAMMAHUN, QAALA INNEE JAA-E’LOKA LIN-NAASE EMAAMAA, QAALA WA MIN ZURRIYYATEE, QAALA LAA YANAALO A’HDIZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd remember when his Lord tried Abraham with certain words then he fulfilled them; He said, “Verily I make thee Imam for mankind; ‘(Abraham) said “And of my offspring”? He said: “My covenant reacheth not the unjust\nوَاِذْ جَعَلْنَا الْبَيْتَ مَثَابَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَاَمْنًا ؕ وَاتَّخِذُوْا مِنْ مَّقَامِ اِبْرٰهٖمَ مُصَلًّى ؕ وَعَهِدْنَآ اِلٰٓى اِبْرٰهٖمَ وَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ اَنْ طَهِّرَا بَيْتِىَ لِلطَّآئِفِيْنَ وَالْعٰكِفِيْنَ وَالرُّكَّعِ السُّجُوْدِ‏(125)\nWA IZ JA-A’LNAL BAYTA MASAABATAL LIN-NAASE WA AMNAA, WAT TAKHAZOO MIM MAQAAME IBRAAHEEMA MOSALLAA, WA A’HIDNAA ELAA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAA-E’ELA AN TAHHERA BAYTEYA LIT-TAAA-EFEENA WAL A’AKEFEENA WAR RUKKA-I’S SOJOOD.\nAnd remember when we made the House a resort for mankind and a Sanctuary (saying), ‘Take ye the station of Abraham a place of prayer (for you)’, and covenanted with Abraham and Ishmael (saying) ‘purify ye two My House for those who make circuit, and for those who abide in it and pay devotion and for those who bow down, and for those who prostrate (adoring)\nوَاِذْ قَالَ اِبْرٰهٖمُ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ هٰذَا بَلَدًا اٰمِنًا وَّارْزُقْ اَهْلَهٗ مِنَ الثَّمَرٰتِ مَنْ اٰمَنَ مِنْهُمْ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِؕ قَالَ وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَاُمَتِّعُهٗ قَلِيْلًا ثُمَّ اَضْطَرُّهٗۤ اِلٰى عَذَابِ النَّارِؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏‏(126)\nWA IZ QAALA IBRAAHEEMO RABBIJ A’L HAAZAA BALADAN AAMENANW WAR ZUQ AHLAHU MENAS SAMARAATE MAN AAMANA MINHUM BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHER, QAALA WA MAN KAFARA FA-OMATTE-O’HU QALEELAN SUMMA AZTARROHU ELAA A’ZAABIN NAAR, WA BEASAL MASEER.\nAnd remember when Abraham said, “My Lord! make this a city (a place) of security and provide the dwellers therein with fruits such of them as believe in God and the Last Day;” He said, “Yea! such as who disbelieveth, I will grant him enjoyment for a short while but soon drive him to the doom of fire and an evil destination it is\nوَاِذْ يَرْفَعُ اِبْرٰهٖمُ الْقَوَاعِدَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ وَاِسْمٰعِيْلُؕ رَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(127)\nWA IZ YARFA-O’ IBRAAHEEMUL QAWAA-E’DA MENAL BAYTE WA ISMAA-E’EL, RABBANAA TAQABBAL MINNAA, INNAKA ANTAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nAnd remember when Abraham raised the foundations of the House with Ishmael, (praying) “Our Lord! accept (this service) from us; Verily Thou and Thou (alone) art the All-Hearing and All-Knowing\nرَبَّنَا وَاجْعَلْنَا مُسْلِمَيْنِ لَكَ وَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِنَآ اُمَّةً مُّسْلِمَةً لَّكَ وَاَرِنَا مَنَاسِكَنَا وَتُبْ عَلَيْنَا ۚ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(128)\nRABBANAA WAJ A’LNAA MUSLEMAYNE LAKA WA MIN ZURRIYYATENAA UMMATAM MUSLEMATAL LAK, WA ARENAA MANAASEKANAA WA TUB A’LAYNAA, INNAKA ANTAT TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\nOur Lord! Make us (two) Mus1ims submitting (only) to Thee and of our progeny (make) a group submissive (only) to Thee And show us the ways of Devotion and turn to us (mercifully) for verily Thou and Thou (alone) art the Oft - Returning, the Most Merciful\nرَبَّنَا وَابْعَثْ فِيْهِمْ رَسُوْلًا مِّنْهُمْ يَتْلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِكَ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَ يُزَكِّيْهِمْؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(129)\nRABBANAA WAB A’S FEEHIM RASOOLAM MINHUM YATLOO A’LAYHIM AAYAATEKA WA YO-A’LLEMOHOMUL KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WA YOZAKKEEHIM, INNAKA ANTAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nOur Lord! raise up amongst them an apostle from them, who shall recite unto them Thy revelations and teach them the Book and Wisdom and purify them for Thou and Thou (alone) art the Mighty, the Wise\nوَمَنْ يَّرْغَبُ عَنْ مِّلَّةِ اِبْرٰهٖمَ اِلَّا مَنْ سَفِهَ نَفْسَهٗ ؕ وَلَقَدِ اصْطَفَيْنٰهُ فِى الدُّنْيَا ۚ وَاِنَّهٗ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ لَمِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(130)\nWA MAN-Y YARGHABO A’M MILLATE IBRAAHEEMA ILLAA MAN SAFEHA NAFSAH, WA LAQADIS TAFAYNAAHO FID DUNYAA, WA INNAHU FIL AAKHERTAE LAMENAS SAALEHEEN.\nAnd who turneth away from the creed of Abraham but (one) who debaseth his self; And indeed We have chosen him in this world; and verily in the hereafter he is of the righteous ones\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهٗ رَبُّهٗۤ اَسْلِمْۙ قَالَ اَسْلَمْتُ لِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(131)\nIZ QAALA LAHU RABBOHU ASLIM, QAALA ASLAMTO LE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd remember when his Lord said unto him, “Surrender (thyself to me)” he said, “I have surrendered (myself) to the Lord of the worlds\nوَوَصّٰى بِهَآ اِبْرٰهٖمُ بَنِيْهِ وَ يَعْقُوْبُؕ يٰبَنِىَّ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ اصْطَفٰى لَكُمُ الدِّيْنَ فَلَا تَمُوْتُنَّ اِلَّا وَاَنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَؕ‏‏(132)\nWA WASSAA BEHAA IBRAAHEEMO BANEEHE WA YA’QOOB, YAA BANIYYA INNAL LAAHAS TAFAA LAKOMUD DEENA FALAA TAMOOTUNNA ILLAA WA ANTUM MUSLEMOON.\nAnd this did Abraham bequeath to his sons and so (did) Jacob; (Saying), “O my sons! verily God hath chosen for you the religion (Islam) Therefore, ye die not but as ‘Muslims\nاَمْ كُنْتُمْ شُهَدَآءَ اِذْ حَضَرَ يَعْقُوْبَ الْمَوْتُۙ اِذْ قَالَ لِبَنِيْهِ مَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِىْؕ قَالُوْا نَعْبُدُ اِلٰهَكَ وَاِلٰهَ اٰبَآئِكَ اِبْرٰهٖمَ وَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِسْحٰقَ اِلٰهًا وَّاحِدًاۖۚ وَّنَحْنُ لَهٗ مُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(133)\nAM KUNTUM SHOHADAAA-A IZ HAZARA YA’QOOBAL MAWTO, IZ QAALA LE-BANEEHE MAA TA’BODOONA MIM BA’DEE, QAALOO NA’BODO ELAAHAKA WA ELAAHA AABAAA-EKA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAAA-E’ELA WA ISHAAQA ELAAHANW WAAHEDANW, WA NAHNO LAHU MUSLEMOON.\nWere ye witnesses when death approached Jacob? When he said unto his sons, “what will ye worship after me?” They said, “We will worship thy God and the God of thy fathers, Abraham and Ishmael and Isaac, One God (alone) and (only) to Him do we submit\nتِلْكَ اُمَّةٌ قَدْ خَلَتْۚ لَهَا مَا كَسَبَتْ وَلَكُمْ مَّا كَسَبْتُمْۚ وَلَا تُسْئَلُوْنَ عَمَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(134)\nTILKA UMMATUN QAD KHALAT, LAHAA MAA KASABAT WA LAKUM MAA KASABTUM, WA LAA TUS-ALOONA A’MMAA KAANOO YA’-MALOON.\nThis is a group that hath passed away; for them is the reward which they (have) earned and ye shall have that which ye (have) earned and ye shall not be questioned for what they had been doing\nوَقَالُوْا كُوْنُوْا هُوْدًا اَوْ نَصٰرٰى تَهْتَدُوْا ؕ قُلْ بَلْ مِلَّةَ اِبْرٰهٖمَ حَنِيْفًا ؕ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(135)\nWA QAALOO KOONOO HOODAN AW NASAARAA TAHTADOO, QUL BAL MILLATA IBRAAHEEMA HANEEFAA, WA MAA KAANA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nThey say, “Be ye Jews or Christians (so that) ye shall be (rightly) guided” Say (thou O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Nay! but the creed of Abraham, the upright one; and he was not of those who associate others with God\nقُوْلُوْٓا اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ وَمَآ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْنَا وَمَآ اُنْزِلَ اِلٰٓى اِبْرٰهٖمَ وَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ وَ الْاَسْبَاطِ وَمَآ اُوْتِىَ مُوْسٰى وَعِيْسٰى وَمَآ اُوْتِىَ النَّبِيُّوْنَ مِنْ رَّبِّهِمْۚ لَا نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ اَحَدٍ مِّنْهُمْ وَنَحْنُ لَهٗ مُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(136)\nQOOLOO AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WA MAA UNZELA ELAYNAA WA MAA UNZELA ELAA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAA-E’ELA WA ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA WAL ASBAATE WA MAA OOTEYA MOOSAA WA E’ESAA WA MAA OOTEYAN NABIYYOONA MIR RABBEHIM, LAA NOFARREQO BAYNA AHADIM MINHUM, WA NAHNO LAHU MUSLEMOON.\nSay ye (O’ Muslims!): We believe in God and that which hath been sent down unto us and that which was sent down unto Abraham and Ishmael and Isaac and Jacob and the tribes and which was given unto Moses and Jesus and that which was given unto the apostles from their Lord. No difference do we make between any of them and to Him (alone) have we submitted (ourselves’)\nفَاِنْ اٰمَنُوْا بِمِثْلِ مَآ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِهٖ فَقَدِ اهْتَدَوْا ۚ وَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنَّمَا هُمْ فِىْ شِقَاقٍ ۚ فَسَيَكْفِيْكَهُمُ اللّٰهُ ۚ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُؕ‏(137)\nFAIN AAMANOO BE-MISLE MAA AAMANTUM BEHI FAQADEH TADAW, WA IN TAWALLAW FA-INNAMAA HUM FEE SHEQAAQ, FASAYAKFEEKAHOMUL LAAH, WA HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nSo if they believe as ye believe they are indeed (rightly) guided but if they turn away, it is they who are in schism; then God will suffice thee against them, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing\nصِبْغَةَ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَمَنْ اَحْسَنُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ صِبْغَةً  وَّنَحْنُ لَهٗ عٰبِدُوْنَ‏(138)\nSIBGHATAL LAAH, WA MAN AHSANO MENAL LAAHE SIBGHATANW, WA NAHNO LAHU A’ABEDOON.\n(This is) God’s Colouring and who is better than God in Colouring; while Him (alone) do we worship\nقُلْ اَ تُحَآجُّوْنَنَا فِى اللّٰهِ وَهُوَ رَبُّنَا وَرَبُّكُمْۚ وَلَنَآ اَعْمَالُنَا وَلَكُمْ اَعْمَالُكُمْۚ وَنَحْنُ لَهٗ مُخْلِصُوْنَۙ‏(139)\nQUL A-TOHAAAJ-JOONANAA FIL LAAHE WA HOWA RABBONAA WA RABBOKUM, WA LANAA A-A’MAALONAA WA LAKUM A-A’MAALOKUM, WA NAHNO LAHU MUKHLESOONA.\nSay thou (unto the people of the Book), “Dispute ye with us about God; whereas He is our Lord and your Lord, and for us are our deeds and for you are your deeds; to Him (alone) we are (exclusively) loyal?\nاَمْ تَقُوْلُوْنَ اِنَّ اِبْرٰهٖمَ وَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَاِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ وَالْاَسْبَاطَ كَانُوْا هُوْدًا اَوْ نَصٰرٰىؕ قُلْ ءَاَنْتُمْ اَعْلَمُ اَمِ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ كَتَمَ شَهَادَةً عِنْدَهٗ مِنَ اللّٰهِؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(140)\nAM TAQOOLOONA INNA IBRAAHEEMA WA ISMAA-E’ELA WA ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA WAL ASBAATA KAANOO HOODAN AW NASAARAA, QUL A-ANTUM A-A’LAMO AMIL LAAH, WA MAN AZLAMO MIMMAN KATAMA SHA-HAADATAN I’NDAHU MENAL LAAH, WA MAL LAAHO BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nOr do ye say that Abraham, Ishmael, Isaac, Jacob and the Tribes were Jews or Christians? Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!), “Do ye know better or God (knoweth it)? Who is more unjust than those who conceal the testimony they have from God? And God is not heedless of what ye do\nتِلْكَ اُمَّةٌ قَدْ خَلَتْۚ لَهَا مَا كَسَبَتْ وَلَكُمْ مَّا كَسَبْتُمْۚ وَلَا تُسْئَلُوْنَ عَمَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(141)\nTILKA UMMATUN QAD KHALAT, LAHAA MAA KASABAT WA LAKUM MAA KASABTUM, WA LAA TUS-ALOONA A’MMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThose are a group(a) that hath passed away, for them (shall be) that which they (have) earned and for you (shall be) what ye earn and ye will not be questioned about what they had been doing\nسَيَقُوْلُ السُّفَهَآءُ مِنَ النَّاسِ مَا وَلّٰٮهُمْ عَنْ قِبْلَتِهِمُ الَّتِىْ كَانُوْا عَلَيْهَا ؕ قُل لِّلّٰهِ الْمَشْرِقُ وَالْمَغْرِبُ ؕ يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ اِلٰى صِراطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(142)\nSAYAQOOLUS SOFA-HAAA-O MENAN NAASE MAA WALLAHUM A’N QIBLATEHEMUL LATEE KAANOO A’LAYHAA, QUL LIL-LAAHIL MASHREQO WAL MAGHREB, YAHDEE MAN-Y YASHAAA-O ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nThe fools among men will say, “What hath turned them from their Qiblah towards which they were at (here before), “Say (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!), God’s is the East and the West, He guideth whomsoever He pleaseth to the Right path\nوَكَذٰلِكَ جَعَلْنٰكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّسَطًا لِّتَكُوْنُوْا شُهَدَآءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُوْنَ الرَّسُوْلُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيْدًا ؕ وَمَا جَعَلْنَا الْقِبْلَةَ الَّتِىْ كُنْتَ عَلَيْهَآ اِلَّا لِنَعْلَمَ مَنْ يَّتَّبِعُ الرَّسُوْلَ مِمَّنْ يَّنْقَلِبُ عَلٰى عَقِبَيْهِ ؕ وَاِنْ كَانَتْ لَكَبِيْرَةً اِلَّا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ هَدَى اللّٰهُ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيُضِيْعَ اِيْمَانَكُمْ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِالنَّاسِ لَرَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(143)\nWA KAZAALEKA JA-A’LNAAKUM UMMATANW WASATAL LE-TAKOONOO SHOHADAAA-A A’LAN NAASE WA YAKOONAR RASOOLO A’LAYKUM SHAHEEDA, WA MAA JA-A’LNAL QIBLATAL LATEE KUNTA A’LAYHAA ILLAA LE-NA’LAMA MAN-Y YATTABE-U’R RASOOLA MIMMAN-Y YANQALEBO A’LAA A’QEBAYH, WA IN KAANAT LAKABEERATAN ILLAA A’LAL LAZEENA HADAL LAAH, WA MAA KAANAL LAAHO LE-YOZEE-A’ EEMAANAKUM, INNAL LAAHA BIN-NAASE LA-RAOOFUR RAHEEM.\nAnd thus, have We made you a group of middling stand that ye may be witnesses over mankind and the Prophet be witness over you; And we did not fix the ‘Qiblah’ towards which thou wert at, but that We might distinguish him who followeth the Prophet, from him that turneth back upon his heels; and this was surely a hard thing for any except for those whom God hath guided. And God would not make futile your faith (in Him); verily God unto mankind is Affectionate (and) Merciful\nقَدْ نَرٰى تَقَلُّبَ وَجْهِكَ فِى السَّمَآءِۚ فَلَنُوَلِّيَنَّكَ قِبْلَةً تَرْضٰٮهَا فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِؕ وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنْتُمْ فَوَلُّوْا وُجُوْهَكُمْ شَطْرَهٗ ؕ وَاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ لَيَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّهِمْؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(144)\nQAD NARAA TAQALLOBA WAJHEKA FIS SAMAAA, FALANOWALLEYANNAKA QIBLATAN TARZAAHAA, FAWALLE WAJHAKA SHATRAL MASJEDIL HARAAM, WA HAYSO MAA KUNTUM FAWALLOO WOJOOHAKUM SHATRAH, WA INNAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA LA-YA’LAMOONA ANNAHUL HAQQO MIR RABBEHIM, WA MAL LAAHO BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA YA’MALOON.\nVerily We see the turning of thy face in heaven so We shall turn thee (in prayer) towards a ‘Qiblah’ thou shalt be pleased with. Turn then thy face towards the Sacred Mosque; and whenever ye be (in prayers) turn ye your faces towards it; verily those who have been given the Book know it is the Truth from their Lord; and God is not heedless of what they do\nوَلَئِنْ اَ تَيْتَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْكِتٰبَ بِكُلِّ اٰيَةٍ مَّا تَبِعُوْا قِبْلَتَكَۚ وَمَآ اَنْتَ بِتَابِعٍ قِبْلَتَهُمْۚ وَمَا بَعْضُهُمْ بِتَابِعٍ قِبْلَةَ بَعْضٍؕ وَلَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتَ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَكَ مِنَ الْعِلْمِۙ اِنَّكَ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۘ‏(145)\nWA LA-IN ATAYTAL LAZEENA OOTUL KETAABA BE-KULLE AAYATIM MAA TABE-O’O QIBLATAK, WA MAA ANTA BE-TAA-BE-I’N QIBLATAHUM, WA MAA BA’ZOHUM BE-TAABE-I’N QIBLATA BA’Z, WA LA-ENIT TABA’TA AHWAAA-AHUM MIM BA’DE MAA JAAA-AKA MENAL I’LME, INNAKA EZAL LAMENAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd even if thou wert to bring unto those who have been given the Scripture, every sign yet they would follow not thy ‘Qiblah’, neither thou art the follower of their ‘‘Qiblah’; nor will some of them follow the ‘Qiblah of others; And if thou wert to follow their inclinations after the knowledge that hath come unto thee, then thou surely wouldst be of the unjust ones\nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يَعْرِفُوْنَهٗ كَمَا يَعْرِفُوْنَ اَبْنَآءَهُمْؕ وَاِنَّ فَرِيْقًا مِّنْهُمْ لَيَكْتُمُوْنَ الْحَقَّ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَؔ‏(146)\nALLAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YA’REFOONAHU KAMAA YA’REFOONA ABNAAA-AHUM, WA INNA FAREEQAM MINHUM LA-YAKTOMOONAL HAQQA WA HUM YA’LAMOON.\nThose unto whom We have given the Scripture recognise him (even) as they recognise their own children; but verily some of them do conceal the truth though they know it\nاَلْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِيْنَ‏(147)\nAL-HAQQO MIR RABBEKA FALAA FAKOONANNA MENAL MUMTAREEN.\nIt is the Truth from thy Lord so be thou not of those who doubt\nوَلِكُلٍّ وِّجْهَةٌ هُوَ مُوَلِّيْهَا ۚ فَاسْتَبِقُوا الْخَيْرٰتِؕؔ اَيْنَ مَا تَكُوْنُوْا يَاْتِ بِكُمُ اللّٰهُ جَمِيْعًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(148)\nWA LE-KULLINW WIJHATUN HOWA MOWALLEEHAA FAS-TABEQUL KHAYRAAT, AYNA MAA TAKOONOO YAATE BEKOMUL LAAHO JAMEE-A’A, INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nAnd for everyone is a direction to which He turneth. Hasten then to precede each other in everything good; Wherever ye (may) be, God will bring ye together (unto Him), for verily God hath power over all things\nوَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِؕ وَاِنَّهٗ لَلْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(149)\nWA MIN HAYSO KHARAJTA FAWALLE WAJHAKA SHATRAL MASJEDIL HARAAM, WA INNAHU LAL-HAQQO MIR RABBEK, WA MAL LAAHO BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nAnd from whencesoever thou goest forth, turn thou thy face (while in prayer) towards the Sacred Mosque. And verily that is the truth from thy Lord; And God is not heedless of what ye do\nوَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِؕ وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنْتُمْ فَوَلُّوْا وُجُوْهَڪُمْ شَطْرَهٗ ۙ لِئَلَّا يَكُوْنَ لِلنَّاسِ عَلَيْكُمْ حُجَّةٌ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْهُمْ فَلَا تَخْشَوْهُمْ وَاخْشَوْنِىْ وَلِاُتِمَّ نِعْمَتِىْ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُوْنَ ۙۛ‏(150)\nWA MIN HAYSO KHARAJTA FAWALLE WAJHAKA SHATRAL MASJEDIL HARAAM, WA HAYSO MAA KUNTUM FAWALLOO WOJOOHAKUM SHATRAHU, LE-ALLAA YAKOONA LIN-NAASE A’LAYKUM HUJJATUN, ILLAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO MINHUM, FALAA TAKHSHAWHUM WAKH SHAWNEE, WA LE-OTIMMA NE’MATEE A’LAYKUM WA LA-A’LLAKUM TAHTADOON.\nSo from whencesoever thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) goeth forth, turn thou thy face towards the Sacred Mosque; and wherever ye (O’ Muslims) are, turn ye (too) your faces thither than men may have no plea against you save those of them that are unjust; So fear not them but fear Me! And that I may perfect My bounties on you, and that ye may be guided aright\nكَمَآ اَرْسَلْنَا فِيْكُمْ رَسُوْلًا مِّنْكُمْ يَتْلُوْا عَلَيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِنَا وَيُزَكِّيْكُمْ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمْ مَّا لَمْ تَكُوْنُوْا تَعْلَمُوْنَ ؕۛ‏(151)\nKAMAA ARSALNAA FEEKUM RASOOLAM MINKUM YATLOO A’LAYKUM AAYAATENAA WA YOZAKKEEKUM WA YO-A’LLEMOKOMUL KETAABA WAL HIKMATA WA YO-A’LLEMOKUM MAA LAM TAKOONOO TA’LAMOON.\nEven as We have sent among you a Prophet from amongst yourselves who reciteth unto you Our signs and purifieth you and teacheth you the Book and the Wisdom; and teacheth Qur’an you that which ye did not know\nفَاذْكُرُوْنِىْٓ اَذْكُرْكُمْ وَاشْكُرُوْا لِىْ وَلَا تَكْفُرُوْنِ‏(152)\nFAZKOROONEE AZKURKUM WASH KOROO LEE WA LAA TAKFOROON.\nTherefore, remember Me, I will remember you, and be thankful to Ale and (he) not ungrateful\nيٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اسْتَعِيْنُوْا بِالصَّبْرِ وَالصَّلٰوةِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(153)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEEENA AAMANUS TA-E’ENOO BIS-SABRE WAS SALAAH, INNAL LAAHA MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\nO’ ye who believe! seek help with patience and prayer; Verily God is with the patient ones\nوَلَا تَقُوْلُوْا لِمَنْ يُّقْتَلُ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ اَمْوَاتٌ ؕ بَلْ اَحْيَآءٌ وَّلٰكِنْ لَّا تَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(154)\nWA LAA TAQOOLOO LEMAN-Y YUQTALO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE AMWAAT, BAL AHYAAA-UNW WA LAAKIL LAA TASH-O’ROON.\nAnd say not of those who are slain in the path of God that they are dead; Nay, (they are) living, but ye perceive not\nوَلَنَبْلُوَنَّكُمْ بِشَىْءٍ مِّنَ الْخَوْفِ وَالْجُوْعِ وَنَقْصٍ مِّنَ الْاَمْوَالِ وَالْاَنْفُسِ وَالثَّمَرٰتِؕ وَبَشِّرِ الصّٰبِرِيْنَۙ‏(155)\nWA LA-NABLOWANNAKUM BE-SHAY-IM MENAL KHAWFE WAL JOO-E’ WA NAQSIM MENAL AMWAALE WAL ANFOSE WAS SAMARAAT, WA BASH-SHERIS SAABEREENAL.\nWe will surely test you with something of fear, and hunger and loss of wealth and lives and fruits; and give glad tidings to the patient ones\nالَّذِيْنَ اِذَآ اَصَابَتْهُمْ مُّصِيْبَةٌ  ۙ قَالُوْٓا اِنَّا لِلّٰهِ وَاِنَّآ اِلَيْهِ رٰجِعُوْنَؕ‏(156)\nLAZEENA EZAA ASAABATHUM MOSEEBATUN, QAALOO INNAA LIL-LAAHE WA INNAA ELAYHE RAAJE-O’ON.\nWho when, misfortune befalleth them, say, “Verity we are God’s and verity unto Him shall we return\nاُولٰٓئِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ صَلَوٰتٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُهْتَدُوْنَ‏(157)\nOOLAAA-EKA A’LAYHIM SALAWAATUM MIR RABBEHIM WA RAHMAH, WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MOHTADOON.\nThose are they on whom are the blessings from their Lord and (His) Mercy; and they are the ones that are (rightly) guided\nاِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِنْ شَعَآئِرِ اللّٰهِۚ فَمَنْ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ اَوِ اعْتَمَرَ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ اَنْ يَّطَّوَّفَ بِهِمَا ؕ وَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ خَيْرًا ۙ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ شَاكِرٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(158)\nINNAS SAFAA WAL MARWATA MIN SHA-A’AA-ERIL LAAH, FAMAN HAJJAL BAYTA AWE’ TAMARA FALAA JONAAHA A’LAYHE AN-Y YATTAWWAFA BEHEMAA, WA MAN TATAWWA-A’ KHAYRAN, FA-INNAL LAAHA SHAAKERUN A’LEEM.\nVerily, ‘‘Safa’ and ‘Marwa’ are among the signs of God; whoever therefore, maketh a pilgrimage to the House or performeth ‘Umra’. Therefore, it shall be no blame on him to go round them both; and whoever of his own accord doeth anything good in deed, verily God is Grateful, All-Knowing\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَكْتُمُوْنَ مَآ اَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ الْبَيِّنٰتِ وَالْهُدٰى مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا بَيَّنّٰهُ لِلنَّاسِ فِى الْكِتٰبِۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ يَلْعَنُهُمُ اللّٰهُ وَ يَلْعَنُهُمُ اللّٰعِنُوْنَۙ‏(159)\nINNAL LAZEENA YAKTOMOONA MAA ANZALNAA MENAL BAYYENAATE WAL HODAA MIM BA’DE MAA BAYYANNAAHO LIN-NAASE FIL KETAABE, OOLAAA-EKA YAL-A’NOHOMUL LAAHO WA YAL-A’NOHOMUL LAA-E’NOONA.\nVerily, those that conceal what We have sent of (Our) manifest evidences and guidance, after what We have (so) clearly shown for mankind in the Book, (they are) those that God doth curse them and (also) curse them (all) those who curse (such ones)\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا وَاَصْلَحُوْا وَبَيَّنُوْا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ اَ تُوْبُ عَلَيْهِمْۚ وَاَنَا التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(160)\nILLAL LAZEENA TAABOO WA ASLAHOO WA BAYYANOO FA-OOLAAA-EKA ATOOBO A’LAYHIM, WA ANAT TAWWAABUR RAHEEM.\nExcept those who turn (repentant) and amend (themselves) and make manifest (The Truth), these it is unto whom I turn (mercifully), and I am the Oft-returning (to mercy), the All-Merciful\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَمَاتُوْا وَهُمْ كُفَّارٌ اُولٰٓئِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ لَعْنَةُ اللّٰهِ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ وَالنَّاسِ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(161)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA MAATOO WA HUM KUFFAARUN OOLAAA-EKA A’LAYHIM LA’NATUL LAAHE WAL MALAA-EKATE WAN NAASE AJMA-E’ENA.\nVerily, those who disbelieve and die while they are disbelievers, on them shall be the curse of God, and (of) the angels and (of) mankind all together\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ۚ لَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمُ الْعَذَابُ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(162)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, LAA YOKHAFFAFO A’NHOMUL A’ZAABO WA LAA HUM YUNZAROON.\nAbiding in it the torment shall not be lightened for them nor shall they have respite\nوَاِلٰهُكُمْ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ  ۚ لَآ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ الرَّحْمٰنُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(163)\nWA ELAAHOKUM ELAAHUNW WAAHED, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWAR RAHMAANUR RAHEEM.\nAnd your God is one God! There is no god but He! He is the Beneficent, the Merciful!\nاِنَّ فِىْ خَلْقِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَاخْتِلَافِ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَالْفُلْكِ الَّتِىْ تَجْرِىْ فِى الْبَحْرِ بِمَا يَنْفَعُ النَّاسَ وَمَآ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مِنْ مَّآءٍ فَاَحْيَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا وَبَثَّ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ دَآ بَّةٍ وَّتَصْرِيْفِ الرِّيٰحِ وَالسَّحَابِ الْمُسَخَّرِ بَيْنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(164)\nINNA FEE KHALQIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WAKHTELAAFIL LAYLE WAN NAHAARE WAL FULKIL LATEE TAJREE FIL BAHRE BEMAA YANFAU’N NAASA WA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO MENAS SAMAAA-E MIM MAAA-IN FA-AHYAA BEHIL ARZA BA’DA MAWTEHAA WA BASSA FEEHAA MIN KULLE DAABBATINW, WA TASREEFIR REYAAHE WAS SAHAABIL MOSAKHKHARE BAYNAS SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMIN-Y YA’QELOON.\nVerily in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day and (in) the ships that sail in the sea with what profiteth mankind and (in) the water which God sendeth down from the skies and enliveneth therewith the earth after its death and scattereth therein of (every kind of) animal, and in the changing of the winds and the clouds controlled for service between the heavens and the earth, surely there are signs for (the guidance of) people who understand\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَّتَّخِذُ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَنْدَادًا يُّحِبُّوْنَهُمْ كَحُبِّ اللّٰهِؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْٓا اَشَدُّ حُبًّا لِّلّٰهِ ؕ وَلَوْ يَرَى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْٓا اِذْ يَرَوْنَ الْعَذَابَۙ اَنَّ الْقُوَّةَ لِلّٰهِ جَمِيْعًا ۙ وَّاَنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعَذَابِ‏(165)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN-Y YATTAKHEZO MIN DOONIL LAAHE ANDAADAN-Y YOHIBBOONAHUM KA-HUBBIL LAAH, WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO ASHADDO HUBBAL LIL-LAAH, WA LAW YARAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO IZ YARAWNAL A’ZABA, ANNAL QUWWATA LIL-LAAHE JAMEE-A’NW, WA ANNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL A’ZAAB.\nAnd yet of men there are some who take unto themselves equals to God besides Him and love them as the love for God; But the Believers are stauncher in (their) love for God; And if only those who are unjust could see (what they will realise) when they behold the torment, that unto God belongeth all power and verily God is severe in punishing\nاِذْ تَبَرَّاَ الَّذِيْنَ اتُّبِعُوْا مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْا وَرَاَوُا الْعَذَابَ وَ تَقَطَّعَتْ بِهِمُ الْاَسْبَابُ‏(166)\nIZ TABARRA-AL LAZEENAT TOBE-O’O MENAL LAZEENAT TABA-O’O WA RA-A-WUL A’ZAABA WA TAQATTA-A’T BEHEMUL ASBAAB.\nWhen would those who were followed renounce them that followed them, and they would see the torment and the ties between them are cut asunder\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّبَعُوْا لَوْ اَنَّ لَنَا كَرَّةً فَنَتَبَرَّاَ مِنْهُمْ كَمَا تَبَرَّءُوْا مِنَّا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُرِيْهِمُ اللّٰهُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ حَسَرٰتٍ عَلَيْهِمْؕ وَمَا هُمْ بِخٰرِجِيْنَ مِنَ النَّارِ‏(167)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENAT TABA-O’O LAW ANNA LANAA KARRATAN FANATABARRA-A MINHUM KAMAA TABARRA-OO MINNAA, KAZAALEKA YOREEHEMUL LAAHO A-A’MAALAHUM HASARAATIN A’LAYHIM, WA MAA HUM BE-KHAAREJEENA MENAN NAAR.\nAnd those who followed shall say, “O’ were there for us a return (to the world’) then we would renounce them even as they have renounced us;” Thus, will God show them their deeds (which shall be the cause of) intense regrets for them; and they shall not get out of the (Hell) fire\nيٰٓاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ كُلُوْا مِمَّا فِى الْاَرْضِ حَلٰلًا طَيِّبًا  ۖ وَّلَا تَتَّبِعُوْا خُطُوٰتِ الشَّيْطٰنِؕ اِنَّهٗ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(168)\nYAA AYYOHAN NAASO KOLOO MIMMAA FIL ARZE HALAALAN TAYYEBAA, WA LAA TATTABE-O’O KHOTOWATIS SHAYTAAN, INNAHU LAKUM A’DUWWUM MOBEEN.\nO’ ye men! eat of what is in the earth lawful and good and follow not the footsteps of Satan; for verily he is an open enemy unto you\nاِنَّمَا يَاْمُرُكُمْ بِالسُّوْٓءِ وَالْفَحْشَآءِ وَاَنْ تَقُوْلُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(169)\nINNAMAA YAAMOROKUM BIS-SOOO-E WAL FAH-SHAAA-E WA AN TAQOOLOO A’LAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nFor, verily, verily he commandeth unto you what is evil and shameful and that ye should say against God that which ye know not\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمُ اتَّبِعُوْا مَآ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ قَالُوْا بَلْ نَتَّبِعُ مَآ اَلْفَيْنَا عَلَيْهِ اٰبَآءَنَا ؕ اَوَلَوْ كَانَ اٰبَآؤُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(170)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHOMUT TABE-O’O MAA ANZALAL LAAHO QAALOO BAL NATTA-BE-O’ MAA ALFAYNAA A’LAYHE AABAAA-ANAA, A-WA LAW KAANA AA-BAAA-OHUM LAA YA’QELOONA SHAY-ANW WA LAA YAHTADOON.\nAnd when it is said unto them, “Follow what God hath sent down” They say, “Nay! We follow that which we found our fathers upon” What! even though their fathers had no sense at all, nor were (they) guided aright?\nوَمَثَلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا كَمَثَلِ الَّذِىْ يَنْعِقُ بِمَا لَا يَسْمَعُ اِلَّا دُعَآءً وَّنِدَآءً ؕ صُمٌّۢ بُكْمٌ عُمْىٌ فَهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(171)\nWA MASALUL LAZEENA KAFAROO KAMASALIL LAZEE YAN-E’QO BEMAA LAA YASMA-O’ ILLAA DO-A’AA-ANW WA NEDAAA, SUMMUM BUKMUN U’MYUN FAHUM LAA YA’QELOON.\nThe parable of those that disbelieve is the likeness of one who shouteth to (one) which heareth not but a call and a cry; deaf, dumb, blind (are they) wherefore they do not understand\nيٰٓاَ يُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كُلُوْا مِنْ طَيِّبٰتِ مَا رَزَقْنٰكُمْ وَاشْكُرُوْا لِلّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ اِيَّاهُ تَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(172)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KOLOO MIN TAYYEBAATE MAA RAZAQNAAKUM WASH KOROO LIL-LAAHE IN KUNTUM IYYAAHO TA’BODOON.\nO’ ye who believe! eat of the good things We have provided you with and thank God if Him it is ye worship\nاِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَيْتَةَ وَالدَّمَ وَلَحْمَ الْخِنْزِيْرِ وَمَآ اُهِلَّ بِهٖ لِغَيْرِ اللّٰهِۚ فَمَنِ اضْطُرَّ غَيْرَ بَاغٍ وَّلَا عَادٍ فَلَاۤ اِثْمَ عَلَيْهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(173)\nINNAMAA HARRAMA A’LAYKOMUL MAYTATA WAD DAMA WA LAHMAL KHINZEERE WA MAA OHILLA BEHI LE-GHAYRIL LAAH, FAMANIZ TURRA GHAYRA BAAGHINW WA LAA A’ADIN FALAA ISMA A’LAYH, INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nVerily, verily He hath but prohibited that which dieth of itself and blood and the swine flesh and whatsoever hath other name than God’s invoked upon it, but whoever is forced to it without the desire (for it) nor to transgress (the limits) then it is no sin on him; Verily God is Forgiving, Merciful\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَكْتُمُوْنَ مَآ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِ وَ يَشْتَرُوْنَ بِهٖ ثَمَنًا قَلِيْلًا ۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ مَا يَاْكُلُوْنَ فِىْ بُطُوْنِهِمْ اِلَّا النَّارَ وَلَا يُكَلِّمُهُمُ اللّٰهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَلَا يُزَكِّيْهِمْ ۖۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(174)\nINNAL LAZEENA YAKTOMOONA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO MENAL KETAABE WA YASHTAROONA BEHI SAMANAN QALEELAA, OOLAAA-EKA MAA YAAKOLOONA FEE BOTOONEHIM ILLAN NAARA WA LAA YOKALLEMOHOMUL LAAHO YAWMAL QEYAAMATE WA LAA YOZAKKEEHIM, WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nVerily, those that conceal that of the Scripture which God hath sent down and barter for a small price, these, they eat nothing but fire into their bellies, and God will not speak to them on the Day of Resurrection nor will He purify them, and for them there shall be grievous torment\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اشْتَرَوُا الضَّلٰلَةَ بِالْهُدٰى وَالْعَذَابَ بِالْمَغْفِرَةِ ۚ فَمَآ اَصْبَرَهُمْ عَلَى النَّارِ‏(175)\nOOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENASH TARAWUZ ZALAALATA BIL-HODAA WAL A’ZAABA BIL-MAGHFERAH,  FAMAA ASBARAHUM A’LAN NAAR.\nThese are they who have purchased error in barter for the right guidance and the torment for forgiveness, Oh! how (bold) they are to endure the Fire\nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ نَزَّلَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّؕ وَاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اخْتَلَفُوْا فِى الْكِتٰبِ لَفِىْ شِقَاقٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(176)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA NAZZALAL KETAABA BIL-HAQ, WA INNAL LAZEENAKH TALAFOO FIL KETAABE LAFEE SHEQAAQIM BA-E’ED.\nThis is (their doom) because God hath sent down the Book with the truth; Verily, those who differ in (the matter of) the Book are in a wide gap\nلَيْسَ الْبِرَّ اَنْ تُوَلُّوْا وُجُوْهَكُمْ قِبَلَ الْمَشْرِقِ وَ الْمَغْرِبِ وَلٰكِنَّ الْبِرَّ مَنْ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ وَالْكِتٰبِ وَالنَّبِيّٖنَۚ وَاٰتَى الْمَالَ عَلٰى حُبِّهٖ ذَوِى الْقُرْبٰى وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنَ وَابْنَ السَّبِيْلِۙ وَالسَّآئِلِيْنَ وَفِى الرِّقَابِۚ وَاَقَامَ الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَى الزَّكٰوةَ  ۚ وَالْمُوْفُوْنَ بِعَهْدِهِمْ اِذَا عٰهَدُوْا ۚ وَالصّٰبِرِيْنَ فِى الْبَاْسَآءِ وَالضَّرَّآءِ وَحِيْنَ الْبَاْسِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ صَدَقُوْا ؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ‏(177)\nLAYSAL BIRRA AN TOWALLOO WOJOOHAKUM QEBALAL MASHREQE WAL MAGHREBE WA LAAKINNAL BIRRA MAN AAMANA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WAL MALAA-EKATE WAL KETAABE WAN NABIYYEEN, WA AATAL MAALA A’LAA HUBBEHI ZAWIL QURBAA WAL YATAAMAA WAL MASAAKEENA WAB NAS SABEELE, WAS SAAA-ELEENA WA FIR REQAAB, WA AQAAMAS SALAATA WA AATAZ ZAKAAH, WAL MOOFOONA BE-A’HDEHIM EZAA A’AHADOO, WAS SAABEREENA FIL BAA-SAAA-E WAZ ZARRAAA-E WA HEENAL BAAS, OOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENA SADAQOO, WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUTTAQOON.\nIt is not righteousness that ye turn your faces towards the East and the West, righteousness is rather one who believeth in God and the Last Day and the angels and the Book, the apostles, and giveth his wealth out of 1ove for Him to the kindred and the orphans and the poor and the wayfarer and the needy and for those in bondage; And established prayer and payeth the poor-rate; And those who fulfil their promise when they make a promise and the patient ones in distress and affliction and in the time of war these are they who are the Truthful and these are they who are the pious\nيٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِصَاصُ فِى الْقَتْلٰى  ؕ الْحُرُّ بِالْحُرِّ وَالْعَبْدُ بِالْعَبْدِ وَالْاُنْثَىٰ بِالْاُنْثٰىؕ فَمَنْ عُفِىَ لَهٗ مِنْ اَخِيْهِ شَىْءٌ فَاتِّبَاعٌۢ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَاَدَآءٌ اِلَيْهِ بِاِحْسَانٍؕ ذٰلِكَ تَخْفِيْفٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ  ؕ فَمَنِ اعْتَدٰى بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ فَلَهٗ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌۚ‏(178)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KOTEBA A’LAYKOMUL QESAASO FIL QATLAA, AL-HURRO BIL-HURRE WAL A’BDO BIL-A’BDE WAL UNSAA BIL-UNSAA, FAMAN O’FEYA LAHU MIN AKHEEHE SHAY-UN FATTEBAA-U’M BIL-MA’ROOFE WA ADAAA-UN ELAYHE BE-EHSAAN, ZAALEKA TAKHFEEFUM MIR RABBEKUM WA RAHMAH, FAMANE’ TADAA BA’DA ZAALEKA FALAHU A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nO, ye who believe! Retaliation is prescribed for you in the matter of the (unlawfully) murdered, the freeman for the freeman, the bondman for the bondman the woman for the woman; but. if any remission is made (to any one) by his (aggrieved) brother then the recognised course be adopted, and payment made to him in handsome manner. This is an alleviation and a mercy from your Lord, and whosoever transgresseth the limit after this, then for him shall be a painful chastisement\nوَ لَكُمْ فِى الْقِصَاصِ حَيٰوةٌ يّٰٓاُولِىْ الْاَلْبَابِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(179)\nWA LAKUM FIL QESAASE HAYAATUN-Y YAA OOLIL ALBAABE LA-A’LLAKUM TATTAQOON.\nAnd for you there is (security of) life in (the law of) Retaliation O, ye men of understanding, so that ye may guard yourself (against evil)\nكُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمْ اِذَا حَضَرَ اَحَدَكُمُ الْمَوْتُ اِنْ تَرَكَ خَيْرَا  ۖۚ اۨلْوَصِيَّةُ لِلْوَالِدَيْنِ وَالْاَقْرَبِيْنَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِۚ حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُتَّقِيْنَؕ‏(180)\nKOTEBA A’LAYKUM EZAA HAZARA AHADAKOMUL MAWTO IN TARAKA KHAYRA-NIL, WASIYYATO LIL-WAALEDAYNE WAL AQRABEENA BIL-MA’ROOF, HAQQAN A’LAL MUTTAQEEN.\nIt is prescribed for you when death approacheth (any) one of you, if he leaveth behind any goods that he maketh a bequest for parents and (the nearest) kinsmen in goodness (this is) a duty (incumbent) upon the pious (ones)\nفَمَنْۢ بَدَّلَهٗ بَعْدَمَا سَمِعَهٗ فَاِنَّمَآ اِثْمُهٗ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يُبَدِّلُوْنَهٗؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌؕ‏(181)\nFAMAM BADDALAHU BA’DA MAA SAME-A’HU FA-INNAMAA ISMOHU A’LAL LAZEENA YOBADDELOONAH, INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAnd whosoever altereth the bequest after he has heard it, the guilt shall be on those who alter it. Verily, God is All-hearing and All-Knowing\nفَمَنْ خَافَ مِنْ مُّوْصٍ جَنَفًا اَوْ اِثْمًا فَاَصْلَحَ بَيْنَهُمْ فَلَاۤ اِثْمَ عَلَيْهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(182)\nFAMAN KHAAFA MIM MOOSIN JANAFAN AW ISMAN FA-ASLAHA BAYNAHUM FALAA ISMA A’LAYH, INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nBut he who feareth from a testator anything unjust or sinful and establisheth agreement between them (it shall be) no sin for him; Verily God is Forgiving and Merciful\nيٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الصِّيَامُ كَمَا كُتِبَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُوْنَۙ‏(183)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KOTEBA A’LAYKOMUS SEYAAMO KAMAA KOTEBA A’LAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TATTAQOONA.\nO’ ye who believe! Fasting has been ordained unto you as it was ordained unto those before you so that ye guard yourself (against evil)\nاَيَّامًا مَّعْدُوْدٰتٍؕ فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ مَّرِيْضًا اَوْ عَلٰى سَفَرٍ فَعِدَّةٌ مِّنْ اَيَّامٍ اُخَرَؕ وَعَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يُطِيْقُوْنَهٗ فِدْيَةٌ طَعَامُ مِسْكِيْنٍؕ فَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ خَيْرًا فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّهٗ ؕ وَاَنْ تَصُوْمُوْا خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(184)\nAYYAAMAM MA’DOODAAT, FAMAN KAANA MINKUM MAREEZAN AW A’LAA SAFARIN FA-I’DDATUM MIN AYYAAMIN OKHAR, WA A’LAL LAZEENA YOTEEQOONAHU FIDYATUN TA-A’AMO MISKEEN, FAMAN TATAWWA-A’ KHAYRAN FAHOWA KHAYRUL LAH, WA AN TASOOMOO KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nFor a fixed number of days, but whoso among you is sick or on a journey then (he shall fast) that number of days; and those who are hardly able to do it, may effect a redemption by feeding a poor man, and (even so) whoso of his own accord performeth a good deed, it is better for him; and that ye fast is better for you if ye know\nشَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِىْٓ اُنْزِلَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنُ هُدًى لِّلنَّاسِ وَ بَيِّنٰتٍ مِّنَ الْهُدٰى وَالْفُرْقَانِۚ فَمَنْ شَهِدَ مِنْكُمُ الشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ ؕ وَمَنْ كَانَ مَرِيْضًا اَوْ عَلٰى سَفَرٍ فَعِدَّةٌ مِّنْ اَيَّامٍ اُخَرَؕ يُرِيْدُ اللّٰهُ بِكُمُ الْيُسْرَ وَلَا يُرِيْدُ بِكُمُ الْعُسْرَ وَلِتُكْمِلُوا الْعِدَّةَ وَلِتُكَبِّرُوا اللّٰهَ عَلٰى مَا هَدٰٮكُمْ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(185)\nSHAHRO RAMAZAANAL LAZEE UNZELA FEEHIL QUR-AANO HODAL LIN-NAASE WA BAYYENAATIM MENAL HODAA WAL FURQAAN, FAMAN SHAHEDA MINKOMUSH SHAHRA FAL-YASUMH, WA MAN KAANA MAREEZAN AW A’LAA SAFARIN FA-I’DDATUM MIN AYYAAMIN OKHAR, YOREEDUL LAAHO BEKOMUL YUSRA WA LAA YOREEDO BEKOMUL U’SR, WA LETUKMELUL I’DDATA WA LE-TOKABBERUL LAAHA A’LAA MAA HADAAKUM WA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nThe month of Ramadhan that in which was sent down the Qur’an a Guidance for mankind and Clear Evidence of guidance and Discrimination (for the Right and the Wrong); So whosoever of you witnesseth the month, he shall fast therein; and whosoever is ill or on a journey (he shall fast) the same number of other days; God desireth fasted ease for you and He desireth not for you hardship that ye shall complete the (prescribed) number (of days) and that ye may glorify God for His guiding you and that ye may be thankful (to Him)\nوَاِذَا سَاَلَكَ عِبَادِىْ عَنِّىْ فَاِنِّىْ قَرِيْبٌؕ اُجِيْبُ دَعْوَةَ الدَّاعِ اِذَا دَعَانِ فَلْيَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لِىْ وَلْيُؤْمِنُوْا بِىْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْشُدُوْنَ‏(186)\nWA EZAA SA-ALAKA E’BAADEE A’NNEE FA-INNEE QAREEB, OJEEBO DA’WATAD DAA-E’ EZAA DA-A’ANE, FAL-YASTAJEEBOO LEE WAL-YOAMENOO BEE LA-A’LLAHUM YARSHODOON.\nAnd when My servants ask thee about Me, then (say unto them) verily I am nigh; I answer the prayer of the supplicant when he beseecheth unto Me, so let them hearken unto Me and believe in Me, so that they may be led aright\nاُحِلَّ لَكُمْ لَيْلَةَ الصِّيَامِ الرَّفَثُ اِلٰى نِسَآئِكُمْؕ هُنَّ لِبَاسٌ لَّكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ لِبَاسٌ لَّهُنَّ ؕ عَلِمَ اللّٰهُ اَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَخْتَانُوْنَ اَنْفُسَكُمْ فَتَابَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَعَفَا عَنْكُمْۚ فَالْئٰنَ بَاشِرُوْهُنَّ وَابْتَغُوْا مَا كَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ وَكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا حَتّٰى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكُمُ الْخَيْطُ الْاَبْيَضُ مِنَ الْخَيْطِ الْاَسْوَدِ مِنَ الْفَجْرِؕ ثُمَّ اَتِمُّوا الصِّيَامَ اِلَى الَّيْلِۚ وَلَا تُبَاشِرُوْهُنَّ وَاَنْتُمْ عٰكِفُوْنَ فِى الْمَسٰجِدِؕ تِلْكَ حُدُوْدُ اللّٰهِ فَلَا تَقْرَبُوْهَا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ اٰيٰتِهٖ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(187)\nOHILLA LAKUM LAYLATAS SEYAAMIR RAFASO ELAA NESAAA-EKUM, HUNNA LEBAASUL LAKUM WA ANTUM LEBAASUL LAHUN, A’LEMAL LAAHO ANNAKUN KUNTUM TAKHTAANOONA ANFOSAKUM FATAABA A’LAYKUM WA A’FAA A’NKUM, FAL-AANA BAASHEROOHUNNA WAB-TAGHOO MAA KATABAL LAAHO LAKUM, WA KOLOO WASH RABOO HATTAA YATABAYYANA LAKOMUL KHAYTUL ABYAZO MENAL KHAYTIL ASWADE MENAL FAJR, SUMMA ATIMMUS SEYAAMA ELAL LAYL, WA LAA TOBAASHEROOHUNNA WA ANTUM A’AKEFOONA, FIL MASAAJED, TILKA HODOODUL LAAHE FALAA TAQRABOOHAA, KAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO AAYAATEHI LIL-NAASE LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON.\nIt is made lawful unto you on the nights of the fast to go in unto your wives; they are an apparel for you and ye are apparel for them; God Without knoweth that ye yourselves held it fraudulent so He hath turned (in mercy) towards you and forgiven you. Wherefore go in unto them and seek what God hath prescribed for you, and eat and drink until the white streak (of dawn) becometh manifest unto you from the black streak (of night) thereafter complete the fast until night and associate not with them while ye are confined in the mosques. These are the bounds prescribed by God therefore, draw not (yourselves) near them; Thus, doth God make clear His signs unto mankind so that they may guard themselves (against evil)\nوَلَا تَاْكُلُوْٓا اَمْوَالَكُمْ بَيْنَكُمْ بِالْبَاطِلِ وَتُدْلُوْا بِهَآ اِلَى الْحُكَّامِ لِتَاْكُلُوْا فَرِيْقًا مِّنْ اَمْوَالِ النَّاسِ بِالْاِثْمِ وَاَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(188)\nWA LAA TAAKOLOO AMWAALAKUM BAYNAKUM BIL-BAATELE WA TUDLOO BEHAA ELAL HUKKAAME LE-TAAKOLOO FAREEQAM MIN AMWAALIN NAASE BIL-ISME WA ANTUM TA’LAMOON.\nAnd do not swallow up your property among yourselves by wrongful means, neither seek to gain access thereby to the authorities that ye may swallow up a portion of the property of men wrongfully while ye know\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْاَهِلَّةِ ؕ قُلْ هِىَ مَوَاقِيْتُ لِلنَّاسِ وَالْحَجِّ ؕ وَلَيْسَ الْبِرُّ بِاَنْ تَاْتُوا الْبُيُوْتَ مِنْ ظُهُوْرِهَا وَلٰكِنَّ الْبِرَّ مَنِ اتَّقٰىۚ وَاْتُوا الْبُيُوْتَ مِنْ اَبْوَابِهَا وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏‏‏(189)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL AHILLAH, QUL HEYA MAWAAQEETO LIN-NAASE WAL-HAJ, WA LAYSAL BIRRO BE-AN TAATUL BOYOOTA MIN ZOHOOREHAA WA LAAKINNAL BIRRA MANIT TAQAA, WAA TUL BOYOOTA MIN ABWAABEHAA, WAT TAQUL LAAHA LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nThey ask thee (Our Apostle Muhammad) concerning the new moons; say ‘they are indications of times fixed for men and for the pilgrimage; It is not righteousness that ye should enter your houses from behind but the righteous one is the one who guardeth himself (against evil) and enter ye (the) houses by their doors and take shelter in God so that ye may be successful\nوَقَاتِلُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ الَّذِيْنَ يُقَاتِلُوْنَكُمْ وَلَا تَعْتَدُوْا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِيْنَ‏(190)\nWA QAATELOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHIL LAZEENA YOQAATELOONAKUM WA LAA TA’TADOO, INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL MO’TADEEN.\nAnd fight in the cause of God (against) those who fight you but be not aggressive; for verily God loveth not the aggressors\nوَاقْتُلُوْهُمْ حَيْثُ ثَقِفْتُمُوْهُمْ وَاَخْرِجُوْهُمْ مِّنْ حَيْثُ اَخْرَجُوْكُمْ وَالْفِتْنَةُ اَشَدُّ مِنَ الْقَتْلِۚ وَلَا تُقٰتِلُوْهُمْ عِنْدَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ حَتّٰى يُقٰتِلُوْكُمْ فِيْهِۚ فَاِنْ قٰتَلُوْكُمْ فَاقْتُلُوْهُمْؕ كَذٰلِكَ جَزَآءُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(191)\nWAQ TOLOOHUM HAYSO SAQIFTOMOOHUM WA AKHREJOOHUM MIN HAYSO AKHRAJOOKUM WAL FITNATO ASHADDO MENAL QATL, WA LAA TOQAATELOOHUM I’NDAL MASJEDIL HARAAME HATTAA YOQAATELOOKUM FEEH, FA-IN QAATALOOKUM FAQTOLOOHUM, KAZAALEKA JA-ZAAA-UL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd slay them wherever ye find them and drive them away whencefrom they drove you away for mischief is more grievous than slaughter but fight not with them nigh unto the (Inviolable) Sacred Mosque until they fight with you therein but if they fight with you slay them (for) such is the recompense of the disbelievers\nفَاِنِ انْتَهَوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(192)\nFA-ENIN TAHAW FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nBut if they desist, then verily God is Forgiving, Merciful\nوَقٰتِلُوْهُمْ حَتّٰى لَا تَكُوْنَ فِتْنَةٌ وَّيَكُوْنَ الدِّيْنُ لِلّٰهِؕ فَاِنِ انتَهَوْا فَلَا عُدْوَانَ اِلَّا عَلَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(193)\nWA QAATELOOHUM HATTAA LAA TAKOONA FITNATUNW WA YAKOONAD DEENO LIL-LAAH, FA-ENIN TAHAW FALAA U’DWAANA ILLAA A’LAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd fight with them until there is no (more) mischief and religion be only for God but if they desist then there should be no hostility save against the aggressors\nاَلشَّهْرُ الْحَرَامُ بِالشَّهْرِ الْحَرَامِ وَالْحُرُمٰتُ قِصَاصٌؕ فَمَنِ اعْتَدٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَاعْتَدُوْا عَلَيْهِ بِمِثْلِ مَا اعْتَدٰى عَلَيْكُمْ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ مَعَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(194)\nASH-SHAHRUL HARAAMO BISH-SHAHRIL HARAAME WAL HOROMAATO QESAAS, FAMANE’ TADAA A’LAYKUM FA’TADOO A’LAYHE BE-MISLE MA’ TADAA A’LAYKUM, WAT TAQUL LAAHA WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nA sacred month (in reprisal) for a sacred month and reprisal (is lawful) in (all) things sacred; whoever then inflicteth aggression on you, inflict ye the like aggression on him as was inflicted by him on you; and fear God, and know that God is (always) with the pious ones\nوَاَنْفِقُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا تُلْقُوْا بِاَيْدِيْكُمْ اِلَى التَّهْلُكَةِ ۖ  ۛۚ وَاَحْسِنُوْا  ۛۚ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(195)\nWA ANFEQOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA LAA TULQOO BE-AYDEEKUM ELAT TAHLOKAH, WA AHSENOO, INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUL MOHSENEEN.\nAnd spend in the path of God and cast not yourselves with your own hands into perdition, and do good, for verily God loveth the beneficent ones\nوَاَتِمُّوا الْحَجَّ وَالْعُمْرَةَ لِلّٰهِؕ فَاِنْ اُحْصِرْتُمْ فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْىِۚ وَلَا تَحْلِقُوْا رُءُوْسَكُمْ حَتّٰى يَبْلُغَ الْهَدْىُ مَحِلَّهٗ ؕ فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ مَّرِيْضًا اَوْ بِهٖۤ اَذًى مِّنْ رَّاْسِهٖ فَفِدْيَةٌ مِّنْ صِيَامٍ اَوْ صَدَقَةٍ اَوْ نُسُكٍۚ فَاِذَآ اَمِنْتُمْ فَمَنْ تَمَتَّعَ بِالْعُمْرَةِ اِلَى الْحَجِّ فَمَا اسْتَيْسَرَ مِنَ الْهَدْىِۚ فَمَنْ لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ ثَلٰثَةِ اَيَّامٍ فِى الْحَجِّ وَسَبْعَةٍ اِذَا رَجَعْتُمْؕ تِلْكَ عَشَرَةٌ كَامِلَةٌ  ؕ ذٰ لِكَ لِمَنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ اَهْلُهٗ حَاضِرِىْ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(196)\nWA ATIMMUL HAJJA WAL U’MRATA LIL-LAAH, FA-IN OHSIRTUM FAMAS TAYSARA MENAL HADY, WA LAA TAHLEQOO RO-OOSAKUM HATTAA YABLOGHAL HADYO MAHILLAH, FAMAN KAANA MINKUM MAREEZAN AW BEHI AZAM MIR RAASEHI FA-FIDYATUM MIN SEYAAMIN AW SADAQATIN AW NOSOK, FA-EZAA AMINTUM, FAMAN TAMATTA-A’ BIL-UMRATE ELAL HAJJE FAMAS TAYSARA MENAL HADY, FAMAL LAM YAJID FA-SEYAAMO SALAASATE AYYAAMIN FIL HAJJE WA SAB-A’TIN EZAA RA-JA’TUM, TILKA A’SHARATUN KAAMELAH, ZAALEKA LEMAL LAM YAKUN AHLOHU HAAZERIL MASJEDIL HARAAM, WAT TAQUL LAAHA WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nComplete the pilgrimage and ‘Umra’ for the sake of God; but if ye be prevented, then be sent whatever offering easily available (for you) and shave not your heads until your offering reacheth its place; but whosoever among you is sick and hath an ailment in his head then let him effect a compensation by fasting or alms or sacrifice; But when ye are secure (from the hinderance), then whoever enjoyeth from the ‘Umra’ to the ‘Hajj’ let him offer of whatsoever offering easily available (for him) but he who is not able to find (any offering) should fast for three days during the pilgrimage and for seven days when ye return; this (maketh) the ten (days) complete; this is for him whose people (nearest kith and kin) dwell not near the Sacred Mosque; and fear God and know ye! that God is severe in requiting evil\nاَلْحَجُّ اَشْهُرٌ مَّعْلُوْمٰتٌ ۚ فَمَنْ فَرَضَ فِيْهِنَّ الْحَجَّ فَلَا رَفَثَ وَلَا فُسُوْقَۙ وَلَا جِدَالَ فِى الْحَجِّ ؕ وَمَا تَفْعَلُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ يَّعْلَمْهُ اللّٰهُ ؕؔ وَتَزَوَّدُوْا فَاِنَّ خَيْرَ الزَّادِ التَّقْوٰى وَاتَّقُوْنِ يٰٓاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِ‏(197)\nAL-HAJJO ASH-HORUM MA’LOOMAAT, FAMAN FARAZA FEEHINNAL HAJJA FALAA RAFASA WA LAA FOSOOQA, WA LAA JEDAALA FIL HAJJ, WA MAA TAF-A’LOO MIN KHAYRIN-Y YA’LAMHUL LAAH, WA TAZAWWADOO FA-INNA KHAYRAZ ZAADIT TAQWAA, WAT TAQOONE YAA OOLIL ALBAAB.\nHajj is in the months well-known, whosoever then undertaketh the pilgrimage therein, then let there be no intercourse, nor bad language, nor quarrelling during the pilgrimage; and whatever of good ye do, God knoweth it; so make provision (for your journey) and verily the best provision is piety; and fear Me O ye people of understanding\nلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ اَنْ تَبْتَغُوْا فَضْلًا مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْؕ فَاِذَآ اَفَضْتُمْ مِّنْ عَرَفٰتٍ فَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ عِنْدَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ وَاذْكُرُوْهُ كَمَا هَدٰٮكُمْۚ وَاِنْ كُنْتُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلِهٖ لَمِنَ الضَّآ لِّيْنَ‏(198)\nLAYSA A’LAYKUM JONAAHUN AN TABTAGHOO FAZLAM MIR RABBEKUM, FA-EZAA AFAZTUM MIN A’RAFAATIN FAZKORUL LAAHA I’NDAL MASH-A’RIL HARAAM, WAZ KOROOHO KAMAA HADAAKUM, WA IN KUNTUM MIN QABLEHI LAMENAZ ZAAAL-LEEN.\nIt shall be no guilt on your part if ye seek bounty from your Lord (in trade during pilgrimage); then when ye march from Arafat remember God near the Holy Monument, and remember Him as He hath guided you, although ye were surely before this, of those who had gone astray\nثُمَّ اَفِيْضُوْا مِنْ حَيْثُ اَفَاضَ النَّاسُ وَاسْتَغْفِرُوا اللّٰهَؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(199)\nSUMMA AFEEZOO MIN HAYSO AFAAZAN NAASO WAS TAGHFERUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nThen march ye on from whence the other people march on and seek pardon of God; verily God is Forgiving, Merciful\nفَاِذَا قَضَيْتُمْ مَّنَاسِكَكُمْ فَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ كَذِكْرِكُمْ اٰبَآءَكُمْ اَوْ اَشَدَّ ذِكْرًا ؕ فَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَّقُوْلُ رَبَّنَآ اٰتِنَا فِى الدُّنْيَا وَمَا لَهٗ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ مِنْ خَلَاقٍ‏(200)\nFA-EZAA QAZAYTUM MANAASEKAKUM  FAZKORUL LAAHA KAZIKREKUM AABAAA-AKUM AW ASHADDA ZIKRAA, FAMENAN NAASE MAN-Y YAQOOLO RABBANAA AATENAA FID DUNYAA WA MAA LAHU FIL AAKHERATE MIN KHALAAQ.\nAnd when ye have performed your rites, remember God as ye remember your fathers, rather with a more intense remembrance; for of men there are those who say, ‘Our Lord! give us in this world’ and for him there shall be no portion in the Hereafter\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّقُوْلُ رَبَّنَآ اٰتِنَا فِى الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَّفِى الْاٰخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَّ قِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ‏(201)\nWA MINHUM MAN-Y YAQOOLO RABBANAA AATENAA FID DUNYAA HASANATANW WA FIL AAKHERATE HASANATANW WA QENAA A’ZAABAN NAAR.\nAnd among them there are some who say Our Lord! give us good in this world and good in the hereafter and save us from the torment of the (Hell) Fire\nاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ نَصِيْبٌ مِّمَّا كَسَبُوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(202)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAHUM NASEEBUM MIMMAA KASABOO, WAL LAAHO SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nThese shall have a portion of what they have earned; verily, God is quick in reckoning\nوَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ فِىْٓ اَيَّامٍ مَّعْدُوْدٰتٍؕ فَمَنْ تَعَجَّلَ فِىْ يَوْمَيْنِ فَلَاۤ اِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ ۚ وَمَنْ تَاَخَّرَ فَلَاۤ اِثْمَ عَلَيْهِ ۙ لِمَنِ اتَّقٰى ؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّكُمْ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(203)\nWAZ KORUL LAAHA FEE AYYAAMIM MA’DOODAAT, FAMAN TA-A’JJALA FEE YAWMAYNE FALAA ISMA A’LAYH, WA MAN TA-AKHKHARA FALAA ISMA A’LAYHE, LEMANIT TAQAA, WAT TAQUL LAAHA WA’ LAMOO ANNAKUM ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nAnd remember ye God on the numbered days; and whosoever hasteneth off in two days it will be no sin on him, and whoso tarrieth (there), on him (also) there will be no sin and this is for him who guardeth (against evil) so take ye shelter in God and know ye (that) unto Him ye shall (all) be gathered\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يُّعْجِبُكَ قَوْلُهٗ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَيُشْهِدُ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى مَا فِىْ قَلْبِهٖۙ وَهُوَ اَلَدُّ الْخِصَامِ‏(204)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN-Y YO’JEBOKA QAWLOHU FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA YUSH-HEDUL LAAHA A’LAA MAA FEE QALBEHI, WA HOWA ALADDUL KHESAAM.\nAnd among men there are those whose talk concerning the life here marveleth thee and he taketh God to witness as to what is in his heart, yet he is the most violent of adversaries\nوَاِذَا تَوَلّٰى سَعٰى فِى الْاَرْضِ لِيُفْسِدَ فِيْهَا وَيُهْلِكَ الْحَرْثَ وَالنَّسْلَؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْفَسَادَ‏(205)\nWA EZAA TAWALLAA SA-A’A FIL ARZE LE-YUFSEDA FEEHAA WA YOHLEKAL HARSA WAN NASL, WAL LAAHO LAA YOHIBBUL FASAAD.\nAnd when he turneth his back (unto thee) he striveth on earth (runs hither and thither) that he may cause mischief therein and destroy the tilth and stock; but God loveth not mischief\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُ اتَّقِ اللّٰهَ اَخَذَتْهُ الْعِزَّةُ بِالْاِثْمِ فَحَسْبُهٗ جَهَنَّمُؕ وَلَبِئْسَ الْمِهَادُ‏(206)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUT TAQIL LAAHA AKHAZATHUL I’ZZATO BIL-ISME FA-HASBOHU JAHANNAM, WA LA-BEASAL MEHAAD.\nAnd when it is said unto him, fear God, pride driveth him on to sin; so enough for him is Hell; and it is an evil abode indeed\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَّشْرِىْ نَفْسَهُ ابْتِغَآءَ مَرْضَاتِ اللّٰهِؕ وَ اللّٰهُ رَءُوْفٌ ۢ بِالْعِبَادِ‏(207)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN-Y YASHREE NAFSAHUB TEGHAAA-A MARZAATIL LAAH, WAL LAAHO RA-OOFUM BIL-E'BAAD.\nAnd among men there is one who selleth his self (soul) seeking the pleasure of God; and verily, God is affectionate unto His (faithful) servants\nيٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا ادْخُلُوْا فِى السِّلْمِ كَآفَّةً  وَلَا تَتَّبِعُوْا خُطُوٰتِ الشَّيْطٰنِؕ اِنَّهٗ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(208)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUD KHOLOO FIS SILME KAAAF-FATANW, WA LAA TATTABE-O’O KHOTOWAATISH SHAYTAAN, INNAHU LAKUM A’DUWWUM MOBEEN.\nO’ ye who believe! enter ye all into submission (to God) wholly and follow not the footsteps of Satan; for, verily, he is to you an Open Enemy\nفَاِنْ زَلَلْتُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَتْكُمُ الْبَيِّنٰتُ فَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(209)\nFA-IN ZALALTUM MIM BA’DE MAA JAAA-ATKOMUL BAYYENAATO FA’LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nBut if ye slip after that which hath come unto you of the clear signs then know ye that God is Mighty, Wise\nهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَهُمُ اللّٰهُ فِىْ ظُلَلٍ مِّنَ الْغَمَامِ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ وَقُضِىَ الْاَمْرُؕ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ تُرْجَعُ الْاُمُوْرُ‏(210)\nHAL YANZOROONA ILLAA AN-Y YAATEYAHOMUL LAAHO FEE ZOLALIM MENAL GHAMAAME WAL MALAAA-EKATO WA QOZEYAL AMR, WA ELAL LAAHE TURJA-U’L OMOOR.\nAwait they aught but that (the wrath of) God come unto them under canopies of bright cloud and the angels (of wrath) (come upon them) and the (whole) matter is decreed away; and to God all matters shall return\nسَلْ بَنِىْٓ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ كَمْ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ اٰيَةٍۢ بَيِّنَةٍ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّبَدِّلْ نِعْمَةَ اللّٰهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَتْهُ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(211)\nSAL BANEE ISRAAA-EELA KAM AATAYNAAHUM MIN AAYATIM BAYYENAH, WA MAN-Y YOBADDIL NE’MATAL LAAHE MIM BA’DE MAA JAAA-ATHO FA-INNAL LAAHA SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nAsk the Children of Israel how many of clear signs have We given them; and whosoever changeth the bounty of God after it hath come unto him, then, verily God is severe in requiting (evil)\nزُيِّنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا وَيَسْخَرُوْنَ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا  ۘ وَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا فَوْقَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(212)\nZUYYENA LIL-LAZEENA KAFARUL HAYAATUD DUNYAA WA YASKHAROONA MENAL LAZEENA AAMANOO, WAL LAHZEENAT TAQAW FAWQAHUM YAWMAL QEYAAMAH, WAL LAAHO YARZOQO MAN-Y YASHAAA-O BE-GHAYRE HESAAB.\nThe life of this world hath been made alluring to those who disbelieve and they scoff at those who believe; but those who guard (against evil) will be above them on the Day of Judgment; and verily God provideth with sustenance for whomso He willeth without (any) measure\nكَانَ النَّاسُ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً  فَبَعَثَ اللّٰهُ النَّبِيّٖنَ مُبَشِّرِيْنَ وَمُنْذِرِيْنَ وَاَنْزَلَ مَعَهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ لِيَحْكُمَ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ فِيْمَا اخْتَلَفُوْا فِيْهِ ؕ وَمَا اخْتَلَفَ فِيْهِ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوْهُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّنٰتُ بَغْيًا ۢ بَيْنَهُمْۚ فَهَدَى اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لِمَا اخْتَلَفُوْا فِيْهِ مِنَ الْحَقِّ بِاِذْنِهٖ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(213)\nKAANAN NAASO UMMATANW WAAHEDAH, FA-BA-A’SAL LAAHUN NABIYYEENA MOBASH-SHEREENA WA MUNZEREEN, WA ANZALA MA-A’HOMUL KETAABA BIL-HAQQE LE-YAHKOMA BAYNAN NAASE FEEMAKH TALAFOO FEEH, WA MAKH TALAFA FEEHE ILLAL LAZEENA OOTOOHO MIM BA’DE MAA JAAA-ATHOMUL BAYYENATO BAGHYAM BAYNAHUM, FA-HADAL LAAHUL LAZEENA AAMANOO LEMAKH TALAFOO FEEHE MENAL HAQQE BE-IZNEH, WAL LAAHO YAHDEE MAN-Y YASHAAA-O ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nMankind was but one people; and God sent apostles as bearers of good tidings and warners and sent down with them the Book with the Truth that it might judge between men in that wherein they differed; and none differed therein; but those very (people) whom it was given unto, after clear signs had come unto them, through revolt among themselves; whereupon God guided those who believed, by His Will, regarding that which the people differed about the Truth and verily God guideth whomso He willeth to the Right Path\nاَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ اَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَ لَمَّا يَاْتِكُمْ مَّثَلُ الَّذِيْنَ خَلَوْا مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْؕ مَسَّتْهُمُ الْبَاْسَآءُ وَالضَّرَّآءُ وَزُلْزِلُوْا حَتّٰى يَقُوْلَ الرَّسُوْلُ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ مَتٰى نَصْرُ اللّٰهِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ نَصْرَ اللّٰهِ قَرِيْبٌ‏(214)\nAM HASIBTUM AN TADKHOLUL JANNATA WA LAMMAA YAATEKUM MASALUL LAZEENA KHALAW MIN QABLEKUM, MASSATHOMUL BAASAAA-O WAZ ZARRAAA-O WA ZULZELOO HATTAA YAQOOLAR RASOOLO WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU MATAA NASRUL LAAH, ALAA INNA NASRAL LAAHE QAREEB.\nOr think ye that ye will enter the Garden while yet upon you hath not yet come the like of that which befell those who passed before you; distress and affliction came upon them, they were shaken so that (ultimately) the apostle saith, and (when) those who believed with him (asked the Apostle) “when will come the help of God”? “(Fear not) Verily God’s help is nigh\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ مَاذَا يُنْفِقُوْنَ ؕ قُلْ مَآ اَنْفَقْتُمْ مِّنْ خَيْرٍ فَلِلْوَالِدَيْنِ وَالْاَقْرَبِيْنَ وَالْيَتٰمٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيْلِؕ وَمَا تَفْعَلُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِهٖ عَلِيْمٌ‏(215)\nYAS-ALOONAKA MAA ZAA YUNFEQOON, QUL MAA ANFAQTUM MIN KHAYRIN FA-LILWAALEDAYNE WAL AQRABEENA WAL YATAAMAA WAL MASAAKEENE WAB NIS SABEEL, WA MAA TAF-A’LOO MIN KHAYRIN FA-INNAL LAAHA BEHI A’LEEM.\nThey ask thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) what they should spend; Say, whatever good ye spend let it be for parents, the near of kin, and the orphans, and the poor and the wayfarer; and whatever good ye do, verily God knoweth it\nكُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتَالُ وَهُوَ كُرْهٌ لَّكُمْۚ وَعَسٰۤى اَنْ تَكْرَهُوْا شَيْئًا وَّهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْۚ وَعَسٰۤى اَنْ تُحِبُّوْا شَيْئًا وَّهُوَ شَرٌّ لَّكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(216)\nKOTEBA A’LAYKOMUL QETAALO WA HOWA KURHUL LAKUM, WA A’SAA AN TAKRAHOO SHAY-ANW WA HOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM, WA A’SAA AN TOHIBBOO SHAY-ANW WA HOWA SHARRUL LAKUM, WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO WA ANTUL LAA TA’LAMOON.\nFighting (in the cause of God) is ordained unto you, and it is hateful to you, and perchance ye hate a thing whereas it is good for you, and perchance ye love a thing whereas it is bad for you; and verily God knoweth while ye know not\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الشَّهْرِ الْحَرَامِ قِتَالٍ فِيْهِؕ قُلْ قِتَالٌ فِيْهِ كَبِيْرٌ ؕ وَصَدٌّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَ كُفْرٌ ۢ بِهٖ وَالْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ وَاِخْرَاجُ اَهْلِهٖ مِنْهُ اَكْبَرُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَالْفِتْنَةُ اَكْبَرُ مِنَ الْقَتْلِؕ وَلَا يَزَالُوْنَ يُقَاتِلُوْنَكُمْ حَتّٰى يَرُدُّوْكُمْ عَنْ دِيْنِكُمْ اِنِ اسْتَطَاعُوْا ؕ وَمَنْ يَّرْتَدِدْ مِنْكُمْ عَنْ دِيْنِهٖ فَيَمُتْ وَهُوَ كَافِرٌ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ ۚ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(217)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NISH SHAHRIL HARAAME QETAALIN FEEH, QUL QETAALUN FEEHE KABEER, WA SADDUN A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WA KUFRUM BEHI WAL MASJEDIL HARAAM, WA IKHRAAJO AHLEHI MINHO AKBARO I’NDAL LAAH, WAL FITNATO AKBARO MENAL QATL, WA LAA YAZAALOONA YOQAATELOONAKUM HATTAA YARUDOOKUM A’N DEENEKUM ENIS TATAA-O’O, WA MAN-Y YARTADID MINKUM A’N DEENEHI FA-YAMOOT WA HOWA KAAFERUN FA-OOLAAA-EKA HABETAT A-A’MAALOHUM FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH, WA OOLAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR, HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nMischief is greater or graver than murder\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَالَّذِيْنَ هَاجَرُوْا وَجَاهَدُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ يَرْجُوْنَ رَحْمَتَ اللّٰهِؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(218)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAL LAZEENA HAAJAROO WA JAAHADOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE, OOLAAA-EKA YARJOON RAHMATAL LAAH, WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nVerily, those who believed and those who migrated (suffered exile) and fought (strove and struggled) in the way of God, these are they who (rightly) hope for the Mercy of God; and God is Oft-Forgiving, All-Merciful\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِؕ قُلْ فِيْهِمَآ اِثْمٌ كَبِيْرٌ وَّمَنَافِعُ لِلنَّاسِ وَاِثْمُهُمَآ اَكْبَرُ مِنْ نَّفْعِهِمَا ؕ وَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ مَاذَا يُنْفِقُوْنَؕ  قُلِ الْعَفْوَؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمُ الْاٰيٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَفَكَّرُوْنَۙ‏(219)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL KHAMRE WAL MAYSER, QUL FEEHEMAA ISMUN KABEERUNW WA MANAA-FE-O’ LIN-NAAS, WA ISMOHOMAA AKBARO MIN NAF-E’HEMAA, WA YAS-ALOONAKA MAA ZAA YUNFEQOON, QOLIL A’FW, KAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKOMUL AAYAATE LA-A’LLAKUM TATAFAKKAROONA.\nThey ask thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) concerning wine and lots (gambling and games of chance); Say, in both these is great sin and also (some) profits for men; but their sin is greater than their profit; And they will ask thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) as to what they shall spend (in alms); Say, ‘whatsoever can be spared’; thus, doth God maketh clear for you the signs so that ye may ponder\nفِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِؕ وَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْيَتٰمٰىؕ قُلْ اِصْلَاحٌ لَّهُمْ خَيْرٌ ؕ وَاِنْ تُخَالِطُوْهُمْ فَاِخْوَانُكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ الْمُفْسِدَ مِنَ الْمُصْلِحِؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَاَعْنَتَكُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(220)\nFID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH, WA YAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL YATAAMAA, QUL ISLAAHUL LAHUM KAHYR, WA IN TOKHAALETOOHUM FA-IKHWAANOKUM, WAL LAAHO YA’LAMUL MUFSEDA MENAL MUSLEH, WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LA-A-A’NATAKUM, INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nConcerning this world and the next; they will ask thee concerning orphans; Say, to set right for them (their affairs) is best; But if ye become co-partners with them, then they are your brethren; and God knoweth the corrupt from well-doer; and if God had willed, He could have surely made it hard for you; Verily, God is Mighty, Wise\nوَلَا تَنْكِحُوا الْمُشْرِكٰتِ حَتّٰى يُؤْمِنَّؕ وَلَاَمَةٌ مُّؤْمِنَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِّنْ مُّشْرِكَةٍ وَّلَوْ اَعْجَبَتْكُمْۚ وَلَا تُنْكِحُوا الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ حَتّٰى يُؤْمِنُوْا ؕ وَلَعَبْدٌ مُّؤْمِنٌ خَيْرٌ مِّنْ مُّشْرِكٍ وَّلَوْ اَعْجَبَكُمْؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ يَدْعُوْنَ اِلَى النَّارِ  ۖۚ وَاللّٰهُ يَدْعُوْٓا اِلَى الْجَنَّةِ وَالْمَغْفِرَةِ بِاِذْنِهٖۚ وَيُبَيِّنُ اٰيٰتِهٖ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ ‏(221)\nWA LAA TANKEHUL MUSHREKAATE HATTAA YOAMEN, WA LA-AMATUM MOAMENATUN KHAYRUM MIM MUSHREKATINW WA LAW A-A’JABATKUM, WA LAA TUNKEHUL MUSHREKEENA HATTAA YOAMENOO, WA LA-A’BDUM MOAMENUN KHAYRUM MIM MUSHREKINW WA LAW A-A’JABAKUM, OOLAAA-EKA YAD-O’ONA ELAN NAAR, WAL LAAHO YAD-O’O ELAL JANNAHTE WAL MAGHFERATE BE-IZNEH, WA YOBAYYENO AAYAATEHI LIN-NAASE LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nAnd marry not idolater women until they believe; a believer bondswoman is definitely better than an idolater (free) woman even though she may allure you; and give not in marriage (your women) to idolater men until they believe; a believer bondsman is better than an idolater (free) man; even though he may allure you; they beckon (you) to the (Hell) Fire, and verily God beckoneth (you) to the Garden and forgiveness by His leave and maketh clear His signs for men so that they may be mindful\nوَ يَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْمَحِيْضِۙ قُلْ هُوَ اَذًى فَاعْتَزِلُوْا النِّسَآءَ فِى الْمَحِيْضِۙ وَلَا تَقْرَبُوْهُنَّ حَتّٰى يَطْهُرْنَۚ فَاِذَا تَطَهَّرْنَ فَاْتُوْهُنَّ مِنْ حَيْثُ اَمَرَكُمُ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُحِبُّ التَّوَّابِيْنَ وَيُحِبُّ الْمُتَطَهِّرِيْنَ‏(222)\nWA YAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL MAHEEZ, QUL HOWA AZAN, FA’TAZELUN NESAAA-A FIL MAHEEZE, WA LAA TAQRABOOHUNNA HATTAA YATHURN, FA-EZAA TATAH-HARNAA FAATOOHUNNA MIN HAYSO AMARAKOMUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA YOHIBBUT TAWWAABEENA WA YOHIBBUL MOTATAHHEREEN.\nAnd they ask thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) concerning menstruation; say, it (is) a pollution, therefore, keep (yourselves) away from women when in menstruation and go not nigh unto them until they be cleansed, then when they are cleansed, go in unto them as God hath ordained unto you; verily, God loveth those who turn unto Him constantly and loveth those who clean themselves\nنِسَآؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَّكُمْ فَاْتُوْا حَرْثَكُمْ اَنّٰى شِئْتُمْ  وَقَدِّمُوْا لِاَنْفُسِكُمْؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّكُمْ مُّلٰقُوْهُ ؕ وَ بَشِّرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(223)\nNESAAA-OKUM HARSUL LAKUM, FAATOO HARSAKUM ANNAA SHEATUM, WA QADDEMOO LE-ANFOSEKUM, WAT TAQUL LAAHA WA’ LAMOO ANNAKUM MOLAAQOOH, WA BASH-SHERIL MOAMENEEN.\nYour women are your tilth, wherefor enter your tillage as ye please and provide in advance for yourselves (for the life hereafter); and take shelter in God, and know ye Beware) that ye are meeting Him (one day); and bear thou (O’ Our Apostle) glad tidings unto the faithful\nوَلَا تَجْعَلُوا اللّٰهَ عُرْضَةً لِّاَيْمَانِكُمْ اَنْ تَبَرُّوْا وَتَتَّقُوْا وَتُصْلِحُوْا بَيْنَ النَّاسِؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(224)\nWA LAA TAJ-A’LUL LAAHA U’RZATAL LE-AYMAANEKUM AN TABARROO WA TATTAQOO WA TUSLEHOO BAYNAN NAAS, WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAnd (O’ ye who believe!) make not (the name of) God in your oaths a hindrance against that ye may do good, and be pious and bring about peace among men; and verily, God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing\nلَا يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِىْٓ اَيْمَانِكُمْ وَلٰكِنْ يُّؤَاخِذُكُمْ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ قُلُوْبُكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(225)\nLAA YO-AAKHEZOKOMUL LAAHO BIL-LAGHWE FEE AYMAANEKUM WA LAAKIN-Y YO-AAKHEZOKUM BEMAA KASABAT QOLOOBOKUM, WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUN HALEEM.\nGod will call you not to account for a thoughtless oath but He will call you to account (for such oaths) what your hearts have earned and God is Oft-Forgiving, the Most Forbearing\nلِّلَّذِيْنَ يُؤْلُوْنَ مِنْ نِّسَآئِهِمْ تَرَبُّصُ اَرْبَعَةِ اَشْهُرٍۚ فَاِنْ فَآءُوْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(226)\nLIL-LAZEENA YOALOONA MIN NESAAA-EHIM TARABBOSO AR-BA-A’TE ASH-HOR, FA-IN FAAA-OO FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nFor those who swear to abstain from their wives, is ordained a waiting for four months, and if then they go back (from their oath) then verily God is Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful\nوَاِنْ عَزَمُوا الطَّلَاقَ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(227)\nWA IN A’ZAMUT TALAAQA FA-INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAnd if they resolve on divorce then verily God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing\nوَالْمُطَلَّقٰتُ يَتَرَ بَّصْنَ بِاَنْفُسِهِنَّ ثَلٰثَةَ قُرُوْٓءٍ ؕ وَلَا يَحِلُّ لَهُنَّ اَنْ يَّكْتُمْنَ مَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ فِىْٓ اَرْحَامِهِنَّ اِنْ كُنَّ يُؤْمِنَّ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِؕ وَبُعُوْلَتُهُنَّ اَحَقُّ بِرَدِّهِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ اِنْ اَرَادُوْٓا اِصْلَاحًا ؕ وَلَهُنَّ مِثْلُ الَّذِىْ عَلَيْهِنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَلِلرِّجَالِ عَلَيْهِنَّ دَرَجَةٌ  ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(228)\nWAL MOTALLAQAATO YATARABBASNA BE-ANFOSEHINNA SALAASATA QOROOO, WA LAA YAHILLO LAHUNNA AN-Y YAKTUMNA MAA KHALAQAL LAAHO FEE ARHAAMEHINNA IN KUNNA YOAMINNA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHER, WA BO-O’OLATOHUNNA AHAQQO BE-RADDEHINNA FEE ZAALEKA IN ARAADOO ISLAAHAA, WA LAHUNNA MISLUL LAZEE A’LAYHINNA BIL-MA’ROOF, WA LIR-REJAALE A’LAYHINNA DARAJAH, WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nThe divorced women shall await (not wedding anyone else) until three monthly courses; and it shall not be lawful for them to conceal what God hath created in their wombs, if they believe in God and (in) the Last Day (of Judgment): and their husbands shall have the greater right to take them back during the period, if they wish for reconciliation; and for the women shall be similar rights (over men) in fairness, and for men (their rights) on women, is a degree above; and God is Mighty, Wise\nاَلطَّلَاقُ مَرَّتٰنِ فَاِمْسَاكٌ ۢ بِمَعْرُوْفٍ اَوْ تَسْرِيْحٌ ۢ بِاِحْسَانٍ ؕوَلَا يَحِلُّ لَكُمْ اَنْ تَاْخُذُوْا مِمَّآ اٰتَيْتُمُوْهُنَّ شَيْئًا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّخَافَآ اَ لَّا يُقِيْمَا حُدُوْدَ اللّٰهِؕ فَاِنْ خِفْتُمْ اَ لَّا يُقِيْمَا حُدُوْدَ اللّٰهِۙ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَا فِيْمَا افْتَدَتْ بِهٖؕ تِلْكَ حُدُوْدُ اللّٰهِ فَلَا تَعْتَدُوْهَا ۚ وَمَنْ يَّتَعَدَّ حُدُوْدَ اللّٰهِ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(229)\nAT-TALAAQO MARRATAAN, FA-IMSAAKUM BE-MA’ROOFIN AW TASREEHUM BE-EHSAAN, WA LAA YAHILLO LAKUM AN TAAKHOZOO MIMMAA AATAYTOMOOHUNNA SHAY-AN ILLAA AN-Y YAKHAAFAA ALLAA YOQEEMAA HODOODAL LAAH, FA-IN KHIFTUM ALLAA YOQEEMAA HODOODAL LAAHE, FALAA JONAAHA A’LAYHEMAA FEEMAF TADAT BEH, TILKA HODOODUL LAAHE FALAA TA’TADOOHAA, WA MAN-Y YATA-A’DDA HODOODAL LAAHE FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUZ ZAALEMOON.\nDivorce (shall be lawful) only twice then (you should) either keep her in fairness or send her away with kindness; and it shall not be lawful for you to take away anything ye have given them but if both fear that they shall not (be able to) keep (themselves within) the limits (fixed) by God; and if ye fear that they shall not (be. able to) keep (themselves within) the limits (fixed) by God, there shall be no sin on either of them about what she giveth up to get herself freed (from the wedlock); These are the limits ordained by God, (Beware!) exceed them not; and those that exceed the limits ordained by God, then these are they that are unjust\nفَاِنْ طَلَّقَهَا فَلَا تَحِلُّ لَهٗ مِنْۢ بَعْدُ حَتّٰى تَنْكِحَ زَوْجًا غَيْرَهٗ ؕ فَاِنْ طَلَّقَهَا فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَآ اَنْ يَّتَرَاجَعَآ اِنْ ظَنَّآ اَنْ يُّقِيْمَا حُدُوْدَ اللّٰهِؕ وَتِلْكَ حُدُوْدُ اللّٰهِ يُبَيِّنُهَا لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(230)\nFA-IN TALLAQAHAA FALAA TAHILLO LAHU MIM BA’DO HATTAA TANKEHA ZAWJAN GHAYRAH, FA-IN TALLAQAHAA FALAA JONAAHA A’LAYHEMAA AN-Y YATARAAJA-A’A IN ZANNAA AN-Y YOQEEMAA HODOODAL LAAH, WA TILKA HODOODUL LAAHE YOBAYYENOHAA LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nSo if he divorceth her (for a third time) then she shall not be lawful unto him until she wedeth another husband; and if he (also) divorceth her, then there shall be no sin on either of them if they return to each other if they think that they shall (be able to) keep (themselves) within the limits ordained by God; these are the limits ordained by God (which) He maketh them clear for a people who understand\nوَاِذَا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّسَآءَ فَبَلَغْنَ اَجَلَهُنَّ فَاَمْسِكُوْهُنَّ بِمَعْرُوْفٍ اَوْ سَرِّحُوْهُنَّ بِمَعْرُوْفٍ وَلَا تُمْسِكُوْهُنَّ ضِرَارًا لِّتَعْتَدُوْا ۚ وَمَنْ يَّفْعَلْ ذٰ لِكَ فَقَدْ ظَلَمَ نَفْسَهٗ ؕ وَلَا تَتَّخِذُوْٓا اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ هُزُوًا وَّاذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَمَآ اَنْزَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِ وَالْحِكْمَةِ يَعِظُكُمْ بِهٖؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(231)\nWA EZAA TALLAQTOMUN NESAAA-A FA-BALAGHNA AJALAHUNNA FA-AMSEKOOHUNNA BE-MA’ROOFIN AW SARREHOOHUNNA BE-MA’ROOFIN, WA LAA TUMSEKOOHUNNA ZERAARAL LE-TA’TADOO, WA MAN-Y YAF-A’L ZAALEKA FAQAD ZALAMA NAFSAH, WA LAA TATTAKHEZOO AAYAATIL LAAHE HOZOWANW, WAZ KOROO NEA’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA MAA ANZALA A’LAYKUM MENAL KETAABE WAL HIKMATE YA-E’ZOKUM BEH, WAT TAQUL LAAHA WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA BE-KULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nAnd when ye have divorced women and they reach their prescribed period then (either) retain them in fairness or set them free with fairness, and do not retain them to hurt them that ye may transgress, for whosoever shall do this, he indeed is unjust to his (own) self; and take not the signs (commandments) of God a joke and remember the bounty of God upon you and what He hath sent down unto you of the Book and Wisdom, admonish you thereby; and take shelter in God and know ye that God is the Knower of all things\nوَاِذَا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّسَآءَ فَبَلَغْنَ اَجَلَهُنَّ فَلَا تَعْضُلُوْهُنَّ اَنْ يَّنْكِحْنَ اَزْوَاجَهُنَّ اِذَا تَرَاضَوْا بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِؕ ذٰ لِكَ يُوْعَظُ بِهٖ مَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ اَزْكٰى لَكُمْ وَاَطْهَرُؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(232)\nWA EZAA TALLAQTOMUN NESAAA-A FA-BALAGHNA AJALAHUNNA FALAA TA’ZOLOOHUNNA AN-Y YANKEHNA AZWAAJAHUNNA EZAA TARAAZAW BAYNAHUM BIL-MA’ROOF, ZAALEKA YOO-A’ZO BEHI MAN KAANA MINKUM YOAMENO BIL LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHER, ZAALEKUM AZKAA LAKUM WA ATHAR, WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO WA ANTUM LAA TA’LAMOON.\nAnd when ye have divorced (your) women and they have completed their (prescribed) term (of waiting) prevent them not from marrying their husbands when they agree among themselves in fairness; with this is admonished whosoever among you believeth in God and (in) the Last Day (of Judgment); this (way) is more profitable and purer for you; and verily, God knoweth and ye know not\nوَالْوَالِدٰتُ يُرْضِعْنَ اَوْلَادَهُنَّ حَوْلَيْنِ كَامِلَيْنِ لِمَنْ اَرَادَ اَنْ يُّتِمَّ الرَّضَاعَةَ  ؕ وَعَلَى الْمَوْلُوْدِ لَهٗ رِزْقُهُنَّ وَكِسْوَتُهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِؕ لَا تُكَلَّفُ نَفْسٌ اِلَّا وُسْعَهَا ۚ لَا تُضَآرَّ وَالِدَةٌ ۢ بِوَلَدِهَا وَلَا مَوْلُوْدٌ لَّهٗ بِوَلَدِهٖ وَعَلَى الْوَارِثِ مِثْلُ ذٰ لِكَ ۚ فَاِنْ اَرَادَا فِصَالًا عَنْ تَرَاضٍ مِّنْهُمَا وَتَشَاوُرٍ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَا ؕ وَاِنْ اَرَدْتُّمْ اَنْ تَسْتَرْضِعُوْٓا اَوْلَادَكُمْ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ اِذَا سَلَّمْتُمْ مَّآ اٰتَيْتُمْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(233)\nWAL WAALEDAATO YURZE’NA AWLAADAHUNNA HAWLAYNE KAAMELAYNE LEMAN ARAADA AN-Y YOTIMMAR RA-ZAA-A’H, WA A’LAL MAWLOODE LAHU RIZQOHUNNA WA KISWATOHUNNA BIL-MA’ROOF, LAA TOKALLAFO NAFSUN ILLAA WUS-A’HAA, LAA TOZAAAR-RA WAALADADUN BE-WALADEHAA WA LAA MAWLOODUL LAHU BE-WALADEH, WA A’LAL WAARESE MISLO ZAALEK, FA-IN ARAADA FESAALAN A’N TARAAZIM MINHOMAA WA TASHAAWORIN FALAA JONAAHA A’LAYHEMAA, WA IN ARAD-TUM AN TASTARZE-O’O AWLAADAKUM FALAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM EZAA SALLAMTUM MAA AATAYTUM BIL-MA’ROOF, WAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA BEMAA TA’MALOONA BASEER.\nAnd the mothers shall suckle their children two entire years, if the father desires to complete the term of suckling; and on the father shall be their sustenance and their clothing in fairness; burdened not is any soul save to (the extent of) his (individual) ability neither shall a mother be made to suffer (any difficulty or loss) on account of her child nor a father because of his child, and (if the father be not there) on the heir (of the father) devolves a similar responsibility, and if both (the father and the mother) decide on weaning, by mutual consent and (with due) consultation there shall be no blame on them; But if ye decide to engage a wet- nurse for your children there shall be no blame on you provided ye pay what ye promise in fairness and fear God and know ye! that God seeth what (all) ye do\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَذَرُوْنَ اَزْوَاجًا يَّتَرَبَّصْنَ بِاَنْفُسِهِنَّ اَرْبَعَةَ اَشْهُرٍ وَّعَشْرًا ۚ فَاِذَا بَلَغْنَ اَجَلَهُنَّ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيْمَا فَعَلْنَ فِىْٓ اَنْفُسِهِنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(234)\nWAL LAZEENA YOTAWAFFAWNA MINKUM WA YAZAROONA AZWAAJAN-Y YATARABBASNA BE-ANFOSEHINNA ARBA-A’TA ASH-HORINW WA A’SHRAA, FA-EZAA BALAGHNA AJALAHUNNA FALAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM FEEMAA FA-A’LNA FEE ANFOSEHINNA BIL-MA’ROOF, WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOONA KHABEER.\nAnd of you who die leaving (their) wives, these shall wait four months and ten days and when they have completed their (prescribed) term there shall be no blame on you in what they may do with themselves in fairness; And verily, God is (fully) aware of whatever ye do\nوَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيْمَا عَرَّضْتُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ خِطْبَةِ النِّسَآءِ اَوْ اَكْنَنْتُمْ فِىْٓ اَنْفُسِكُمْؕ عَلِمَ اللّٰهُ اَنَّكُمْ سَتَذْكُرُوْنَهُنَّ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا تُوَاعِدُوْهُنَّ سِرًّا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَقُوْلُوْا قَوْلًا مَّعْرُوْفًا ؕ وَلَا تَعْزِمُوْا عُقْدَةَ النِّكَاحِ حَتّٰى يَبْلُغَ الْكِتٰبُ اَجَلَهٗ ؕ وَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِىْٓ اَنْفُسِكُمْ فَاحْذَرُوْهُ ؕ وَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(235)\nWA LAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM FEEMAA A’RRAZTUM BEHI MIN KHITBATIN NESAAA-E AW AKNANTUM FEE ANFOSEKUM, A’LEMAL LAAHO ANNAKUM SATAZKOROONAHUNNA WA LAAKIL LAA TOWAA-E’DOOHUNNA SIRRAN ILLAA AN TAQOOLOO QAWLAM MA’ROOFAA, WA LAA TA’ZEMOO U’QDATAN NEKAAHE HATTAA YABLOGHAL KETAABO AJALAH, WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA FEE ANFOSEKUM FAHZAROOH, WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUN HALEEM.\nBut there shall be no blame on you in indirect proposal of marriage (before the completion of the waiting term) that ye may make to women or keep (the proposal) concealed within yourselves; God knoweth that ye will mention them, but make no promise in secret except ye speak in fairness; and resolve not on a wedlock until the prescribed term is completed; and know ye! that God knoweth whatever is (latent) in yourselves, therefore, be careful of Him; and know ye! that God is Oft-Forgiving and Forbearing\nلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ اِنْ طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّسَآءَ مَا لَمْ تَمَسُّوْهُنَّ اَوْ تَفْرِضُوْا لَهُنَّ فَرِيْضَةً  ۖۚ وَّمَتِّعُوْهُنَّ ۚ عَلَى الْمُوْسِعِ قَدَرُهٗ وَ عَلَى الْمُقْتِرِ قَدَرُهٗ ۚ مَتَاعًا ۢ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِۚ حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(236)\nLAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM IN TALLAQTOMUN NESAAA-A MAA LAM TAMASSOOHUNNA AW TAFREZOO LAHUNNA FAREEZATANW, WA MATTE-O’OHUN, A’LAL MOOSE-E’ QADAROHU WA A’LAL MUQTERE QADAROH, MATAA-A’M BIL-MA’ROOF, HAQQAN A’LAL MOHSENEEN.\nThere is no blame on you if ye divorce women while yet ye have not touched them nor settled any dowry on them; but provide for them, the wealthy according to his means and the poor according to his means, a provision with fairness (this is) (the bounded) duty on doers of good\nوَاِنْ طَلَّقْتُمُوْهُنَّ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ تَمَسُّوْهُنَّ وَقَدْ فَرَضْتُمْ لَهُنَّ فَرِيْضَةً فَنِصْفُ مَا فَرَضْتُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّعْفُوْنَ اَوْ يَعْفُوَا الَّذِىْ بِيَدِهٖ عُقْدَةُ النِّكَاحِ ؕ وَاَنْ تَعْفُوْٓا اَقْرَبُ لِلتَّقْوٰىؕ وَ لَا تَنْسَوُا الْفَضْلَ بَيْنَكُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(237)\nWA IN TALLAQTOMOOHUNNA MIN QABLE AN TAMASSOHUNNA WA QAD FARAZTUM LAHUNNA FAREEZATAN FA-NISFO MAA FARAZTUM ILLAA AN-Y YA’FOONA AW YA’FOWAL LAZEE BE-YADEHI U’QDATUN NEKAAH, WA AN TA’FOO AQRABO LIT-TAQWAA, WA LAA TANSAWUL FAZLA BAYNAKUM, INNAL LAAHA BEMAA TA’MALOONA BASEER.\nAnd if ye divorce them ere ye have touched them and have already settled a dowry on them, then ye shall give them half of what ye have settled unless they (women) remit it or remiteth it he in whose hands is the marriage knot; and that ye yourselves (voluntarily) remit (the whole) is nigher to righteousness; forget not generosity among yourselves; verily, God beholdeth whatever ye do\nحَافِظُوْا عَلَى الصَّلَوٰتِ وَالصَّلٰوةِ الْوُسْطٰى وَقُوْمُوْا لِلّٰهِ قٰنِتِيْنَ‏(238)\nHAAFEZOO A’LAS SALAWAATE WAS SALAATIL WUSTAA, WA QOOMOO LIL-LAAHE QAANETEEN.\nBe strict in observance of prayers; and (in particular) The midmost prayer; and stand ye attent in praying (supplicant) unto God\nفَاِنْ خِفْتُمْ فَرِجَالًا اَوْ رُكْبَانًا  ۚ فَاِذَآ اَمِنْتُمْ فَاذْكُرُوا اللّٰهَ كَمَا عَلَّمَكُمْ مَّا لَمْ تَكُوْنُوْا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(239)\nFA-IN KHIFTUM FA-REJAALAN AW RUKBAANAA, FA-EZAA AMINTUM FAZ-KORUL LAAHA KAMAA A’LLAMAKUM MAA LAM TAKOONOO TA’LAMOON.\nAnd if ye be in fear, (and cannot pray as prescribed) (pray ye) then (as ye may) on foot or riding, but when ye are safe, remember God as He hath taught you (through His Apostle) what ye knew not\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَذَرُوْنَ اَزْوَاجًا  ۖۚ وَّصِيَّةً لِّاَزْوَاجِهِمْ مَّتَاعًا اِلَى الْحَوْلِ غَيْرَ اِخْرَاجٍ ۚ فَاِنْ خَرَجْنَ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِىْ مَا فَعَلْنَ فِىْٓ اَنْفُسِهِنَّ مِنْ مَّعْرُوْفٍؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(240)\nWAL LAZEENA YOTAWAFFAWNA MINKUM WA YAZAROONA AZWAAJANW, WASIYYATAL LE-AZWAAJEHIM MATAA-A’N ELAL HAWLE GHAYRA IKHRAAJ, FA-IN KHARAJNA FALAA JONAAHA A’LAYKUM FEE MAA FA-A’LNA FEE ANFOSEHINNA MIM MA’ROOF, WAL LAAHO A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nAnd those of you who die leaving wives, they shall bequeath for their wives a year’s maintenance without causing them to quit their homes, but if they (the wives) of their own accord quit their homes, there shall be no blame on you in what they may do for themselves in lawful manner; and verily, God is Mighty, Wise\nوَلِلْمُطَلَّقٰتِ مَتَاعٌ ۢ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ ؕ حَقًّا عَلَى الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(241)\nWA LIL-MOTAALLAQAATE MATAA-U’M BIL-MA’ROOF, HAQQAN A’LAL MUTTAQEEN.\nAnd for the divorced women (too) (shall) be a provision in fairness; (this is) a duty on those who guard themselves (against evil)\nكَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(242)\nKAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKUM AAYAATEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TA’QELOON.\nThus, doth God make clear unto you (for your guidance) His signs that ye may understand\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ خَرَجُوْا مِنْ دِيَارِهِمْ وَهُمْ اُلُوْفٌ حَذَرَ الْمَوْتِ فَقَالَ لَهُمُ اللّٰهُ مُوْتُوْا ثُمَّ اَحْيَاھُمْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(243)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA KHARAJOO MIN DEYAAREHIM WA HUM OLOOFUN HAZARAL MAWT, FA-QAALA LAHOMUL LAAHO MOOTOO, SUMMA AHYAAHUM, INNAL LAAHA LA-ZOO FAZLIN A’LAN NAASE WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YASHKOROON.\nDidst thou not see those who went forth from their homes, and they were in thousands, for fear of death; then God said unto them, ‘Die ye!’ (and they died) and thereafter He restored them to life; verily, God is gracious unto them, but most men thank (Him) not\nوَقَاتِلُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَاعْلَمُوْٓا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(244)\nWA QAATELOO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAnd (O’ Muslims!) fight ye in the path of God, and know ye that God is Hearer and Knower (of all things)\nمَنْ ذَا الَّذِىْ يُقْرِضُ اللّٰهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا فَيُضٰعِفَهٗ لَهٗۤ اَضْعَافًا كَثِيْرَةً  ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَقْبِضُ وَيَبْصُۜطُ وَ اِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(245)\nMAN ZAL LAZEE YUQREZUL LAAHA QARZAN HASANAN FA-YOZAA-E’FAHU LAHU AZ-A’AFAN KASEERAH, WAL LAAHO YAQBEZO WA YABSOT, WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nWho is he that will lend unto God a fair loan; verily, He will multiply it unto him manifold; for it is God that holdeth and extendeth and unto Him shall ye be returned\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الْمَلَاِ مِنْۢ بَنِىْٓ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مُوْسٰىۘ اِذْ قَالُوْا لِنَبِىٍّ لَّهُمُ ابْعَثْ لَنَا مَلِكًا نُّقَاتِلْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِؕ قَالَ هَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِتَالُ اَلَّا تُقَاتِلُوْا ؕ قَالُوْا وَمَا لَنَآ اَلَّا نُقَاتِلَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَقَدْ اُخْرِجْنَا مِنْ دِيَارِنَا وَاَبْنَآئِنَا ؕ فَلَمَّا كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقِتَالُ تَوَلَّوْا اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّنْهُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِالظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(246)\nALAM TARA ELAL MALA-E MIM BANEE ISRAAA-EELA MIM BA’DE MOOSAA, IZ QAALOO LE-NABIYYIL LAHOMUB A’S LANAA MALEKAN NOQAATEL FEE SABEELIL LAAH, QAALA HAL A’SAYTUM IN KOTEBA A’LAYKOMUL QETAALO ILLAA TOQAATELOO, QAALOO WA MAA LANAA ALLAA NOQAATELA FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WA QAD UKHRIJNAA MIN DEYAARENAA WA ABNAAA-ENAA, FALAMMAA KOTEBA A’LAYHEMUL QETAALO TAWALLAW ILLAA QALEELAM MINHUM, WAL LAAHO A’LEEMUM BIZ-ZAALEMEEN.\nHast thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) not seen the chiefs of the children of Israel, after Moses, when they spake to a Prophet (who was) unto them (saying) “Raise up for us a king, that we may fight in the path of God”; he said, “May it not be that if fighting were ordained unto you, ye would not fight?” they said, “What aileth us that we should not fight in the path of God, when we have indeed been driven out from our homes and our children?” but when fighting was ordained unto them they turned back save a few of them; and verily, God knoweth the unjust\nوَقَالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَدْ بَعَثَ لَكُمْ طَالُوْتَ مَلِكًا ؕ قَالُوْٓا اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ عَلَيْنَا وَنَحْنُ اَحَقُّ بِالْمُلْكِ مِنْهُ وَلَمْ يُؤْتَ سَعَةً مِّنَ الْمَالِؕ قَالَ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ اصْطَفٰٮهُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَزَادَهٗ بَسْطَةً فِى الْعِلْمِ وَ الْجِسْمِؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُؤْتِىْ مُلْكَهٗ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(247)\nWA QAALA LAHUM NABIYYOHUM INNAL LAAHA QAD BA-A’SA LAKUM TAALOOTA MALEKAA, QAALOO ANNAA YAKOONO LAHUL MULKO A’LAYNAA WA NAHNO AHAQQO BIL-MULKE MINHO WA LAM YOATA SA-A’TAM MENAL MAAL, QAALA INNAL LAAHAS TAFAAHO A’LAYKUM WA ZAADAHU BASTATAN FIL I’LME WAL JISM, WAL LAAHO YOATEE MULKAHU MAN-Y YASHAAA, WAL LAAHO WAASE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAnd their Prophet said unto them “Verily, God hath raised up for you Saul (to be) the king (over you);” They said, “How can the kingdom be his, over us, whereas we are more rightful for it than he while he is not gifted with abundance of wealth;” he said, “Verily, God hath chosen him over you and hath increased him abundantly in knowledge and physique; and verily, God granteth His kingdom unto whomso He pleaseth; God is Omniscient and All-knowing\nوَقَالَ لَهُمْ نَبِيُّهُمْ اِنَّ اٰيَةَ مُلْكِهٖۤ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَكُمُ التَّابُوْتُ فِيْهِ سَكِيْنَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَبَقِيَّةٌ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ اٰلُ مُوْسٰى وَاٰلُ هٰرُوْنَ تَحْمِلُهُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاٰيَةً لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(248)\nWA QAALA LAHUM NABIYYOHUM INNA AAYATA MULKEHI AN-Y YAATEYAKOMUT TAABOOTO FEEHE SAKEENATUM MIR RABBEKUM WA BAQIYYATUM MIMMAA TARAKA AALO MOOSAA WA AALO HAAROONA TAHMELOHUL MALAAA-EKAH, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYATAL LAKUM IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nAnd (then) said their Prophet unto them saying, “Verily, the sign of His kingship shall be that the Ark shall come unto you wherein shall be the tranquillity from your Lord and the Relics of what the family of Moses and the family of Aaron left behind; the angels (of God) shall bear it; verily, therein shall be a sign for you if ye are (indeed) believers\nفَلَمَّا فَصَلَ طَالُوْتُ بِالْجُنُوْدِۙ قَالَ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ مُبْتَلِيْكُمْ بِنَهَرٍۚ فَمَنْ شَرِبَ مِنْهُ فَلَيْسَ مِنِّىْۚ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَطْعَمْهُ فَاِنَّهٗ مِنِّىْٓ اِلَّا مَنِ اغْتَرَفَ غُرْفَةً ۢ بِيَدِهٖۚ فَشَرِبُوْا مِنْهُ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّنْهُمْؕ فَلَمَّا جَاوَزَهٗ هُوَ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ ۙ قَالُوْا لَا طَاقَةَ لَنَا الْيَوْمَ بِجَالُوْتَ وَجُنُوْدِهٖؕ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ يَظُنُّوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ مُّلٰقُوا اللّٰهِۙ كَمْ مِّنْ فِئَةٍ قَلِيْلَةٍ غَلَبَتْ فِئَةً كَثِيْرَةً ۢ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَاللّٰهُ مَعَ الصّٰبِرِيْنَ‏(249)\nFA-LAMMAA FASALA TAALOOTO BIL-JONOODE, QAALA INNAL LAAHA MUBTALEEKUM BE-NAHAR, FAMAN SHAREBA MINHO FA-LAYSA MINNEE, WA MAL LAM YAT-A’MHO FA-INNAHU MINNEE ILLAA MANIGH TARAFA GHURFATAM BE-YADEH, FA-SHAREBOO MINHO ILLAA QALEELAM MINHUM, FA-LAMMAA JAA-WAZAHU HOWA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU, QAALOO LAA TAAQATA LANAL YAWMA BE-JAALOOTA WA JONOODEH, QAALAL LAZEENA YAZUNNOONA ANNAHUM MOLAAQUL LAAHE, KAM MIN FE-ATIN QALEELATIN GHALABAT FE-ATAN KASEERATAM BE-IZNIL LAAH, WAL LAAHO MA-A’S SAABEREEN.\n(And) When Saul set forth with (his) armies, he said, “Verily God will try (your patience) at a stream; whosoever (of you) drinketh from it, then he is not of me and whosoever doth not taste of it then verily he is of me save he who drinketh a draught with the hollow of his hand,” but save a few of them they drank of it; and when he had crossed it, those he and those who believed with him said they, “we have no strength this day against Goliath and his hosts;” but those who thought (rightly) that they shall meet God, spoke saying, “How oft by God’s permission a small army did vanquish a big host; and verily, God is with the patient ones\nوَلَمَّا بَرَزُوْا لِجَالُوْتَ وَجُنُوْدِهٖ قَالُوْا رَبَّنَآ اَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنَا صَبْرًا وَّثَبِّتْ اَقْدَامَنَا وَانْصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَؕ‏(250)\nWA LAMMAA BARAZOO LE-JAALOOTA WA JONOODEHI QAALOO RABBANAA AFRIGH A’LAYNAA SABRANW WA SABBIT AQDAAMANAA WAN SURNAA A’LAL QAWMIL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd when they set forth against Goliath and his hosts, they said, “O’ our Lord! shower on us (Thy blessings of) endurance and set our feet firm and help us against the disbelieving people\nفَهَزَمُوْهُمْ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ ۙ وَقَتَلَ دَاوٗدُ جَالُوْتَ وَاٰتٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ الْمُلْكَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَعَلَّمَهٗ مِمَّا يَشَآءُ ؕ وَلَوْلَا دَفْعُ اللّٰهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُمْ بِبَعْضٍ لَّفَسَدَتِ الْاَرْضُ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ ذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(251)\nFA-HAZAMOOHUM BE-IZNIL LAAHE, WA QATALA DAA-OODO JAALOOTA WA AATAAHUL LAAHUL MULKA WAL HIKMATA WA A’LLAMAHU MIMMAA YASHAAA, WA LAW LAA DAF-U’L LAAHIN NAASA BA’ZAHUM BE-BA’ZIL, LA-FASADATIL ARZO WA LAAKINNAL LAAHA ZOO FAZLIN A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhereupon they routed them by God’s permission and David slew Goliath, and God gave him Kingdom and Wisdom and taught him whatsoever he pleased, and were it not for God’s repelling some men with the others, the earth would have been full of mischief, but God is gracious to all (His) creatures\nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ اللّٰهِ نَتْلُوْهَا عَلَيْكَ بِالْحَقِّؕ وَاِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(252)\nTILKA AAYAATUL LAAHE NATLOOHAA A’LAYKA BIL-HAQ, WA INNAKA LAMENAL MURSALEEN.\nThese are the signs of God with truth do we rehearse them unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!); and verily, thou art (one) of (our) apostles\nتِلْكَ الرُّسُلُ فَضَّلْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍۘ مِنْهُمْ مَّنْ كَلَّمَ اللّٰهُ وَرَفَعَ بَعْضَهُمْ دَرَجٰتٍؕ وَاٰتَيْنَا عِيْسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ الْبَيِّنٰتِ وَاَيَّدْنٰهُ بِرُوْحِ الْقُدُسِؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَا اقْتَتَلَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَتْهُمُ الْبَيِّنٰتُ وَلٰكِنِ اخْتَلَفُوْا فَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اٰمَنَ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ كَفَرَؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَا اقْتَتَلُوْا وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَفْعَلُ مَا يُرِيْدُ‏(253)\nTILKAR ROSOLO FAZZALNAA BA’ZAHUM A’LAA BA’Z, MINHUM MAN KALLAMAL LAAHO WA RA-FA-A’ BA’ZAHUM DARAJAAT, WA AATAYNAA E’ESAB NA MARYAMAL BAYYENAATE WA AYYADNAAHO BE-ROOHIL QODOS, WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAQ TATALAL LAZEENA MIM BA’DEHIM MIM BA’DE MA JAAA-ATHOMUL BAYYENAATO WA LAAKENIKH TALAFOO FA-MINHUM MAN AAMANA WA MINHUM MAN KAFAR, WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAQ TATALOO, WA LAAKINNAL LAAHA YAF-A’LO MAA YOREED.\nThese apostles, We have exalted some of them above the others; of them are some unto whom God hath spoken and some He hath raised in degrees; and we gave Jesus, son of Mary, clear evidence and aided him with the Holy Ghost; and hath God so willed, those who came after them had not have fought among themselves after the clear evidences had come unto them. But they differed; and of them there were some who believed and some who disbelieved; and hath God so willed they would not have fought among themselves: but God doeth whatever He willeth\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَنْفِقُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ يَوْمٌ لَّا بَيْعٌ فِيْهِ وَلَا خُلَّةٌ وَّلَا شَفَاعَةٌ  ؕ وَالْكٰفِرُوْنَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(254)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO ANFEQOO MIMMAA RAZAQNAAKUM MIN QABLE AN-Y YAATEYA YAWMUL LAA BAY-U’N FEEHE WA LAA KHULLATUNW WA LAA SHAFAA-A’H, WAL KAAFEROONA HOMUZ ZAALEMOON.\nO’ ye who believe! Spend (in alms) out of what We have provided you with before the day cometh wherein there shall be no bargaining, nor friendship, nor intercession; and those who disbelieve they are the unjust\nاللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ الْحَىُّ الْقَيُّوْمُۚ  لَا تَاْخُذُهٗ سِنَةٌ وَّلَا نَوْمٌؕ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ مَنْ ذَا الَّذِىْ يَشْفَعُ عِنْدَهٗۤ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِهٖؕ يَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْۚ وَلَا يُحِيْطُوْنَ بِشَىْءٍ مِّنْ عِلْمِهٖۤ اِلَّا بِمَا شَآءَ ۚ وَسِعَ كُرْسِيُّهُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَۚ وَلَا يَئُوْدُهٗ حِفْظُهُمَا ۚ وَ هُوَ الْعَلِىُّ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(255)\nALLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWAL, HAYYUL QAYYOOM, LAA TAA-KHOZOHU SENATUNW WA LAA NAUM, LAHU MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE, MAN ZAL LAZEE YASHFAO’ I’NDAHU ILLAA BE-IZNEH, YA’LAMO MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM, WA LAA YOHEETOONA BE-SHAY-IM MIN I’LMEHI ILLAA BEMAA SHAA-A, WASEA’ KURSIYYOHUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, WA LAA YA-OODOHU HIFZOHOMAA WA HOWAL A’LIYYUL A’ZEEM.\nGod! There is no God but He, the (Ever) Living the self-subsistent. Slumber seizeth Him not nor sleep; His it is whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth; Who is he that can intercede with Him but with His permission; He knoweth what is before them and what is behind them, while they cannot comprehend anything out of His Knowledge save that which He willeth, His Throne extendeth over the heavens and the earth, and the preservation of them both, tireth Him not, And He is the Most High and the Most Great\nلَاۤ اِكْرَاهَ فِى الدِّيْنِۙ  قَد تَّبَيَّنَ الرُّشْدُ مِنَ الْغَىِّۚ فَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِالطَّاغُوْتِ وَيُؤْمِنْۢ بِاللّٰهِ فَقَدِ اسْتَمْسَكَ بِالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقٰى لَا انْفِصَامَ لَهَا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(256)\nLAA IKRAAHA FID DEENE, QAD TABAYYANAR RUSHDO MENAL GHAYY, FAMANY YAKFUR BIT-TAAGHOOTE WA YOA-MIM BILLAAHE FAQADIS TAMSAKA BIL-U’RWATIL WUSQAA, LAN FESAAMA LAHAA, WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEMUN.\nNo compulsion be in religion; Indeed, truth has been made manifest distinct from error; therefore he who disbelieveth the rebels (false deities) and believeth in God, hath indeed laid hold on the strongest handle no break is for it; and verily God is All-Hearing, All-Knowing\nاَللّٰهُ وَلِىُّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يُخْرِجُهُمْ مِّنَ الظُّلُمٰتِ اِلَى النُّوْرِؕ  وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَوْلِيٰٓئُهُمُ الطَّاغُوْتُۙ يُخْرِجُوْنَهُمْ مِّنَ النُّوْرِ اِلَى الظُّلُمٰتِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(257)\nALLAAHO WALIYYUL LAZEENA AAMANOO, YUKHREJOHUM MENAZ ZOLOMAATE ELAN NOOR, WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO AWLE-YAAA-OHOMUT TAAGHOOTO, YUKHREJOONAHUM MENAN NOORE ELAZ ZOLOMAAT, OOLAAA-EKA AS-HAABUN NAAR, HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nGod is the Guardian of those who believe; He taketh them out of darkness into light; and those who disbelieve, the rebels are their guardians they take them out from light into darkness; They are the companions of the (Hell) fire, therein shall they abide\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِىْ حَآجَّ اِبْرٰهٖمَ فِىْ رَبِّهٖۤ اَنْ اٰتٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ الْمُلْكَۘ اِذْ قَالَ اِبْرٰهٖمُ رَبِّىَ الَّذِىْ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُۙ قَالَ اَنَا اُحْىٖ وَاُمِيْتُؕ قَالَ اِبْرٰهٖمُ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَاْتِىْ بِالشَّمْسِ مِنَ الْمَشْرِقِ فَاْتِ بِهَا مِنَ الْمَغْرِبِ فَبُهِتَ الَّذِىْ كَفَرَؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۚ‏(258)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEE HAAAJ-JA IBRAAHEEMA FEE RABBEHI AN AATAAHUL LAAHUL MULK, IZ QAALA IBRAAHEEMO RABBEYAL LAZEE YOHYEE WA YOMEETO, QAALA ANAA OHYEE WA OMEET, QAALA IBRAAHEEMO FA-INNAL LAAHA YAATEE BISH-SHAMSE MENAL MASHREQE FAATE BEHAA MENAL MAGHREBE FA-BOHETAL LAZEE KAFAR, WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nDidst thou not see he who disputed (argued) with Abraham about his Lord, because God hath given him kingdom, when Abraham said unto him (saying) “My Lord is He who giveth life and causeth death,” he said “I (also) give life and cause death;” (then) said Abraham “(well then) Verily, God (My Lord) bringeth the Sun from the East, do thou (then) bring it from the West” whereupon he who disbelieved was confounded; And verily God guideth not unjust people\nاَوْ كَالَّذِىْ مَرَّ عَلٰى قَرْيَةٍ وَّ هِىَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلٰى عُرُوْشِهَا ۚ قَالَ اَنّٰى يُحْىٖ هٰذِهِ اللّٰهُ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا ۚ فَاَمَاتَهُ اللّٰهُ مِائَةَ عَامٍ ثُمَّ بَعَثَهٗ ؕ قَالَ كَمْ لَبِثْتَؕ قَالَ لَبِثْتُ يَوْمًا اَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍؕ قَالَ بَلْ لَّبِثْتَ مِائَةَ عَامٍ فَانْظُرْ اِلٰى طَعَامِكَ وَشَرَابِكَ لَمْ يَتَسَنَّهْۚ وَانْظُرْ اِلٰى حِمَارِكَ وَلِنَجْعَلَكَ اٰيَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَانْظُرْ اِلَى الْعِظَامِ كَيْفَ نُنْشِزُهَا ثُمَّ نَكْسُوْهَا لَحْمًا ؕ فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهٗ ۙ قَالَ اَعْلَمُ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(259)\nAW KALLAZEE MARRA A’LAA QARYATINW WA HEYA KHAAWEYATUN A’LAA O’ROOSHEEHAA, QAALA ANNAA YOHYEE HAAZEHIL LAAHO BA’DA MAWTEHAA, FA-AMAATAHUL LAAHO ME-ATA A’AMIN SUMMA BA-A’SAH, QAALA KAM LABIST, QAALA LABISTO YAWMAN AW BA’ZA YAWM, QAALA BAL LABISTA ME-ATA A’AMIN FAN-ZUR ELAA TA-A’AMEKA WA SHARAABEKA LAM YATASANNAH, WAN ZUR ELAA HEMAAREKA WA LE-NAJ-A’LAKA AAYATAL LIN-NAASE WAN-ZUR ELAL E’ZAAME KAYFA NUNSHE-ZOHAA SUMMA NAKSOOHAA LAHMAA, FALAMMAA TABAYYANA LAHU, QAALA A-A’LAMO ANNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nOr (didst thou not see) like him who passed by a town, and it had fallen on its roofs, he exclaimed, “(Oh!) How can God (ever) bring it to life (again), after (this) its death,” Where-upon God caused him to die a hundred years and thereafter raised him (again) to life; He (God) asked him “How long didst thou tarry (thus)”? said (he) “Perhaps I tarried a day or part of a day;” He said “Nay! Thou hast tarried (thus) a hundred years; But look at thy food and thy drink they indicate not (in the least) passing of any time (upon them) changing (its original state) and look at thy donkey and verily We (will to) make thee a sign (of Our powers) unto mankind and look thou further on the bones how We assemble them together and thereafter (how We) clothe them with flesh”; And when it became clear to him, said he (then) “Now I know that God hath power over all things\nوَاِذْ قَالَ اِبْرٰهٖمُ رَبِّ اَرِنِىْ كَيْفَ تُحْىِ الْمَوْتٰى ؕ قَالَ اَوَلَمْ تُؤْمِنْؕ قَالَ بَلٰى وَلٰكِنْ لِّيَطْمَئِنَّ قَلْبِىْؕ قَالَ فَخُذْ اَرْبَعَةً مِّنَ الطَّيْرِ فَصُرْهُنَّ اِلَيْكَ ثُمَّ اجْعَلْ عَلٰى كُلِّ جَبَلٍ مِّنْهُنَّ جُزْءًا ثُمَّ ادْعُهُنَّ يَاْتِيْنَكَ سَعْيًا ؕ وَاعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(260)\nWA IZ QAALA IBRAAHEEMO RABBE ARENEE KAYFA TOHYIL MAWTAA, QAALA AWA LAM TOAMEN, QAALA BALAA WA LAAKIL LE-YATMA-INNA QALBEE, QAALA FA-KHUZ ARBA-A’TAM MENAT TAYRE FA-SURHUNNA ELAYKA SUMMAJ A’L A’LAA KULLE JABALIM MIN-HUNNA JUZ-AN SUMMAD O’HUNNA YAATEENAKA SA’YAA, WA’ LAM ANNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN HAKEEM.\nAnd (Recollect O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) when said Abraham: “My Lord! Let me see how Thou enliveneth the dead” He said What! Dost thou not (then) believe (in it)”? He said, “Yea but (I ask Thee for) only that my heart resteth convinced”. He said, “Take thou four of the birds and make them to incline unto thee, and (cutting them into parts) place thou on each mountain a part of them and thereafter call them and they will come unto thee rushing” and know (thou) that God is All-Mighty, All-Wise!\nمَثَلُ الَّذِيْنَ يُنْفِقُوْنَ اَمْوَالَهُمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ كَمَثَلِ حَبَّةٍ اَنْۢبَتَتْ سَبْعَ سَنَابِلَ فِىْ كُلِّ سُنْۢبُلَةٍ مِّائَةُ حَبَّةٍؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُضٰعِفُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(261)\nMASALUL LAZEENA YUNFEQOONA AMWAALAHUM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE KAMASALE HABBATIN AMBATAT SAB-A’ SANAABELA FEE KULLE SUMBOLATIM ME-ATO HABBAH, WAL LAAHO YOZAA-E’FO LEMAN-Y YASHAAA, WAL LAAHO WAASE-U’N A’LEEM.\nThe similitude of those who spend their wealth in the path of God is the similitude of a grain of corn that groweth seven ears, in each ear whereof are a hundred grains; And verily God giveth manifold increase to whosoever He willeth, And God is Omniscient, All Knowing\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يُنْفِقُوْنَ اَمْوَالَهُمْ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ لَا يُتْبِعُوْنَ مَاۤ اَنْفَقُوْا مَنًّا وَّلَاۤ اَذًىۙ لَّهُمْ اَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْۚ وَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(262)\nAL-LAZEENA YUNFEQOONA AMWAALAHUM FEE SABEELIL LAAHE SUMMA LAA YUTBE-O’ONA MAA ANFAQOO MANNAW WA LAA AZAL, LAHUM AJROHUM I’NDA RABBEHIM, WA LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM YAHZANOON.\nThose who spend their wealth in the path of God, (and) thereafter follow it not obligation or injury, for them is their reward with their Lord, and neither shall they have (any) fear and nor shall they grieve\nقَوْلٌ مَّعْرُوْفٌ وَّمَغْفِرَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِّنْ صَدَقَةٍ يَّتْبَعُهَاۤ اَذًىؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَنِىٌّ حَلِيْمٌ‏(263)\nQAWLUM MA’ROOFUNW WA MAGHFERATUN KHAYRUM MIN SADAQATIN-Y YATBA-O’HAA AZAA, WAL LAAHO GHANIYYUN HALEEM.\nA kind word and pardon is better than charity that is followed by injury, and verily God is Self-Sufficient, the Most Forbearing\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تُبْطِلُوْا صَدَقٰتِكُمْ بِالْمَنِّ وَالْاَذٰىۙ كَالَّذِىْ يُنْفِقُ مَالَهٗ رِئَآءَ النَّاسِ وَلَا يُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِؕ فَمَثَلُهٗ كَمَثَلِ صَفْوَانٍ عَلَيْهِ تُرَابٌ فَاَصَابَهٗ وَابِلٌ فَتَرَكَهٗ صَلْدًا ؕ لَا يَقْدِرُوْنَ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ مِّمَّا كَسَبُوْا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(264)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TUBTELOO SADAQAATEKUM BIL-MANNE WAL AZAA, KAL-LAZEE YUNFEQO MAA LAHU RE-AAA-AN NAASE WA LAA YOAMENO BIL LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHER, FAMASALOHU KAMASALE SAFWAANIN A’LAYHE TORAABUN FA-ASAABAHU WAABELUN FATARAKAHU SALDAA, LAA YAQDEROONA A’LAA SHAY-IM MIMMAA KASABOO, WAL LAAHO LAA YAHDIL QAWMAL KAAFEREEN.\nO’ ye who believe! Render not your charities worthless by obligation and injury (laid on them) like one who spendeth his wealth to be seen of men and believeth not in God and the Last Day (of Judgment); His similitude is as the likeness of a smooth hard rock, on it is (a little) dust, a heavy rain falleth upon it and leaveth it just a bare stone; They shall not gain anything of what they have earned (in this world) and verily God guideth not the disbelieving people\nوَمَثَلُ الَّذِيْنَ يُنْفِقُوْنَ اَمْوَالَهُمُ ابْتِغَآءَ مَرْضَاتِ اللّٰهِ وَ تَثْبِيْتًا مِّنْ اَنْفُسِهِمْ كَمَثَلِ جَنَّةٍۢ بِرَبْوَةٍ اَصَابَهَا وَابِلٌ فَاٰتَتْ اُكُلَهَا ضِعْفَيْنِۚ فَاِنْ لَّمْ يُصِبْهَا وَابِلٌ فَطَلٌّؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(265)\nWA MASALUL LAZEENA YUNFEQOONA AMWAALAHOMUB TEGHAAA-A MARZAATIL LAAHE WA TASBEETAM MIN ANFOSEHIM KA-MASALE JANNATIM BE-RABWATIN ASAABAHAA WAABELUN FA-AATAT OKOLAHAA ZEA’FAYN, FA-IL LAM  YOSIBHAA WAABELUN FATAL, WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOONA BASEER.\nThe similitude of those who spend their wealth seeking God’s pleasure and or asserting of thesmelves in devotion, is as the similitude of a garden on an elevation; heavy rain falleth upon it and it yieldeth its fruit two-fold, and if heavy rain falleth not upon it, then a gentle shower (itself suffices it); And verily God be- holdeth all that ye do\nاَيَوَدُّ اَحَدُكُمْ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ لَهٗ جَنَّةٌ مِّنْ نَّخِيْلٍ وَّاَعْنَابٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُۙ لَهٗ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِۙ وَاَصَابَهُ الْكِبَرُ وَلَهٗ ذُرِّيَّةٌ ضُعَفَآءُۖۚ فَاَصَابَهَاۤ اِعْصَارٌ فِيْهِ نَارٌ فَاحْتَرَقَتْؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمُ الْاٰيٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(266)\nA-YAWADDO AHADOKUM AN TAKOONA LAHU JANNATUM MIN NAKHEELINW WA A-A’NAABIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO, LAHU FEEHAA MIN KULLIS SAMARAATE, WA ASAABAHUL KEBARO WA LAHU ZURRIYYATUN ZO-A’FAAA, FA-ASAABAHAA E-A’SAARUN FEEHE NAARUN FAH-TARAQAT, KAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKOMUL AAYAATE LA-A’LLAKUM TATAFAKKAROON.\n(What!) would any one of you like that there should be for him a garden of palms, vines, (with) streams flowing from underneath it for him all kinds of fruit therein, he is stricken with old age, and for him there be issues (young and) weak, striketh it a whirlwind with fire therein and it gets burnt up? Thus doth God make clear to you His signs; that ye may reflect\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَنْفِقُوْا مِنْ طَيِّبٰتِ مَا كَسَبْتُمْ وَمِمَّاۤ اَخْرَجْنَا لَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ وَلَا تَيَمَّمُوا الْخَبِيْثَ مِنْهُ تُنْفِقُوْنَ وَلَسْتُمْ بِاٰخِذِيْهِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تُغْمِضُوْا فِيْهِؕ وَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ غَنِىٌّ حَمِيْدٌ‏(267)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO ANFEQOO MIN TAYYEBAATE MAA KASABTUM WA MIMMAA AKH-RAJNAA LAKUM MENAL ARZ, WA LAA TAYAMMAMUL KHABEESA MINHO TUNFEQOONA WA LASTUM BE-AAKHEZEEHE ILLAA AN TUGHMEZOO FEEH, WA’ LAMOO ANNAL LAAHA GHANIYYUN HAMEED.\nO’ ye who believe! Give in charity out of (only) the good things which ye have earned and of that which we have produced for you from the earth and (even) aim not at the bad things to spend thereof (in charity); while ye yourselves would not accept it except that ye connive at it; and know ye, God is Self-Sufficient, Praiseworthy\nاَلشَّيْطٰنُ يَعِدُكُمُ الْفَقْرَ وَيَاْمُرُكُمْ بِالْفَحْشَآءِ ۚ وَاللّٰهُ يَعِدُكُمْ مَّغْفِرَةً مِّنْهُ وَفَضْلًا ؕ وَاللّٰهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيْمٌۚ  ۙۖ‏(268)\nASH-SHAYTAANO YA-E’DOKOMUL FAQRA WA YAAMOROKUM BIL-FAHSHAAA, WAL LAAHO YA-E’DOKUM MAGHFERATAM MINHO WA FAZLAA, WAL LAAHO WAASE-U’N A’LEEM.\nThe Satan threatened! you with poverty and enjoineth on you sordidness, whereas God promiseth you pardon from Him and grace; And verily God is Omniscient, All-Knowing\nيُؤْتِى الْحِكْمَةَ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ۚ وَمَنْ يُّؤْتَ الْحِكْمَةَ فَقَدْ اُوْتِىَ خَيْرًا كَثِيْرًا ؕ وَمَا يَذَّكَّرُ اِلَّاۤ اُولُوا الْاَلْبَابِ‏(269)\nYOATIL HIKMATA MAN-Y YASHAAA, WA MAN-Y YOATAL HIKMATA FAQAD OOTEYA KHAYRAN KASEERAA, WA MAA YAZZAKKARO ILLAA OOLUL ALBAAB.\nHe granteth wisdom to whomsoever He willeth, and he who hath been granted wisdom hath been given abundant good; and none shall mind it save those endowed with wisdom\nوَمَاۤ اَنْفَقْتُمْ مِّنْ نَّفَقَةٍ اَوْ نَذَرْتُمْ مِّنْ نَّذْرٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُهٗ ؕ وَمَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ اَنْصَارٍ‏(270)\nWA MAA ANFAQTUM MIN NAFAQATIN AW NAZARTUM MIN NAZRIN FA-INNAL LAAHA YA’LAMOH, WA MAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN ANSAAR.\nAnd whatever alms ye give or whatever vow ye make, Verily God knoweth it; but for the unjust there shall be no helpers\nاِنْ تُبْدُوا الصَّدَقٰتِ فَنِعِمَّا هِىَۚ وَاِنْ تُخْفُوْهَا وَ تُؤْتُوْهَا الْفُقَرَآءَ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْؕ وَيُكَفِّرُ عَنْكُمْ مِّنْ سَيِّاٰتِكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(271)\nIN TUBDUS SADAQAATE FA-NE-I’MMAA HEE,  WA IN TUKHFOOHAA WA TOATOOHAL FOQARAAA-A FA-HOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM, WA YOKAFFERO A’NKUM MIN SAYYEAATEKUM, WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOONA KHABEER.\nAnd if ye give alms openly (even so) it is well, and if ye hide it and give it to the poor, it will be better still for yourselves; and (it) will remove from you some of your sins, and verily God is aware of all that ye do\nلَيْسَ عَلَيْكَ هُدٰٮهُمْ وَلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَلِاَنْفُسِكُمْؕ وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْنَ اِلَّا ابْتِغَآءَ وَجْهِ اللّٰهِؕ وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ يُّوَفَّ اِلَيْكُمْ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(272)\nLAYSA A’LAYKA HODAAHUM WA LAAKINNAL LAAHA YAHDEE MAN-Y YASHAAA, WA MAA TUNFEQOO MIN KHAYRIN FA-LE-ANFOSEKUM, WA MAA TUNFEQOONA ILLAB TEGHAAA-A WAJHIL LAAH, WA MAA TUNFEQOO MIN KHAYRIN-Y YOWAFFA ELAYKUM WA ANTUM LAA TUZLAMOON.\nNot on thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) is incumbent their guidance, but (nay!) God guideth aright whomsoever He willeth; and whatever good thing ye spend (in charity) shall be for your own selves; and ye give not except seeking the pleasure of God; and whatever ye shall spend of good, shall be rendered back to you (in full) and ye shall not be wronged\nلِلْفُقَرَآءِ الَّذِيْنَ اُحْصِرُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ لَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ ضَرْبًا فِى الْاَرْضِ يَحْسَبُهُمُ الْجَاهِلُ اَغْنِيَآءَ مِنَ التَّعَفُّفِۚ تَعْرِفُهُمْ بِسِيْمٰهُمْۚ لَا يَسْئَلُوْنَ النَّاسَ اِلْحَافًا ؕ وَمَا تُنْفِقُوْا مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِهٖ عَلِيْمٌ‏(273)\nLIL-FOQARAAA-IL LAZEENA OHSEROO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA ZARBAN FIL ARZ, YAHSABOHOMUL JAAHELO AGHNEYAAA-A MENAT TA-A’FFOF, TA’REFOHUM BE-SEEMAAHUM, LAA YAS-ALOONAN NAASA ILHAAFAA, WA MAA TUNFEQOO MIN KHAYRIN FA-INNAL LAAHA BEHI A’LEEM.\n(Charity is) for those poor that are besieged in the path of God and thereby prevented from moving about in the land the ignorant thinketh them to be rich for their Self-Control (from begging) thou wouldst recognise them by their Countenance, they beg not of men importunately; and whatever of good things ye give in charity, verily God fully knoweth of it\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يُنْفِقُوْنَ اَمْوَالَهُمْ بِالَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ سِرًّا وَّعَلَانِيَةً فَلَهُمْ اَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْۚ وَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَؔ‏(274)\nAL-LAZEENA YUNFEQOONA AMWAALAHUM BIL-LAYLE WAN NAHAARE SIRRANW WA A’LAANEYATAN FA-LAHUM AJROHUM I’NDA RABBEHIM, WA LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM YAHZANOON.\nThose who spend their wealth by night and (by) day, secretly and openly, for them shall be their reward with their Lord, fear shall not be on them nor shall they grieve\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَاْكُلُوْنَ الرِّبٰوا لَا يَقُوْمُوْنَ اِلَّا كَمَا يَقُوْمُ الَّذِىْ يَتَخَبَّطُهُ الشَّيْطٰنُ مِنَ الْمَسِّؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَا الْبَيْعُ مِثْلُ الرِّبٰوا ۘ وَاَحَلَّ اللّٰهُ الْبَيْعَ وَحَرَّمَ الرِّبٰوا ؕ فَمَنْ جَآءَهٗ مَوْعِظَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ فَانْتَهٰى فَلَهٗ مَا سَلَفَؕ وَاَمْرُهٗۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِؕ وَمَنْ عَادَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(275)\nAL-LAZEENA YAAKOLOONAR REBAA LAA YAQOOMOONA ILLAA KAMAA YAQOOMUL LAZEE YATAKHABBATOHUSH SHAYTAANO MENAL MAS, ZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM QAALOO INNAMAL BAY-O’ MISLUR REBAA, WA AHALLAL LAAHUL BAY-A’ WA HARRAMAR REBAA, FAMAN JAAA-AHU MAW-E’ZATUM MIR RABBEHI FAN-TAHAA FA-LAHU MAA SALAF, WA AMROHU ELAL LAAH, WA MAN A’ADA FA-OOLAAAEKA ASHAABUN NAAR, HUM FEEHAA KHALEDOON.\nThose who swallow interest will not (be able to) stand (in resurrection) except as standeth one whom Satan hath confounded with his touch; this because they say, trade is only like (earning) interest, whereas God hath decreed trade lawful and hath forbidden interest, wherefore whosoever (after) the admonition hath come unto him from his Lord desists, shall have what hath gone before; and his affair rests with God, and whoever returneth (to it even after the admonition); They are the inmates of the (Hell) fire, therein shall they abide\nيَمْحَقُ اللّٰهُ الرِّبٰوا وَيُرْبِى الصَّدَقٰتِؕ وَاللّٰهُ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ كَفَّارٍ اَثِيْمٍ‏(276)\nYAMHAQUL LAAHUR REBAA WA YURBIS SADAQAAT, WAL LAAHO LAA YOHIBBO KULLA KAFFAARIN ASEEM.\nGod blotteth out (the gains of) interest and causeth charities to grow; God loveth not any ingrate sinner\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ لَهُمْ اَجْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْۚ وَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(277)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA AQAAMUS SALAATE WA AATAWUZ ZAKAATE LAHUM AJROHUM I’NDA RABBEHIM, WA LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM YAHZANOON.\nVerily those who believe, and act righteously and establish prayer and disburse away the (Prescribed) poor-rate, they shall have their reward with their Lord, neither shall they have (any) fear nor shall they grieve\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَذَرُوْا مَا بَقِىَ مِنَ الرِّبٰٓوا اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(278)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANUT TAQUL LAAHA WA ZAROO MAA BAQEYA MENAR REBAA IN KUNTUM MOAMENOON.\nO’ Ye who believe! take shelter in God and forego what remaineth (due to you) of the interest if ye are (indeed) believers\nفَاِنْ لَّمْ تَفْعَلُوْا فَاْذَنُوْا بِحَرْبٍ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖۚ وَاِنْ تُبْتُمْ فَلَكُمْ رُءُوْسُ اَمْوَالِكُمْۚ لَا تَظْلِمُوْنَ وَلَا تُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(279)\nFA-IL LAM TAF-A’LOO FAAZANOO BE-HARBIM MENAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEH, WA IN TUBTUM FA-LAKUM RO-OOSO ANWAALEKUM, LAA TAZLEMOONA WA LAA TUZLAMOON.\nAnd if ye do it not, then be ye apprised of war from God and His Apostle, and if ye repent (and give up interest) then shall ye have your capital; Deal ye not unjustly (with others) and nor ye be dealt with unjustly\nوَاِنْ كَانَ ذُوْ عُسْرَةٍ فَنَظِرَةٌ اِلٰى مَيْسَرَةٍ ؕ وَاَنْ تَصَدَّقُوْا خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(280)\nWA IN KAANA ZOO U’SRATIN FA-NAZERATUN ELAA MAYSARAH, WA AN TASADDAQOO KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nAnd if (any debtor) be in straitened circumstances, then let there be respite until (he is in) ease; and that if ye forego it (even the capital) (as charity) it is better for you if ye only knew\nوَاتَّقُوْا يَوْمًا تُرْجَعُوْنَ فِيْهِ اِلَى اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ تُوَفّٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(281)\nWAT TAQOO YAWMAN TURJAO’ONA FEEHE ELAL LAAH, SUMMA TOWAFFAA KULLO NAFSIM MAA KASABAT WA HUM LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAnd Fear ye the Day wherein ye shall return unto God; each one shall be measured back (in full) what he earned and they shall not be wronged\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا تَدَايَنْتُمْ بِدَيْنٍ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى فَاكْتُبُوْهُ ؕ وَلْيَكْتُب بَّيْنَكُمْ كَاتِبٌۢ بِالْعَدْلِ وَلَا يَاْبَ كَاتِبٌ اَنْ يَّكْتُبَ كَمَا عَلَّمَهُ اللّٰهُ فَلْيَكْتُبْ ۚوَلْيُمْلِلِ الَّذِىْ عَلَيْهِ الْحَقُّ وَلْيَتَّقِ اللّٰهَ رَبَّهٗ وَلَا يَبْخَسْ مِنْهُ شَيْئًا ؕ فَاِنْ كَانَ الَّذِىْ عَلَيْهِ الْحَقُّ سَفِيْهًا اَوْ ضَعِيْفًا اَوْ لَا يَسْتَطِيْعُ اَنْ يُّمِلَّ هُوَ فَلْيُمْلِلْ وَلِيُّهٗ بِالْعَدْلِؕ وَاسْتَشْهِدُوْا شَهِيْدَيْنِ مِنْ رِّجَالِكُمْۚ فَاِنْ لَّمْ يَكُوْنَا رَجُلَيْنِ فَرَجُلٌ وَّامْرَاَتٰنِ مِمَّنْ تَرْضَوْنَ مِنَ الشُّهَدَآءِ اَنْ تَضِلَّ اِحْدٰٮهُمَا فَتُذَكِّرَ اِحْدٰٮهُمَا الْاُخْرٰىؕ وَ لَا يَاْبَ الشُّهَدَآءُ اِذَا مَا دُعُوْا ؕ وَلَا تَسْئَمُوْۤا اَنْ تَكْتُبُوْهُ صَغِيْرًا اَوْ كَبِيْرًا اِلٰٓى اَجَلِهٖؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ اَقْسَطُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَاَقْوَمُ لِلشَّهَادَةِ وَاَدْنٰۤى اَلَّا تَرْتَابُوْٓا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ تِجَارَةً حَاضِرَةً تُدِيْرُوْنَهَا بَيْنَكُمْ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ اَلَّا تَكْتُبُوْهَا ؕ وَاَشْهِدُوْۤا اِذَا تَبَايَعْتُمْ وَلَا يُضَآرَّ كَاتِبٌ وَّلَا شَهِيْدٌ  ؕ وَاِنْ تَفْعَلُوْا فَاِنَّهٗ فُسُوْقٌ ۢ بِكُمْ ؕ وَ اتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(282)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA TADAAYANTUM BE-DAYNIN ELAA AJALIM MOSAMMAA FAKTOBOOH, WAL-YAKTUB BAYNAKUM KAATEBUM BIL-A’DL, WA LAA YAABA KAATEBUN AN-Y YAKTOBA KAMAA A’LLAMAHUL LAAHO FAL-YAKTUB, WAL YUMLELIL LAZEE A’LAYHIL HAQQO WAL YATTAQIL LAAHA RABBAHU WA LAA YABKHAS MINHO SHAY-AA, FA-IN KAANAL LAZEE A’LAYHIL HAQQO SAFEEHAN AW ZA-E’EFAN AW LAA YASTA-TEE-O’ AN-Y YOMILLA HOWA FAL-YUMLIL WALIYYOHU BIL-A’DL, WAS TASH-HEDOO SHAHEEDAYNE MIR REJAALEKUM, FA-IL LAM TARZAWNA MENASH SHOHA-DAAA-E AN TAZILLA EHDAAHOMAA FA-TOZAKKERA EHDAAHOMAL UKHRAA, WA LAA YAABASH SHOHADAAA0O EZAA MAA DO-O’O, WA LAA TAS-AMOO AN TAKTOBOOHO SAGHEERAN AW KABEERAN ELAA AJALEH, ZAALEKUM AQSATO I’NDAL LAAHE WA AQWAMO LISH-SHAHAADATE WA ADNAA ALLAA TARTAABOO ILLAA AN TAKOONA TEJAARATAN HAAZERATAN TODEEROONAHAA BAYNAKUM FA-LAYSA A’LAYKUM JONAAHUN ILLAA TAKTOBOOHAA, WA ASH-HEDOO EZAA TABAA-YA’TUM, WA LAA YOZAAAR-RA KAATEBUNW WA LAA SHAHEED, WA IN TAF-A’LOO FA-INNAHU FOSOOQUM BEKUM, WAT TAQUL LAAH, WA YO-A’LLEMOKOMUL LAAH, WAL LAAHO BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nO’ ye who believe: when ye contract each other, a loan for a fixed term, then write it down; and let a scribe write it down justly between you, and the scribe should not refuse to write (record it down) as God hath taught him so let him write and let him who oweth dictate, and he should take shelter in God his Lord and diminish not aught thereof; but if he who oweth be witless or infirm, or if he be not able to dictate himself then let his guardian dictate justly, then call to witness two witnesses from among your men and if there not be two men, then (take) a man and two women, of those ye approve of the witnesses, so that should one of the two (women) forget the (second) one of the two may remind the other; the witnesses should not refuse when summoned (to evidence); disdain not ye of writing it down, be the transaction small or big, with its fixed term, (of its falling due): this procedure is the most equitable with God and the most confirmatory for evidence and nearest (to confirmation) that ye may not fall in (any kind of) doubt (thereafter) except (when) it be a ready (hand to hand) transaction of trade in which ye give and take among yourselves or then there be no blame on you if ye write it not; and have witnesses when (in this way) ye transact together and no scribe or witness should cause or suffer harm and if ye do (so), verily then it will be transgression of you; and take shelter in God, and God teacheth you; and God knoweth all things\nوَاِنْ كُنْتُمْ عَلٰى سَفَرٍ وَّلَمْ تَجِدُوْا كَاتِبًا فَرِهٰنٌ مَّقْبُوْضَةٌ  ؕ فَاِنْ اَمِنَ بَعْضُكُمْ بَعْضًا فَلْيُؤَدِّ الَّذِى اؤْتُمِنَ اَمَانَتَهٗ وَلْيَتَّقِ اللّٰهَ رَبَّهٗؕ وَلَا تَكْتُمُوا الشَّهَادَةَ  ؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْتُمْهَا فَاِنَّهٗۤ اٰثِمٌ قَلْبُهٗؕ وَ اللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ عَلِيْمٌ‏(283)\nWA IN KUNTUM A’LAA SAFARINW WA LAM TAJEDOO KAATEBAN FAREHAANUM MAQBOOZAH, FA-IN AMENA BA’ZOKUM BA’ZAN FAL-YO-ADDIL LAZEA TOMENA AMAANATAHU WAL YATTAQIL LAAHA RABBAH, WA LAA TAKTOMUSH SHAHAADAH, WA MAN-Y YAKTUMHAA  FA-INNAHU AASEMUN QALBOH, WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOONA A’LEEM.\nAnd if ye be on a journey and ye find not a scribe then take a pledge with possession; but if one of you trusteth the other, let the one trusted fulfil his trust, and take shelter in God his Lord; and conceal not evidence; And whosoever concealeth it, then surely his heart is sinful; And Verily God knoweth all that ye do\nلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَاِنْ تُبْدُوْا مَا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِكُمْ اَوْ تُخْفُوْهُ يُحَاسِبْكُمْ بِهِ اللّٰهُؕ فَيَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(284)\nLIL-LAAHE MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ, WA IN TUBDOO MAA FEE ANFOSEKUM AW TUKHFOOHO YOHAASIBKUM BEHIL LAAH, FA-YAGHFERO LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YO-A’ZZEBO MAN-Y YASAAA, WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nGod’s is whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth; and whether ye manifest what is in your selves or conceal it, God will call you to account for it; and then will He forgive whomsoever He willeth and will punish whomsoever He willeth and Verily God is powerful over all things\nاٰمَنَ الرَّسُوْلُ بِمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ رَّبِّهٖ وَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَؕ كُلٌّ اٰمَنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَمَلٰٓئِكَتِهٖ وَكُتُبِهٖ وَرُسُلِهٖ لَا نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ اَحَدٍ مِّنْ رُّسُلِهٖ وَقَالُوْا سَمِعْنَا وَاَطَعْنَا غُفْرَانَكَ رَبَّنَا وَاِلَيْكَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(285)\nAAMANAR RASOOLO BEMAA UNZELA MIR RABBEHI WAL MOA-MENOONA, KULLUN AAMANA BILLAAHE WA MALAA-EKATEHI WA KOTOBEHI WA ROSOLEHI, LAA NOFARREQO BAYNA AHADIM MIR ROSOLEH, WA QAALU SAME’NAA WA ATA’NAA, GHUFRAANAKA RABBANAA WA ELAYKAL MASEER.\nThe Prophet believeth in what hath come down unto him from his Lord, and (so do) the believers; all believe in God, and in His Angels and in His Books and in His apostles; (they say) “We make no difference between His apostles;” and they say, “We have heard and obeyed (and we implore ) Thy forgiveness, O’ Our Lord! and unto Thee is our march\nلَا يُكَلِّفُ اللّٰهُ نَفْسًا اِلَّا وُسْعَهَا ؕ لَهَا مَا كَسَبَتْ وَعَلَيْهَا مَا اكْتَسَبَتْؕ رَبَّنَا لَا تُؤَاخِذْنَاۤ اِنْ نَّسِيْنَاۤ اَوْ اَخْطَاْنَا ۚ رَبَّنَا وَلَا تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْنَاۤ اِصْرًا كَمَا حَمَلْتَهٗ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِنَا ۚرَبَّنَا وَلَا تُحَمِّلْنَا مَا لَا طَاقَةَ لَنَا بِهٖ ۚ وَاعْفُ عَنَّا وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا اَنْتَ مَوْلٰٮنَا فَانْصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(286)\nLAA YOKALLEFUL LAAHO NAFSAN ILLAA WUS-A’HAA, LAHAA MAA KASABAT WA A’LAYHAA MAKTASABAT, RABBANAA LAA TOAA-KHIZNAA IN NASEENAA AW AKHTAA-NAA, RABBANAA WA LAA TAHMIL A’LAYNAA ISRAN KAMAA HAMALTAHU A’LAL LAZEENA MIN QABLENAA, RABBANAA WA LAA TOHAMMIL NAA MAA LAA TAAQATA LANAA BEHI, WA’FO A’NNAA, WAGH FIRLANAA, WAR HAMNAA, ANTA MAWLAANAA FAN-SURNAA A’LAL QAWMIL KAAFEREEN.\nImposeth not God, any soul but to its (individual) ability; for it shall be (the good) what he hath acquired and against it (shall be) (the evil) he hath wrought; O’ Our Lord! hold us not responsible if we forget or make a mistake; O’ Our Lord! lay not on us a burden as thou didst lay on those before us and lay not on us that which we have not the strength (to bear): pardon us; and forgive us, and have mercy on us; Thou art our Lord, so help us then against the unbeliever people!"
}
